00:16:22 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I need to build "SIGNAL" — an Awwwards-level interactive engineering portfolio for Anurag Koushik, an electrical engineer. The README spec is extremely detailed. I need you to give me step-by-step detailed instructions for implementing this.\n\nHere\'s the core spec:\n\n**Tech Stack:**\n- Next.js + React + TypeScript\n- Tailwind CSS for layout + custom CSS for motion/visuals\n- GSAP + ScrollTrigger for motion\n- Lenis for smooth scrolling\n- Three.js + React Three Fiber + Drei for WebGL\n- MDX for case studies\n- Deploy on Vercel\n\n**Design:**\n- Warm technical editorial: bg #F1F0EB, text #111111, accent signal green #5BFF87\n- Typography: one expressive grotesk/display family + one technical mono family\n- 12-column grid desktop, 8 tablet, 4 mobile\n- Large editorial typography (9-15vw display)\n\n**Key Features:**\n1. Hero WebGL field (particle system that reacts to pointer/scroll)\n2. Custom cursor with magnetic interactions\n3. Cinematic scroll-based page transitions\n4. 3 flagship project case studies (embedded, FPGA, power electronics)\n5. Capabilities section as connected system diagram\n6. Velocity typography, image distortion shaders\n7. Reduced motion support\n8. Mobile-first responsive with different interaction choreography\n\n**Page Structure:**\n- Homepage with scenes: System Entry → Identity → Positioning → Selected Work → Capabilities → About → Contact\n- Project pages with narrative template\n- About page\n- Contact page\n\nPlease provide extremely detailed step-by-step instructions for building this from scratch. Break it down into phases:\n\n**Phase 0:** Project setup (npx create-next-app, install dependencies, folder structure)\n**Phase 1:** Design tokens, typography, globals.css, grid system\n**Phase 2:** Static layout - Header, Footer, PageShell, Homepage scenes, project pages\n**Phase 3:** Motion - Lenis smooth scroll, GSAP animations, ScrollTrigger, text reveals, custom cursor, magnetic interactions\n**Phase 4:** WebGL hero field with Three.js/R3F, shader particles, pointer interaction\n**Phase 5:** Project page transitions, FLIP animations, project interactions\n**Phase 6:** Mobile pass, performance optimization, accessibility\n\nFor each phase, give me:\n1. Exact files to create\n2. What each file should contain (code snippets)\n3. The order to implement them in\n4. Any gotchas or important considerations\n\nBe very specific with code. I want production-quality implementation, not placeholders.', 'timeout': 600000}
