es a cohesive technical documentation feel. The risk is being too utilitarian and lacking the Awwwards/editorial character.\n\nRecommended direction:\n- B (Editorial — Bricolage Grotesque + IBM Plex Mono)\n- reason: SIGNAL\'s thesis is "precision of engineering × experimentation of creative development." Direction B best captures the creative experimentation side while maintaining enough clarity for technical content. It avoids the generic developer-template trap that Direction A risks, and brings more editorial character than Direction C\'s utilitarian approach.\n\nRunner-up:\n- C (Industrial — Archivo + IBM Plex Mono)\n- reason: Strongest engineering credibility. If the final design direction needs to lean more technical/editorial-balance, this is the safer fallback.\n\nScope check:\n- homepage untouched: YES\n- package.json unchanged: YES\n- package-lock.json unchanged: YES\n- motion introduced: NO\n- WebGL introduced: NO\n\nStep 2 commit:\n- hash: 4f62cca\n- message: feat: add typography exploration lab\n\nProblems encountered:\n- None. Build, lint, TypeScript, and route tests all passed cleanly.\n\nREADME/spec discrepancies:\n- None.\n\nReady for Step 3:\nWAITING FOR TYPOGRAPHY DECISION before proceeding to Step 3.\n\nPlease confirm which typography direction (A, B, or C) should be adopted for the production site, or if you want to discuss further.', 'timeout': 300000}
