15:54:24 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I need to report progress on Step 7 (Responsive Layout Pass). Here is what was done:\n\n## What was done\nImplemented comprehensive mobile responsive breakpoints (@media max-width: 47.99rem) across all 14 CSS module files in the portfolio, plus updated the responsive QA checklist.\n\n## Why it was done\nStep 7 from the ChatGPT instruction sequence requires a full responsive layout pass to ensure the portfolio renders correctly on mobile (320px-479px), tablet (480px-1023px), and desktop (1024px+) viewports. The previous steps established the design system (typography, colors, grid, components) but all layouts were desktop-first with no mobile fallbacks.\n\n## How it was done\nAdded `@media (max-width: 47.99rem)` blocks to each CSS module:\n\n1. **Header.module.css** — 4 nav items visible without hamburger, 2.75rem min touch height\n2. **Hero.module.css** — Title scales from 3.6rem to 7rem, KOUSHIK flush-left on mobile\n3. **IntroStatement.module.css** — clamp() padding, 9ch statement max-width\n4. **SelectedWork.module.css** — Responsive headings, stacked project cards\n5. **ProjectVisual.module.css** — min-height reduced to clamp(18rem, 55vw, 44rem)\n6. **Capabilities.module.css** — 6 nodes stack in single column, heading-sm labels\n7. **AboutPreview.module.css** — display-md heading, stacked system nodes\n8. **ContactCTA.module.css** — Heading scales to clamp(3rem, 12vw, 5rem), stacked channels/footer\n9. **ProjectHero.module.css** — Title clamp(3rem, 14vw, 5rem), stacked meta info\n10. **ProjectSection.module.css** — Scaled title, reduced pending state margins\n11. **ProjectCaseStudy.module.css** — Full-width copy, stacked readout labels\n12. **ProjectArchitecture.module.css** — Nodes stack vertically, connections vertical on mobile\n13. **ProjectMetrics.module.css** — Metric values scale to heading-lg, reduced height\n14. **NextProject.module.css** — Title clamp(2.5rem, 12vw, 4rem), arrow clamp(2rem, 8vw, 4rem)\n\nAlso updated `docs/responsive-qa.md` with a complete viewport checklist for all components.\n\n## Output\n- Build: PASS (next build — all 9 routes generate successfully)\n- Lint: PASS (eslint — no errors)\n- TypeScript: PASS (tsc --noEmit — no errors)\n- Dev server: All routes return correct HTTP status codes (200 for valid, 404 for invalid slugs)\n- Git: Committed as `0facd89` — "Step 7: Responsive layout pass"\n\n## Problems encountered\n- One edit to ProjectCaseStudy.module.css failed multiple times due to exact string mismatch (likely whitespace/encoding difference from a prior edit). Fixed by rewriting the entire file.\n- No CSS parsing errors or hydration warnings in dev server logs.\n\n## Files changed (15 total)\n- 14 CSS modules modified\n- 1 new file: docs/responsive-qa.md\n\nReady for Step 8 instructions.', 'timeout': 1800000}
