reated centralized motion language consumed by all future animation systems:\n- Created motion/tokens.ts: TypeScript motion vocabulary (MOTION_DURATION, MOTION_EASE, MOTION_STAGGER, MOTION_DISTANCE, REDUCED_MOTION_QUERY)\n- Created styles/motion.css: CSS custom properties for motion tokens with full prefers-reduced-motion policy (collapses all durations to 1ms, staggers to 0ms, distances to 0px, scroll-behavior to auto)\n- Created docs/motion-system.md: Motion system documentation with purpose, duration/easing/stagger/distance vocabularies, implementation rules\n- Imported motion.css globally in app/layout.tsx\n- Token parity verified: TS seconds = CSS milliseconds, CSS rem = TS pixels\n- No actual animation added, no dependencies installed\n- Lint: PASS, TypeScript: PASS, Build: PASS\n\n## Step 9: Smooth Scroll / Lenis (Commit 7ebac5d)\nInstalled and configured Lenis 1.3.26 as global smooth-scroll layer:\n- Created components/providers/SmoothScroll.tsx: Client component wrapping children in Lenis with configuration (autoRaf: false, autoResize: true, anchors: true, lerp: 0.1, smoothWheel: true, syncTouch: false, respectReducedMotion: true, stopInertiaOnNavigate: true)\n- Imported lenis/dist/lenis.css in layout.tsx\n- Created docs/smooth-scroll.md: Smooth scroll documentation with configuration details, touch policy, accessibility policy\n- Updated docs/motion-system.md current state\n- Native document/window scrolling (no fake containers)\n- Manual RAF loop (leaves path for GSAP ScrollTrigger)\n- Lint: PASS, TypeScript: PASS, Build: PASS, All routes HTTP 200\n\n## Step 10: Text Reveal Animations (Commit f6fe855)\nInstalled GSAP 3.15.0 + @gsap/react 2.1.2 and implemented line-based text reveals:\n- Created motion/gsap.ts: Centralized GSAP plugin registration (ScrollTrigger, SplitText, CustomEase, useGSAP) with CustomEase derived from Step 8 easing tokens\n- Created components/motion/TextMotion.tsx: Client component using GSAP matchMedia with (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference), SplitText line-based reveals for hero (48px, 1.1s, 70ms stagger) and scroll (24px, 560ms, 40ms stagger, top 88% trigger, once: true)\n- Updated SmoothScroll.tsx: Replaced manual RAF with GSAP ticker (gsap.ticker.add/remove), Lenis scroll → ScrollTrigger.update sync\n- Marked 12 text targets with data-text-reveal attributes:\n  - Hero (hero): ANURAG KOUSHIK title\n  - IntroStatement (lines): "I DESIGN SYSTEMS THAT CONNECT"\n  - SelectedWork (lines): Heading + 3 project titles\n  - Capabilities (lines): "FROM CIRCUITS TO CODE."\n  - AboutPreview (lines): "ENGINEER BY TRAINING..."\n  - ContactCTA (lines): "HAVE SOMETHING INTERESTING?"\n  - ProjectHero (hero): All 3 dynamic project titles\n  - ProjectSection (lines): All 8 case-study section titles\n  - NextProject (lines): Next project title\n- SSR build issue: CustomEase.create() rejected CSS cubic-bezier() strings, fixed with SVG path format (M0,1 C0.16,1,0.3,1,1,0)\n- No character/word animation, no scrub/pin, no arbitrary timings\n- Lint: PASS, TypeScript: PASS, Build: PASS\n\n## Step 11: Custom Cursor System (Commit 917df7a)\nImplemented capability-aware custom cursor for fine-pointer desktop:\n- Easing remediation: Created canonical cubic-bezier control points in motion/tokens.ts (MOTION_EASE_POINTS), derived both CSS (toCssCubicBezier) and GSAP (toGsapCubicBezier) representations from single source. Removed hardcoded SVG paths from motion/gsap.ts.\n- Created components/cursor/CustomCursor.tsx: Client component with zero React state, zero RAF loop. Uses GSAP matchMedia for (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) and (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference). Direct 4px dot (gsap.set), 36px ring with GSAP.quickTo interpolation (MICRO duration), contextual labels. No glow/blur/blend modes.\n- Created components/cursor/CustomCursor.module.css: Conditional native cursor hiding via html[data-custom-cursor="true"], reduced-motion display:none, IBM Plex Mono labels, pointer-events: none on all cursor elements.\