pe |\n|------|-------|------|\n| 2026-09-01 | First Day of Classes | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-09-07 | Labour Day | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-09-30 | National Day for Truth and Reconciliation | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-10-12 | Thanksgiving Day | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-11-09 to 2026-11-13 | Fall Reading Week | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-11-11 | Remembrance Day | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-12-08 | Last Day of Classes | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2026-12-09 to 2026-12-22 | Final Exam Period | ACADEMIC_CALENDAR |\n| 2027-01-09 | ECE449 Deferred Final Exam (contingency) | CONTINGENCY |\n\n### Corrected Data-Model Rules\n\n**Course Event:** An official, dated, one-off event belonging to a specific course and section (or course-wide). Includes: labs, quizzes, assignments, midterms, term exams, lecture meetings, discussion posts, tech checks, training sessions, project milestones.\n\n**Semester-Wide Event:** A university-wide academic calendar date (holidays, reading week, first/last day, exam period). Not attributed to any single course.\n\n**Recurring Timetable Block:** A standing meeting that recurs weekly throughout the term (lectures, seminars, lab blocks). Defined by: course, section, meeting type, days, time, location, recurrence rule, exceptions. NOT counted as individual one-off event rows.\n\n**TBA Event:** An official assessment whose date is known to exist but whose specific date/time has not been released. Includes: ECE302 Final Exam, ECE449 Final Exam.\n\n**Contingency Event:** A policy-level event that applies only under specific circumstances (deferred exams, excused absence deferrals). Documented but not placed in the weekly calendar.\n\n**Section-Specific Event:** An event that applies only to a particular registered section (lab dates, lab report due dates, section-specific seminar events). Filtered to user\'s registered section.\n\n**Course-Wide Event:** An assessment or deadline that applies to all sections of a course (quizzes, midterms, term