e lecture notes.\n\n**Cannot be mapped to M/W/F dates:** The syllabus lists M/W/F lectures (10:00-10:50) for 12 weeks, but only 5 lecture PDFs exist. There is no source establishing which lecture PDF corresponds to which class date. The filenames "lec1" through "lec5" could map to the first 5 lectures, but this is an assumption, not a source fact.\n\n**Proposed final tracker treatment:**\n- The syllabus "Approximate Lecture Timeline" table provides a WEEK_ORDERED_CONTENT topic sequence (diodes → semiconductors → BJTs → FETs → amplifiers) that can be displayed as a course overview.\n- The 5 lecture PDFs and 2 example PDFs should be listed as available materials with filename provenance only.\n- No dated lecture topics should be attached to specific calendar dates.\n- Classification: SEQUENCE_ONLY_CONTENT for PDFs, WEEK_ORDERED_CONTENT for the syllabus timeline.\n\n## ECE449 Content Findings\n\n**Lecture/course topics available:** NONE. The syllabus has a course description mentioning topics (fuzzy systems, neural networks, evolutionary computing, LLMs) but no week-by-week or dated topic breakdown.\n\n**Lab-topic progression:**\n- Lab 1: AI pipelines in Scikit-learn (Sep 17)\n- Lab 2: Prompt Engineering with OpenAI (Oct 1)\n- Lab 3: Deep Learning in Tensorflow/Keras (Oct 15)\n- Lab 4: Fuzzy Trees with skfuzzy (Oct 29)\n- Lab 5: Genetic-Fuzzy systems with skfuzzy and EasyGA (Nov 19)\n- Report due dates follow (Oct 1, Oct 15, Oct 29, Nov 19, Dec 3)\n\n**Lab titles vs lecture topics:** Lab titles are dated and specific. They should be used in the lab tracker because the dates are official. However, they should NOT be presented as the corresponding lecture topic unless a source explicitly establishes that relationship (none exists).\n\n**Lecture dates/topics cannot be mapped:** No source maps lecture content to specific dates. The ICS recurrence (MWF 13:00-13:50) provides the standing timetable but no topic content.\n\n**Proposed tracker treatment:** Lab-only topic tracker with exact dates. No lecture topic section. The group project (Dec 8) is the only dated non-lab milestone.\n\n## ECE485 Chapter Progression\n\n| Order | File/Chapter | Official Title | Major Topic | Date Metadata | Week Metadata | Calendar-Mappable? |\n|-------|-------------|---------------|-------------|---------------|---------------|-------------------|\n| 00 | 00-Preface-and-Contents.md | A Short Course on Digital Communications | Preface + Table of Contents | None | None | No |\n| 01 | 01-Why-Digital-Communication.md | Chapter 1: Why Digital Communication? | Motivation, history, analog vs digital, system block diagram | None | None | No |\n| 02 | 02-Basics-Of-Probability-Theory.md | Chapter 2: Basics of Probability Theory | Probability axioms, random variables, CDF, expected value, variance | None | None | No |\n| 03 | 03-Information-Theory.md | Chapter 3: Information Theory | Entropy, mutual information, source/channel coding, channel capacity | None | None | No |\n| 04 | 04-Geometric-Representation-Of-Signals.md | Chapter 4: Geometric Representation of Signals | Signal space, vector space, orthonormal basis, Gram-Schmidt | None | None | No |\n| 05 | 05-An-Introduction-To-Binary-Modulations.md | Chapter 5: An Introduction to Binary Modulations | Binary antipodal/orthogonal signaling, constellation, decision regions | None | None | No |\n| 06 | 06-Pulse-Amplitude-Modulation.md | Chapter 6: Pulse Amplitude Modulation | PAM, AWGN channel, matched filter, constellation design, QAM | None | None | No |\n| 07 | 07-Transmission-On-Bandlimited-Additive-White-Gaussian-Noise-Channel.md | Chapter 7: Transmission on Band-Limited AWGN Channel | ISI, Nyquist criterion, root-raised-cosine pulses, spectral efficiency | None | None | No |\n\n**Exact sequence:** Chapters 1-7 in the order listed above. The preface explicitly describes the progression: probability (Ch 2) → information theory (Ch 3) → signal space (Ch 4) → binary modulation (Ch 5) → PAM (Ch 6) → band-limited channels (Ch 7). Chapter 8 (advanced modulations) is mentioned in the preface but explicitly noted as NOT included.\n\n**Chapter-to-quiz/exam coverage:** DOES NOT EXIST. The syllabus lists 6 quiz dates and 3 term exam dates but does NOT state which chapters each covers. The following tempting inferences are explicitly rejected:\n- Quiz 1 does NOT explicitly cover "Chapters 1-2"\n- Term Exam 1 does NOT explicitly cover "Chapters 1-4"\n- No chapter-to-quiz mapping should be invented\n\n**No chapter-date mapping is legitimate:** The syllabus provides no weekly schedule, no chapter-to-week mapping, and no reading deadlines. The lectures are on Tuesdays and Thursdays (11:00-12:20) but no source states which chapter is taught on which day.\n\n**Proposed progress-tracker design:** A simple chapter checklist with status columns:\n```\nStatus | Chapter | Title\n[ ]    | 1       | Why Digital Communication?\n[ ]    | 2       | Basics of Probability Theory\n...\n```\nNo dates, no week assignments. The existing dated events (quizzes, exams, labs) are listed separately as assessment deadlines.\n\n## ECE490 Weekly Progression\n\n| Week/Date | Activity/Topic | Classification | Associated Deadline if Explicit |\n|-----------|---------------|---------------|-------------------------------|\n| Week 1 | Term starts | ADMINISTRATIVE | — |\n| Week 2, Sep 11 | Assignment 1 Due (forms) | ASSIGNMENT | Sep 11 (Friday) |\n| Week 3, Sep 14-18 | Lab Safety Training + Solder Training | TRAINING | Window Sep 14-18 |\n| Week 3, Sep 18 | Group Form Submission | ADMINISTRATIVE | Sep 18 (Friday) |\n| Week 4, Sep 21 | Lab Orientation | LAB_ACTIVITY | — |\n| Week 4, Sep 21 | Lab 2: Soldering – Lab Assignment starts | LAB_ACTIVITY | — |\n| Week 5, Sep 28 | Lecture 3 | LECTURE_TOPIC | — |\n| Week 5, Oct 2 | Assignment 2 Due (Altium+PCB) | ASSIGNMENT | Oct 2 (Friday) |\n| Week 5, Oct 2 | Project Form Submission | ADMINISTRATIVE | Oct 2 (Friday) |\n| Week 7, Oct 13 | Assignment 3 Due (Requirement Specs) | ASSIGNMENT | Oct 13 (Tuesday) |\n| Week 8, Oct 19 | Lecture 5 | LECTURE_TOPIC | — |\n| Week 9, Oct 26 | Lecture 6 | LECTURE_TOPIC | — |\n| Week 9, Oct 30 | Assignment 4 Due (Progress Report I) | ASSIGNMENT | Oct 30 (Friday) |\n| Week 12, Nov 16 | Assignment 5 Due (CDR PowerPoint) | ASSIGNMENT | Nov 16 (Monday) |\n| Week 12, Nov 16-20 | CDR Presentations (window 1) | CDR_ACTIVITY | Window Nov 16-20 |\n| Week 13, Nov 23-27 | CDR Presentations continue (window 2) | CDR_ACTIVITY | Window Nov 23-27 |\n| Week 15, Dec 7 | Assignment 6 Due (Revised Design Report) | ASSIGNMENT | Dec 7 (Monday) |\n\n**Calendar content:** The 6 labeled lectures (Lectures 1-6) and assignment deadlines should appear in the calendar with their dates.\n\n**Milestone tracker:** The training activities (safety, soldering), lab activities, and CDR presentation windows should appear in a separate milestone tracker showing the project progression.\n\n**Both:** Some items (like Assignment 5 due Nov 16) overlap with CDR presentations — these are both calendar events and milestones.\n\n**Neither:** Generic "Lecture N" entries for the 5 unmarked Mondays (Nov 2, Nov 30, Dec 7; and the two CDR weeks) should not have lecture titles manufactured.\n\n**Classification:** MIXED — WEEK_ORDERED_CONTENT for the 6 labeled lectures, MILESTONE_TRACKER for training/lab/CDR activities, ASSIGNMENT_DEADLINES for all 6 assignments.\n\n## ENGG400 Dated Topic Progression\n\n| Lecture | Date | Topic | Related Official Assessment if Explicit |\n|---------|------|-------|----------------------------------------|\n| Lecture 1 | 2026-09-04 (Fri) | Onboarding | — |\n| Lecture 2 | 2026-09-11 (Fri) | Life-long Learning | Quiz 1 due same day |\n| Lecture 3 | 2026-09-18 (Fri) | Ethics + Innovation in Industry | Quiz 2 due same day |\n| Lecture 4 | 2026-09-25 (Fri) | Choose Your Own Adventure (Post-Grad Edition) | — |\n| Lecture 5 | 2026-10-02 (Fri) | Intellectual Property | Quiz 3 due same day |\n| Lecture 6 | 2026-10-09 (Fri) | Entrepreneurship + Intrapreneurship | — |\n| Lecture 7 | 2026-10-16 (Fri) | APEGA | Quiz 4 due same day |\n| Lecture 8 | 2026-10-23 (Fri) | Ethics in Engineering | Quiz 5 due same day |\n| Lecture 9 | 2026-10-30 (Fri) | Reconciliation in Engineering | — |\n| Lecture 10 | 2026-11-06 (Fri) | Advice from an ENGG Alumni | — |\n| Lecture 11 | 2026-11-20 (Fri) | Calling of the Engineer (Iron Ring) | — |\n| Lecture 12 | 2026-11-27 (Fri) | Equity in Engineering | Quiz 6 due same day |\n| Lecture 13 | 2026-12-04 (Fri) | Environmental Stewardship | Quiz 7 due same day |\n\n**All 13 lectures are exactly date-mappable.** Each has a specific Friday date, a topic title, and associated learning outcomes from the Course Plan.\n\n**Quiz-lecture associations from proximity only:** Some quizzes are due on the same Friday as a lecture (e.g., Quiz 1 due Sep 11, Lecture 2 on Sep 11). The syllabus does NOT explicitly state which lecture a quiz covers. The quiz table shows "Quiz #1 Week 2" and the Course Plan shows "Week 2: Life-long Learning" — this is a WEEK-BASED association, not an explicit lecture-to-quiz mapping. The assessment deadline summary table does group them together but doesn\'t state causal coverage.\n\n**Classification:** EXACT_DATED_CONTENT — all 13 lectures have explicit date, topic, and learning outcome mappings.\n\n## SUST201 Content/Module Progression\n\n**Module/topic structure:** The syllabus lists 8 course topics under "COURSE OVERVIEW" as bullet points:\n1. Development, Economic Growth, Societal Benefits, and Environmental Harm\n2. The Rise of Sustainability as a Concept\n3. Social Dilemmas, Common Property, and Collective Action\n4. Economic Approaches to Environmental Protection\n5. Cultural Institutions, Growth, and Sustainability and the Environment\n6. Stakeholders and Politics\n7. Case Studies in Sustainability\n8. Sustainability Transition\n\n**Reading structure:** There is no textbook. Readings are available online via Canvas. No reading schedule or reading-to-week mapping exists.\n\n**Relationship to quizzes:** The syllabus states quizzes "cover the content of all readings and assigned content (may include videos or other content) due since the last quiz." This means:\n- Quiz 1 (Sep 18): covers content from Sep 1 through Sep 18\n- Quiz 2 (Oct 2): covers content from Sep 18 through Oct 2\n- etc.\n\nBut NO explicit module-to-quiz mapping exists. The syllabus does NOT say "Quiz 1 covers Modules 1-2."\n\n**Date mapping:** Only quiz/exam dates are available. No weekly topic dates. The async nature means students access content on Canvas on a rolling basis.\n\n**Asynchronous pacing implications:** Creating a fake weekly structure would be misleading. The schedule should show assessment deadlines (quizzes, midterms, final, discussion posts) separately from the topic list. Students are expected to keep up with Canvas content, but there is no official weekly topic release schedule.\n\n**Proposed tracker treatment:** Assessment deadline table only. The 8 course topics listed as a reference checklist. No date-to-topic mapping.\n\n## Content-to-Calendar Mapping Matrix\n\n| Course | Attach Topics to Weekly Calendar? | Separate Progress Tracker? | Exact or Planned? | Reason |\n|--------|----------------------------------|---------------------------|-------------------|--------|\n| ECE302 | No — only approximate week blocks | Yes — topic checklist + PDF inventory | Planned (approximate) | Syllabus timeline is approximate; PDFs lack date metadata |\n| ECE449 | No — no lecture topic dates | Yes — lab topic tracker | Exact for labs only | Lab topics are dated; lecture topics are not |\n| ECE485 | No — no chapter dates | Yes — chapter progress checklist | Sequence only | 7 chapters in order but no dates or quiz coverage |\n| ECE490 | Yes — 6 labeled lectures | Yes — milestone tracker | Exact for labeled lectures, planned for others | 6 lectures have dates; training/CDR are milestones |\n| ENGG400 | Yes — all 13 lectures | No — calendar is sufficient | Exact | Every lecture has explicit date + topic |\n| SUST201 | No — async, no weekly topics | Yes — topic checklist + assessment table | Assessment dates only | Topics listed but no weekly release schedule |\n\n## Progress Status Policy\n\nProgress fields in the final schedule will be:\n- **[ ]** — unchecked, for items not yet completed\n- **NOT TRACKED** — for items where completion is not relevant (e.g., lecture topics)\n\n**Elapsed calendar time is NOT treated as evidence of completion.** The reference date is September 14, 2026. Events in the past (e.g., ENGG400 Lecture 1 on Sep 4, ECE490 Assignment 1 on Sep 11) are marked as PAST in the current-date classification, but their completion status remains **[ ]** (unchecked) unless the user provides evidence of completion.\n\n## Current-Date Classification\n\n**Reference date: September 14, 2026 (Monday)**\n\n| Category | Count |\n|----------|-------|\n| Past (fully before Sep 14) | 5 |\n| Active/Today (includes Sep 14) | 2 |\n| Upcoming (strictly after Sep 14) | 73 |\n\n**Events active on September 14, 2026:**\n1. ECE485 Lab 1 — Monday, Sep 14 (today)\n2. ECE490 Lab Safety Training + Solder Training — window Sep 14-18 (active today)\n\n**5 Past events:**\n1. ECE302 Lab intro session — Sep 8 (Tuesday)\n2. ECE490 Assignment 1 (forms) — Sep 11 (Friday)\n3. ENGG400 Lecture 1 (Onboarding) — Sep 4 (Friday)\n4. ENGG400 Quiz 1 — Sep 11 (Friday)\n5. ENGG400 Lecture 2 (Life-long Learning) — Sep 11 (Friday)\n\n**73 Upcoming events:** All remaining course-specific dated events.\n\n**No events marked as completed.** PAST ≠ COMPLETED.\n\n## Unsupported Mappings Explicitly Rejected\n\n1. **ECE485 chapter-to-quiz mapping:** The syllabus does not state which chapters each quiz or term exam covers. Do NOT distribute 7 chapters across 6 quizzes or 3 exams.\n\n2. **ECE485 chapter-to-week mapping:** The syllabus does not provide a weekly schedule. Do NOT assign "Week 1 = Chapter 1, Week 2 = Chapter 2."\n\n3. **ECE302 PDF-to-class-date mapping:** 5 lecture PDFs exist for 12 weeks of M/W/F lectures. Do NOT assume lec1 = first class, lec2 = second class, etc.\n\n4. **ECE449 lab-to-lecture topic mapping:** Lab titles (e.g., "AI pipelines in Scikit-learn") are NOT necessarily the corresponding lecture topic. Do NOT present lab titles as lecture content without explicit source evidence.\n\n5. **ECE449 lecture topic mapping:** No lecture topics or weekly schedule exists. Do NOT invent lecture content from the learning outcomes.\n\n6. **SUST201 module-to-quiz mapping:** The syllabus does not state which modules each reading quiz covers. Do NOT assign "Quiz 1 = Modules 1-2."\n\n7. **ECE490 unmarked Monday topics:** 5 Mondays have no syllabus lecture title. Do NOT manufacture lecture topics for these dates.\n\n8. **ECE302 PDF content as lecture notes:** The PDFs are 2-4 page scans. Do NOT treat them as complete lecture notes or assume they cover all topics for a given week.\n\n9. **ECE485 Chapter 8:** The preface mentions Chapter 8 (advanced modulations) but explicitly states it is NOT included. Do NOT create content for it.\n\n10. **ECE449 lab dates from syllabus vs LabSchedule.md:** The syllabus lists different lab dates (Sep 10, 24, Oct 8, 22, Nov 5) which are for D41 section. The user is in D42 with different dates (Sep 17, Oct 1, Oct 15, Oct 29, Nov 19). Do NOT use the syllabus lab dates for the user\'s schedule.\n\n## Remaining Content Uncertainties\n\n1. **ECE302 lecture PDF content:** The 5 PDFs are image-based scans with no extractable text. Their actual content (chapters/topics covered) cannot be verified without OCR. The filenames suggest lecture numbers but this is unconfirmed.\n\n2. **ECE449 lecture content:** No lecture notes, slides, or topic materials exist in the repository. The syllabus describes the course scope but provides no week-by-week breakdown.\n\n3. **ECE485 chapter delivery order:** While the chapter sequence is clear (1-7), the actual pace at which the instructor delivers content may differ from the book order. No weekly schedule exists to confirm.\n\n4. **SUST201 Canvas content structure:** The actual module/reading structure on Canvas may differ from the 8 topics listed in the syllabus. The syllabus topics may be high-level themes rather than formal modules.\n\n## Modification Check\n\n**Zero repository files modified.** Step 5 was pure analysis and verification.\n\n---\n\nReady for your review. Awaiting approval to proceed to Step 6.'}
