16:37:16 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'STEP 6 COMPLETE\n\n## Recurring / Policy Source Review\n\n| Course | Sources Re-read | Relevant Policy Sections | Confidence |\n|--------|----------------|-------------------------|------------|\n| ECE302 | Syllabus.md, ECE302 Lab Schedule.md | Labs, problem sets, exams, formula sheets, missed exam policy, calculator policy, pass condition | High — explicit source text |\n| ECE449 | Syllabus.md, LabSchedule.md | Late work, lab attendance, group project, calculator policy, deferred exam, collaboration | High — explicit source text |\n| ECE485 | Syllabus.md (full document) | Best 5 of 6 quizzes, term exam format, formula sheets, calculator policy, open-book quizzes | High — explicit source text |\n| ECE490 | Syllabus.md (full document) | Late policy (20%/day), group work, safety prerequisites, CDR process, lab notebook evaluation, AI use | High — explicit source text |\n| ENGG400 | Syllabus.md (full document, 369 lines) | CR/F rules, 10/13 attendance, 7 quizzes (50% min each, 70% cumulative), 2 attempts, assignment requirements, AI declaration | High — explicit source text |\n| SUST201 | Syllabus.md (full document) | Async model, quiz grace period, midterm/final windows, discussion post cadence, technology check, exam integrity | High — explicit source text |\n\n## Recurring Obligations by Course\n\n### ECE302\n- **Recurring meetings:** LEC A2 MWF 10:00-10:50; SEM E32 WE 12:00-12:50; LAB D22 TU 14:00-16:50\n- **Recurring academic work:** Problem sets — "given throughout the term," selected questions hand-in/marked, solutions posted after deadline. No dates stated. OFFICIAL RECURRING ACADEMIC WORK — DATES UNSPECIFIED.\n- **Attendance requirements:** "Very important that you attend the lectures and seminars for which you are registered." No minimum threshold stated. Not a pass requirement.\n- **Submission cadence:** Problem sets — ad hoc (no stated schedule). Labs — 5 numbered dates only.\n- **Ongoing responsibilities:** Obtain lab manual before Lab 1; find lab partner; purchase lab kits.\n- **Obligations with no exact date:** Problem set due dates.\n\n### ECE449\n- **Recurring meetings:** LEC A1 MWF 13:00-13:50; LAB D42 TH 14:00-16:50\n- **Recurring academic work:** 5 lab reports — individual work.\n- **Attendance requirements:** None explicitly stated.\n- **Submission cadence:** Reports due at beginning of next lab session. Lab 1 due Oct 1 (same date as Lab 2). Lab 5 due Dec 3.\n- **Lab 4 extended completion:** Due to reading week, Lab D42 has 3 weeks to complete Lab 4 (instead of the usual 2-week cycle).\n- **Late-work policy:** "LATE WORK IS NOT ACCEPTED; late assignments will receive a grade of \'0.\'" (from course policies section)\n- **Group-project obligations:** Group-based term project, 3-person teams, 10%. Teams not permitted to collaborate with one another.\n- **Exam/calculator restrictions:** Non-programmable calculator only (gold sticker).\n\n### ECE485\n- **Recurring meetings:** LEC A1 TU TH 11:00-12:20; LAB D11 MO 14:00-16:50\n- **Recurring academic work:** 6 quizzes scheduled, best 5 of 6 count at 2% each. 20 min duration each.\n- **Quiz format:** Open book. No stated attempt limit. No stated time limit (20 min suggests in-class).\n- **Term exams:** 70 min each, closed book, two-sided letter-size formula sheet allowed.\n- **Calculator policy:** No calculator policy — free to use any calculator.\n- **Missed quiz/exam policy:** NOT STATED. The "best 5 of 6" rule implies one quiz is dropped, but the syllabus does NOT explicitly state that a missed quiz is automatically excused/dropped.\n- **Lab requirements:** 5 labs, 15% total (3% each). No pre-lab or post-lab reporting rules stated.\n- **Recurring readings/homework:** NOT STATED.\n\n### ECE490\n- **Recurring meetings:** LEC A1 MO 08:00-08:50; LAB D51 FR 14:00-16:50\n- **Recurring project work:** Team-based design project — ongoing throughout semester.\n- **Team requirements:** Group form due Sep 18. Project form due Oct 2.\n- **Safety prerequisites:** Safety training + solder training required (Sep 14-18 window). Lab-specific safety procedures expected at all times.\n- **CDR process:** Assignment 5 (PowerPoint due Nov 16, Noon) + presentations Nov 16-20 and Nov 23-27.\n- **Lab notebook:** Evaluated individually by client, advisor, and TA — focuses on project progress, technical contributions, teamwork, and communication.\n- **Late policy:** 20% deduction per day. "Missed work will receive a mark of 0%."\n- **Group vs individual:** Assignment 1, 2, 3 are individual (marked *). Assignments 4, 5, 6 include both group and individual assessment (marked ***). Assignment 5 has individual-based assessment too.\n- **Ongoing vs dated milestones:** Training (Sep 14-18), Lab 2 (Sep 21 – Oct 2 window), CDR sessions (Nov 16), project meetings, lab activities — ongoing process not on fixed dates.\n\n### ENGG400\n- **Recurring meetings:** LEC A1 FR 12:00-12:50 (13 weeks)\n- **Attendance requirements:** Minimum 10 of 13 lectures. Attendance recorded via weekly question submitted in class (must be genuine attempt, not just headcount). Records shared with Dean\'s Office and ENGG Advising.\n- **Quiz requirements:** 7 quizzes, open-resource (including AI), 2 attempts each, higher score recorded. Must achieve ≥50% on each quiz AND ≥70% cumulative average across all 7.\n- **Assignment requirements:** All 4 assignments must be satisfactorily completed. Assignment 2 (IDP) must receive ≥70%. AI Use Declaration required on each written assignment.\n- **CR/F logic:** All three conditions must be met. Failure of any = No Credit, graduation delayed.\n\n### SUST201\n- **Recurring meetings:** NONE (fully asynchronous)\n- **Ongoing content expectation:** Canvas-based, rolling basis. Lectures updated on rolling basis (some from previous semester). Readings available 2 weeks before each quiz due date.\n- **Quiz due dates:** Sep 18, Oct 2, Oct 15, Oct 30, Nov 26\n- **Quiz availability/grace:** Quizzes remain open for additional 7 days after due date as automatic extension. Missing extension = zero.\n- **Midterm windows:** Noon to 10pm on exam day (75 min with 1.5x multiplier). Closed book, online via Canvas with Respondus LockDown Browser.\n- **Final window:** Noon Dec 7 to 1:30pm Dec 8 (120 min with 1.5x multiplier).\n- **Discussion posts:** At least 2 posts (one by Oct 17). 6 total replies (3 before Oct 17, 3 after Oct 17). Half marks for posts after Oct 17 but before Dec 4. Final posts/comments due Dec 4 (hard deadline).\n- **Technology:** Respondus LockDown Browser required. Tech check available Sept 1, due Sept 29 for full 1%.\n\n## Assessment and Submission Rules\n\n| Course | Rule | Applies To | Planning Impact | Display Treatment |\n|--------|------|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| ECE302 | Best-of-none (no "best of" rule stated) | All assessments | Must write all midterms and final | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE302 | Pass condition: complete both labs + ≥50% lab mark + ≥50% cumulative raw mark | Overall course | Lab performance is pass-critical | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE302 | Formula sheet allowed (details TBD) | Midterms + Final | Planning for sheet preparation | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE302 | Non-programmable calculator (gold sticker) | All exams | Must obtain sticker | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE302 | Missed midterm: waiver + marks tacked onto final | Midterm 1, Midterm 2 | Deferral transfers weight, does NOT create makeup exam | CONTINGENCY_ONLY |\n| ECE449 | Late work = zero grade | All lab reports | Strict deadline enforcement | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE449 | Lab reports due at beginning of NEXT lab session | All 5 labs | Report deadlines = next lab date | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ECE449 | Lab 4 has 3-week completion window (reading week exception) | Lab 4 | Extended deadline for Lab 4 report | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ECE449 | Non-programmable calculator only (gold sticker) | All exams | Must obtain sticker | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE449 | Deferred final: Jan 9, 2027 | Final exam only | Contingency only | CONTINGENCY_ONLY |\n| ECE485 | Best 5 of 6 quizzes (2% each, 10% total) | Quizzes | One quiz may be dropped — but mechanism NOT specified | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE485 | Open book | All 6 quizzes | Can prepare reference materials | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE485 | Two-sided letter-size formula sheet | Term Exams 1-3 | Planning for sheet preparation | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE485 | No calculator policy | All assessments | Free calculator use | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE490 | 20% late penalty per day | All 6 assignments | Time-sensitive deadlines | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE490 | Missed work = 0% | All assignments | No late submissions accepted beyond penalty | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE490 | Safety training prerequisite for lab access | All labs | Must complete training before Lab 2 | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ECE490 | Individual lab notebook evaluation | All labs | Ongoing documentation requirement | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | Credit/No Credit — ALL conditions required | Overall course | Missing any single requirement = No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE |\n| ENGG400 | 10 of 13 lectures minimum | All lectures | Attendance tracking critical | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | ≥50% on EACH of 7 quizzes | All quizzes | No single quiz can be below 50% | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | ≥70% cumulative across 7 quizzes | All quizzes | Low scores on early quizzes must be recovered | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | Two attempts per quiz, higher score recorded | All quizzes | Can retake any quiz | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ENGG400 | All 4 assignments must be satisfactory | All assignments | Missing any = No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | Assignment 2 (IDP) must be ≥70% | Assignment 2 | Specific threshold for IDP | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | AI Use Declaration on each written assignment | Assignments 1-4 | Must declare AI use | POLICY_NOTE |\n| SUST201 | 7-day automatic extension on quizzes | All 5 quizzes | Nominal due date vs. actual deadline | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Missed quiz = zero (no make-up) | All quizzes | Must write by end of grace period | POLICY_NOTE |\n| SUST201 | Midterm: Noon to 10pm on exam day | Midterm 1, Midterm 2 | 10-hour availability window | CALENDAR_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Final: Noon Dec 7 to 1:30pm Dec 8 | Final Exam | ~25.5-hour availability window | CALENDAR_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Respondus LockDown Browser required | All exams | Tech setup prerequisite | POLICY_NOTE |\n| SUST201 | Discussion: 2 posts + 6 replies total | Discussion posts | Ongoing participation requirement | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Discussion: one post by Oct 17 | Discussion posts | Early deadline for initial posts | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Discussion: final by Dec 4 (hard deadline) | Discussion posts | End-of-semester hard deadline | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n\n## Pass-Critical Requirements\n\n| Course | Requirement | Threshold/Condition | Consequence | Final Schedule Treatment |\n|--------|-----------|---------------------|-------------|-------------------------|\n| ECE302 | Complete both labs | 5 labs (D22 section) | Lab work incomplete | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ECE302 | Cumulative lab mark ≥50% | Across all labs | May not pass course | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE302 | Cumulative raw mark ≥50% | Overall course | May not pass course | POLICY_NOTE |\n| ECE449 | Complete all 5 labs | Lab 1-5 | Late work = zero | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ECE449 | Submit all 5 reports | At beginning of next lab | Late work = zero | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | Attend ≥10 of 13 lectures | Any 10 lectures | No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE |\n| ENGG400 | Complete all 4 assignments | All must be satisfactory | No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | ≥50% on each of 7 quizzes | Per-quiz minimum | No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE |\n| ENGG400 | ≥70% cumulative across 7 quizzes | Average across all | No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| ENGG400 | ≥70% on Assignment 2 (IDP) | Specific assignment | No Credit | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Complete tech check | By Sept 29 | Lose 1% (not pass-critical) | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Complete all 5 quizzes | By end of grace period | Missed = zero | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n| SUST201 | Complete discussion posts | By Dec 4 (hard deadline) | Lose engagement marks | TRACKER_VISIBLE |\n\nNote: ECE485, ECE490 have no explicit pass/fail threshold conditions stated in the syllabi beyond standard university grading. ECE449 has no explicit pass condition beyond standard grading.\n\n## Late / Deadline-Sensitive Policies\n\n| Course | Policy | Trigger | Consequence | Source |\n|--------|--------|---------|-------------|--------|\n| ECE449 | Late lab reports | After lab session begins | Grade of 0 | Syllabus policies: "LATE WORK IS NOT ACCEPTED; late assignments will receive a grade of \'0.\'" |\n| ECE490 | Late assignments | After due date | 20% deduction per day | Syllabus: "late work will receive the described penalty" |\n| ECE490 | Missed work | After deadline | 0% | Syllabus: "missed work will receive a mark of 0%" |\n| SUST201 | Quiz past grace period | 7 days after due date | Zero | Syllabus: "you will get a zero" |\n| SUST201 | Discussion past Dec 4 | After Dec 4 11:59pm | No posts/comments accepted | Syllabus: "hard deadline in which no posts or comments will be accepted after" |\n| ENGG400 | IDP submission folder | Opens 2 weeks before deadline | Cannot submit early (admin) | Syllabus: "submission folder will open two weeks prior" |\n\n## Lab Preparation / Reporting Cadence\n\n| Course | Section | Before Lab | During Lab | After Lab | Recurring Rule Supported? |\n|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|-----------|--------------------------|\n| ECE302 | D22 | Obtain manual ASAP; preparatory work required | Lab work per manual | Lab reports (not explicitly described) | Partial — manual prep stated; report format not described |\n| ECE449 | D42 | Read lab manual (implied) | Lab work per topic | Lab report due beginning of NEXT lab | Yes — report cadence explicit |\n| ECE485 | D11 | NOT STATED | Lab work per topic | NOT STATED | No — no pre/post lab rules stated |\n| ECE490 | D51 | Safety training (Lab 1); safety procedures at all times | Lab work per activity; lab notebook | Lab notebook evaluated continuously | Yes — safety prerequisite + ongoing notebook |\n\nNote: Do NOT generalize Lab 1 instructions (safety training, soldering) to all labs unless explicitly stated. ECE485 has no pre-lab or post-lab reporting rules in the syllabus.\n\n## SUST201 Asynchronous Model\n\n**Ongoing content expectation:**\n- Canvas-based, rolling basis\n- Lectures updated on rolling basis (some recorded from previous semester)\n- Readings available 2 weeks prior to each quiz due date\n- No fixed weekly schedule — students expected to keep up\n- "It is highly unlikely that you will do well without watching lectures regularly"\n\n**Quiz due-date model:**\n- Nominal due dates: Sep 18, Oct 2, Oct 15, Oct 30, Nov 26\n- Readings posted 2 weeks before due date\n- Nominal due date is the DUE DATE\n\n**Quiz availability/grace model:**\n- Quizzes remain open for additional 7 days as automatic extension\n- If crisis after extension: zero\n- No stated attempt limit\n- No stated time limit (but 75-min exam duration suggests quiz is shorter)\n\n**Midterm availability windows:**\n- Available from Noon to 10pm on exam day\n- 75 minutes to write (50 min + 1.5x multiplier)\n- Closed book, online via Canvas with Respondus LockDown Browser\n- Start by 9pm to get full time\n\n**Final availability window:**\n- Opens Noon Dec 7, closes 1:30pm Dec 8\n- 120 minutes to write (80 min + 1.5x multiplier)\n- Start by 11:30am Dec 8 for full time\n\n**Discussion-post cadence:**\n- Initial: at least 2 posts (one by Oct 17)\n- Replies: 6 total (3 before Oct 17, 3 after Oct 17)\n- Half marks for posts/comments after Oct 17 but before Dec 4\n- Final posts/comments due Dec 4 (hard deadline)\n\n**Technology requirements:**\n- Respondus LockDown Browser required for all exams\n- Tech check available Sept 1, due Sept 29 for full 1%\n- Exams monitored via recorded video\n\n**Weekly calendar display:**\n- CALENDAR_VISIBLE: Quiz due dates, midterm/final windows, discussion deadlines, tech check\n- TRACKER_VISIBLE: Discussion post requirements, ongoing content watching\n- POLICY_NOTE: 7-day grace period, async nature, rolling content\n\n## ENGG400 Credit Model\n\n**Attendance requirement:**\n- Minimum 10 of 13 lectures\n- Recorded via weekly question submitted in class (genuine attempt required)\n- Records shared with Dean\'s Office and ENGG Advising\n- Regularly missing lectures triggers contact from teaching team/offices\n\n**Quiz requirements:**\n- 7 quizzes total\n- ≥50% on EACH quiz (per-quiz minimum)\n- ≥70% cumulative average across all 7\n- 2 attempts per quiz, higher score recorded\n- Open-resource (including AI), no declaration required\n\n**Attempt rules:**\n- Two attempts per quiz\n- Higher score recorded\n- No stated limit on when to retake\n\n**Passing thresholds:**\n- ALL three conditions required simultaneously:\n  1. Complete all 4 assignments (satisfactorily, with ≥70% on IDP)\n  2. Complete all 7 quizzes (≥50% each, ≥70% cumulative)\n  3. Attend ≥10 of 13 lectures\n- Failure of ANY = No Credit\n\n**Assignment requirements:**\n- All 4 must be satisfactorily completed\n- Assignment 2 (IDP) must be ≥70%\n- AI Use Declaration on each written assignment\n- Submission folder opens 2 weeks before deadline\n\n**Tracking design for final schedule:**\n- Attendance tracker: 13 checkmarks, need 10 green\n- Quiz tracker: 7 quizzes, each with ≥50% checkmark + cumulative average ≥70%\n- Assignment tracker: 4 assignments, all satisfactory + IDP ≥70%\n- All three trackers must show PASS for Credit\n\n## ECE490 Project-Process Model\n\n**Recurring project/lab work:**\n- Weekly Monday lecture (08:00-08:50)\n- Weekly Friday lab (14:00-16:50)\n- Ongoing team project work (no fixed schedule)\n- Lab notebook maintained continuously\n- Client/advisor/TA evaluations throughout\n\n**Training prerequisites:**\n- Safety training + solder training: Sep 14-18 window\n- Safety glasses selection form (Assignment 1 bundle)\n- Lab safety procedures expected at all times\n\n**Team/project administrative requirements:**\n- Group form submission: Sep 18\n- Project form submission: Oct 2\n- Team of unspecified size (syllabus says "teams")\n\n**CDR process:**\n- Assignment 5: CDR PowerPoint due Nov 16 (Noon)\n- CDR presentations: Nov 16-20 and Nov 23-27\n- Both group and individual assessment\n- Lab notebook evaluation by client, advisor, and TA\n\n**Ongoing vs dated milestones:**\n- Ongoing: team meetings, lab work, design process, documentation, lab notebook\n- Dated: 6 assignments with specific deadlines, 2 CDR presentation windows\n\n**Late policy:**\n- 20% deduction per day\n- Missed work = 0%\n- Group work: "expected that the rest of the group will make an effort to accommodate the delayed work"\n\n**Proposed tracker design:**\n- Milestone tracker: project phases (orientation → safety → design → CDR → report)\n- Assignment tracker: 6 assignments with deadlines\n- Team admin tracker: group form, project form\n- Lab notebook: ongoing checkbox\n- Weekly lecture attendance: 15 Mondays, attendance recorded\n\n## Recurring-Block Display Policy\n\n**10 recurring timetable blocks:**\n\n| # | Block | Schedule | Display Treatment |\n|---|-------|----------|------------------|\n| 1 | ECE302 LEC A2 | MWF 10:00-10:50 | Compact header; attach topics only where syllabus timeline suggests (approximate week blocks) |\n| 2 | ECE302 SEM E32 | WE 12:00-12:50 | Compact header; first session Sep 9 per syllabus |\n| 3 | ECE302 LAB D22 | TU 14:00-16:50 | Compact header; numbered labs listed only on explicit dates |\n| 4 | ECE449 LEC A1 | MWF 13:00-13:50 | Compact header; no lecture topics available |\n| 5 | ECE449 LAB D42 | TH 14:00-16:50 | Compact header; numbered labs listed only on explicit dates |\n| 6 | ECE485 LEC A1 | TU TH 11:00-12:20 | Compact header; no chapter-date mapping |\n| 7 | ECE485 LAB D11 | MO 14:00-16:50 | Compact header; numbered labs listed only on explicit dates |\n| 8 | ECE490 LEC A1 | MO 08:00-08:50 | Compact header; attach 6 labeled lecture topics only on those dates |\n| 9 | ECE490 LAB D51 | FR 14:00-16:50 | Compact header; numbered labs listed only on explicit dates |\n| 10 | ENGG400 LEC A1 | FR 12:00-12:50 | Full topic attached to each Friday entry (13 topics available) |\n\n**Recommended weekly schedule structure:**\n- Standing classes: compact one-line summary (e.g., "MWF 10:00 ECE302 LEC A2")\n- Each week\'s entry: list only the specific events/deadlines for that week\n- Do NOT list every ordinary lecture as a standalone event unless it has a meaningful dated topic\n- ENGG400 is the exception — attach exact topic to each Friday\n\n## Calendar / Tracker / Policy Classification\n\n| Item | Course | Classification | Reason |\n|------|--------|---------------|--------|\n| ECE302 LEC/SEM/LAB schedule | ECE302 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Standing timetable |\n| ECE302 problem sets | ECE302 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Recurring academic work, no dates |\n| ECE302 lab completion + 50% threshold | ECE302 | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE | Pass-critical condition |\n| ECE302 formula sheet (details TBD) | ECE302 | POLICY_NOTE | Important but details pending |\n| ECE449 lab + report deadlines | ECE449 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Exact dates known |\n| ECE449 late work = zero | ECE449 | POLICY_NOTE | Strict deadline enforcement |\n| ECE449 Lab 4 extended window | ECE449 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Reading week exception |\n| ECE485 quiz/exam dates | ECE485 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Exact dates known |\n| ECE485 best 5 of 6 quizzes | ECE485 | POLICY_NOTE | Scoring rule, mechanism unspecified |\n| ECE485 formula sheet for exams | ECE485 | POLICY_NOTE | Two-sided letter-size allowed |\n| ECE490 assignment deadlines | ECE490 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Exact dates known |\n| ECE490 CDR windows | ECE490 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Exact date ranges known |\n| ECE490 safety training prerequisite | ECE490 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Required before lab access |\n| ECE490 20%/day late penalty | ECE490 | POLICY_NOTE | Time-sensitive |\n| ECE490 lab notebook | ECE490 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Ongoing documentation |\n| ECE490 team admin forms | ECE490 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Group/project forms |\n| ENGG400 10/13 attendance | ENGG400 | TRACKER_VISIBLE + POLICY_NOTE | Pass-critical |\n| ENGG400 7 quizzes (50% each, 70% cumulative) | ENGG400 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Pass-critical |\n| ENGG400 4 assignments (all satisfactory) | ENGG400 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Pass-critical |\n| ENGG400 IDP ≥70% | ENGG400 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Specific threshold |\n| ENGG400 2 attempts per quiz | ENGG400 | POLICY_NOTE | Scoring rule |\n| ENGG400 AI declaration | ENGG400 | POLICY_NOTE | Administrative requirement |\n| SUST201 quiz due dates + 7-day grace | SUST201 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Nominal + actual deadlines |\n| SUST201 midterm/final windows | SUST201 | CALENDAR_VISIBLE | Exact availability windows |\n| SUST201 discussion post deadlines | SUST201 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Multi-phase participation |\n| SUST201 tech check | SUST201 | TRACKER_VISIBLE | Single deadline |\n| SUST201 async nature | SUST201 | POLICY_NOTE | No weekly structure |\n| ECE302 missed midterm policy | ECE302 | CONTINGENCY_ONLY | Deferral transfers weight |\n| ECE449 deferred final | ECE449 | CONTINGENCY_ONLY | Jan 9, 2027 only |\n| SUST201 exam integrity (oral exam) | SUST201 | CONTINGENCY_ONLY | Cheating investigation process |\n\n## Current Week Obligations (September 14–20, 2026)\n\n**Monday, Sep 14:**\n- ECE485 Lab 1 (14:00-16:50, ETLC E5-012) — TODAY\n- ECE490 Lab Safety Training + Solder Training (active window: Sep 14-18) — TODAY\n- ECE490 LEC A1 (08:00-08:50, ETLC E1-007) — Lecture 1: Orientation, Safety, Soldering\n- ECE302 LEC A2 (MWF 10:00-10:50)\n- ECE449 LEC A1 (MWF 13:00-13:50)\n- ECE485 LEC A1 (TU TH 11:00-12:20)\n- ECE490 LEC A1 (MO 08:00-08:50)\n\n**Tuesday, Sep 15:**\n- ECE485 Quiz 1 (20 min, open book) — TODAY\n- ECE302 SEM E32 (WE 12:00-12:50) — No class today (Wed only)\n- ECE302 LAB D22 (TU 14:00-16:50)\n\n**Wednesday, Sep 16:**\n- ECE302 SEM E32 (WE 12:00-12:50, ED 129) — TODAY\n- ECE302 LEC A2 (MWF 10:00-10:50)\n\n**Thursday, Sep 17:**\n- ECE449 LAB D42 (TH 14:00-16:50) — Lab 1: AI pipelines in Scikit-learn — TODAY\n- ECE449 LEC A1 (MWF 13:00-13:50)\n- ECE485 LEC A1 (TU TH 11:00-12:20)\n\n**Friday, Sep 18:**\n- ENGG400 LEC A1 (FR 12:00-12:50, CCIS 1-160) — Lecture 3: Ethics + Innovation in Industry — TODAY\n- ENGG400 Quiz 2 due — TODAY (Friday 9:00 AM)\n- SUST201 Reading/Content Quiz 1 due — TODAY\n- ECE490 Group Form Submission due — TODAY (Friday)\n- ECE302 LEC A2 (MWF 10:00-10:50)\n\n**Saturday, Sep 19:**\n- ENGG400 Quiz 3 open date (12:01 AM) — NOT due yet\n- SUST201: no obligations (async, quiz already due)\n\n**Sunday, Sep 20:**\n- No official obligations\n\n**Summary for current week:**\n- 3 actual labs (ECE485 Lab 1, ECE490 training window, ECE449 Lab 1)\n- 1 quiz (ECE485 Quiz 1)\n- 3 assignment/quiz deadlines (ENGG400 Quiz 2, SUST201 Quiz 1, ECE490 Group Form)\n- 3 lectures with topics (ECE490 Lecture 1, ENGG400 Lecture 3)\n- 4 recurring class sessions (ECE302 LEC, ECE302 SEM, ECE449 LEC, ECE485 LEC)\n\n## Unsupported Policy Inferences Rejected\n\n1. **ECE485 "best 5 of 6" means one quiz is automatically dropped** — The syllabus states the scoring rule but does NOT specify the mechanism (is the lowest dropped? is a missed quiz simply not counted? is there a makeup process?). The mechanism is unspecified.\n\n2. **Every lab has a pre-lab** — Only ECE302 mentions "preparatory work required prior to first lab period." This is stated for Lab 1 only, not generalized.\n\n3. **Every lecture requires attendance** — Only ENGG400 has a stated attendance requirement (10/13). ECE302 says "very important" but no minimum. Other courses have no stated attendance policy.\n\n4. **ECE449 lab titles are lecture topics** — Lab titles (e.g., "AI pipelines in Scikit-learn") are NOT explicitly linked to lecture content. The syllabus describes lecture topics broadly but does not map them to specific lab dates.\n\n5. **SUST201 has weekly module deadlines** — The course is fully asynchronous with rolling content. No weekly module structure exists. The 8 topics are high-level themes, not formal modules with release dates.\n\n6. **ECE490 project meetings occur weekly** — No stated meeting schedule. The syllabus mentions "project meetings" as part of ongoing assessment but does not specify frequency.\n\n7. **ECE302 problem sets have weekly due dates** — Problem sets are "given throughout the term" with no stated cadence or schedule.\n\n8. **ECE485 term exams cover specific chapters** — No chapter-to-exam mapping exists. The syllabus lists exam dates but not coverage.\n\n9. **SUST201 quiz 1 covers modules 1-2** — No module-to-quiz mapping exists. The syllabus says quizzes cover "readings and assigned content due since the last quiz" but does not name specific modules.\n\n10. **ECE449 group project has interim milestones** — Only the final group project date (Dec 8) is stated. No interim milestones are specified.\n\n11. **ECE490 Lab 2 (Sep 21 – Oct 2 window) has a specific due date** — The syllabus says "Lab 2: Soldering – Lab Assignment" with a date range of Sep 21 to Oct 2. This is a window, not a single date. The exact due date within the window is not specified.\n\n12. **ECE302 missed midterm = automatic makeup** — The syllabus says missed midterm gets a "waiver and the 15% raw marks tacked onto the final exam." This is NOT a makeup exam — the weight is transferred. This is a critical distinction.\n\n## Remaining Policy / Recurring-Obligation Uncertainties\n\n1. **ECE302 problem set schedule:** "Given throughout the term" — no cadence, no number, no due-day pattern. Unknown how many and when.\n\n2. **ECE302 formula sheet details:** "Details will be provided in lectures and on the web site prior to the exams." Length, format, and other constraints TBD.\n\n3. **ECE485 missed quiz mechanism:** "Best 5 of 6" — mechanism unspecified. Is the lowest score dropped? Is a missed quiz simply uncounted? Is there a formal make-up process?\n\n4. **ECE490 Lab 2 window end:** "Sep 21 to Oct 2" — is the due date Oct 2 (Friday) or is there flexibility within the window? The syllabus does not specify.\n\n5. **SUST201 quiz time limit:** Quizzes are separate from exams. No stated time limit for quizzes (unlike midterms which have 75 min). The 20-min exam-style time limit may not apply.\n\n6. **ECE449 group project team size:** "Three-person teams" is stated, but no team assignment list exists. Team formation date is not specified.\n\n7. **ECE490 team size:** The syllabus says "teams" but does not specify the number of members per team.\n\n## Modification Check\n\n**Zero repository files modified.** Step 6 was pure analysis and verification.\n\n---\n\nReady for your review. Awaiting approval to proceed to Step 7.'}
