rce-backed one-off event (quiz, lab, assignment, exam) | ECE485 Quiz 1 on 2026-09-15 |\n| [RECURRING] | Standing registered timetable block | ECE302 LEC A2 MWF 10:00 |\n| [TBA] | Official assessment, exact date not released | ECE302 Final Exam |\n| [CONTINGENCY] | Only applies under special circumstances | ECE449 deferred final |\n| [APPROXIMATE] | Syllabus-guided but not an exact class date | ECE302 topic timeline |\n| [RECOMMENDED] | Assistant-created planning suggestion | Review ECE485 Ch. 3 before Quiz 3 |\n| [PROGRESS] | Manual checkbox; not evidence of completion | [ ] Lab 1 completed |\n\n=== Status Tags ===\n\n| Tag | Meaning |\n|-----|---------|\n| PAST | Date has passed relative to reference date (2026-09-14). Does NOT mean complete. |\n| ACTIVE | Occurring during current week. |\n| UPCOMING | Future date. |\n| TBA | Date not yet released. |\n| CONTINGENT | Only applies if specific condition is met. |\n\n=== Checkbox Convention ===\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| [ ] | Incomplete / unknown. Never auto-marked. |\n| [x] | User-confirmed complete. |\n| — | Not applicable. |\n\n=== Semester Overview Schema ===\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| University | University of Alberta |\n| Term | Fall 2026 |\n| Classes begin | 2026-09-01 (Tue) |\n| Registered timetable ends | 2026-12-08 (Tue) |\n| University-wide last Fall class day | 2026-12-09 (Wed) |\n| General exam period | 2026-12-10 (Thu) – 2026-12-22 (Tue) |\n| Active courses | 6 |\n| Registered sections | 10 recurring blocks |\n\nNote: Two-layer model preserved — Dec 8 is the last day of scheduled meetings; Dec 9 is the university-wide academic term end marker.\n\n=== Registered Sections Schema ===\n\n| Course | Name | Lecture | Lab | Seminar/Mode |\n|--------|------|---------|-----|-------------|\n| ECE302 | Electronic Devices | A2 | D22 | E32 |\n| ECE449 | Intelligent Systems Engineering | A1 | D42 | — |\n| ECE485 | Digital Communications | A1 | D11 | — |\n| ECE490 | Electrical Engineering Design Project I | A1 | D51 | — |\n| ENGG400 | The Practice of the Engineering Profession | A1 | — | — |\n| SUST201 | Introduction to Sustainability | Async | — | Async |\n\nECE478 is excluded — not an active course.\n\n=== Weekly Timetable Schema ===\n\n| Course | Section | Type | Days | Time (MT) | Location | Effective Range | Notes |\n|--------|---------|------|------|-----------|----------|----------------|-------|\n| ECE302 | A2 | Lecture | Mon, Wed, Fri | 10:00–10:50 | CCIS L2-190 | Sep 1 – Dec 8 | — |\n| ECE302 | E32 | Seminar | Wed | 12:00–12:50 | ED 129 | Sep 2 – Dec 2 | — |\n| ECE302 | D22 | Lab | Tue | 14:00–16:50 | ETLC E4-001 | Sep 1 – Dec 1 | Registered block; numbered labs on official dates only |\n| ECE449 | A1 | Lecture | Mon, Wed, Fri | 13:00–13:50 | ETLC E2-001 | Sep 2 – Dec 8 | — |\n| ECE449 | D42 | Lab | Thu | 14:00–16:50 | ETLC E5-013 | Sep 17 – Nov 19 | Registered block; numbered labs on official dates only |\n| ECE485 | A1 | Lecture | Tue, Thu | 11:00–12:20 | ETLC E1-008 | Sep 1 – Dec 8 | — |\n| ECE485 | D11 | Lab | Mon | 14:00–16:50 | ETLC E5-012 | Sep 7 – Nov 30 | Registered block; numbered labs on official dates only |\n| ECE490 | A1 | Lecture | Mon | 08:00–08:50 | ETLC E1-007 | Sep 7 – Dec 8 | — |\n| ECE490 | D51 | Lab | Fri | 14:00–16:50 | ETLC E3-001 | Sep 4 – Dec 4 | — |\n| ENGG400 | A1 | Lecture | Fri | 12:00–12:50 | CCIS 1-160 | Sep 4 – Dec 4 | — |\n\nLab-block rule: For registered lab blocks (D22, D42, D11), the weekly timetable note explicitly states "numbered labs on official dates only." In the Master Weekly Calendar, numbered labs appear as special events on their official dates; empty reserved blocks do NOT appear in weekly calendar rows.\n\n=== University Calendar Schema ===\n\n| Date / Range | Event | Effect |\n|-------------|-------|--------|\n| 2026-09-01 (Tue) | Fall Term classes begin | TERM_START |\n| 2026-09-07 (Mon) | Labour Day | NO_CLASS — University closed |\n| 2026-09-30 (Wed) | National Day for Truth and Reconciliation | NO_CLASS — University closed |\n| 2026-10-12 (Mon) | Thanksgiving Day | NO_CLASS — University closed |\n| 2026-11-09 to 2026-11-13 | Fall Reading Week | NO_REGULAR_CLASSES — All 5 days |\n| 2026-11-11 (Wed) | Remembrance Day | UNIVERSITY_CLOSED — Nested within Reading Week |\n| 2026-12-08 (Tue) | Registered timetable end | Last scheduled meeting for all sections |\n| 2026-12-09 (Wed) | University-wide last Fall class day | TERM_END — No registered meetings scheduled |\n| 2026-12-10 to 2026-12-22 | Fall Term examinations | EXAM_PERIOD |\n\nNote: Remembrance Day (Wed Nov 11) falls within Reading Week (Mon Nov 9 – Fri Nov 13). It is listed separately for completeness but does not extend Reading Week.\n\n=== Master Weekly Calendar Design ===\n\nWeek numbering: Monday–Sunday blocks. Week 1 starts 2026-09-01 (Tuesday) as a partial week.\n\nWeek 1: 2026-09-01 (Tue) to 2026-09-06 (Sun) — Partial first week\nWeek 2: 2026-09-07 (Mon) to 2026-09-13 (Sun)\n...\nWeek 10: 2026-11-09 (Mon) to 2026-11-15 (Sun) — Reading Week\n...\nWeek 14: 2026-12-07 (Mon) to 2026-12-13 (Sun) — Last instructional week\nWeek 15: 2026-12-14 (Mon) to 2026-12-20 (Sun) — Final Exam Period Week 1\nWeek 16: 2026-12-21 (Mon) to 2026-12-27 (Sun) — Final Exam Period Week 2\n\nEach week template:\n\n```\n## Week N — YYYY-MM-DD to YYYY-MM-DD\n### Regular Schedule\n\n| Day | Time | Course | Section | Meeting |\n|-----|------|--------|---------|---------|\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\n### Special Events & Deadlines\n\n| Date | Time | Course | Event | Type | Notes |\n|------|------|--------|-------|------|-------|\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\n### Recommended Planning\n[Reserved for Step 12 — not populated in this version]\n```\n\nRecurrence handling:\n- ENGG400: Each Friday includes the exact dated topic.\n- ECE490: Only the 6 syllabus-labelled lectures include topics.\n- ECE302: No exact topic per meeting; approximate timeline in course tracker.\n- ECE449: No lecture topic mapping.\n- ECE485: No chapter/date mapping.\n\nHoliday/Reading Week handling:\n- If a week contains a holiday, note it in the week heading (e.g., "Week 2 — Sep 7 (Labour Day)").\n- Reading Week week heading: "Week 10 — Nov 9–13 (Fall Reading Week)".\n- Exam period weeks: "Final Exam Period — Week 1 — Dec 14–20".\n\nRecurring meetings only appear under "Regular Schedule" on days when they actually occur (i.e., holidays are excluded via the EXDATE model).\n\n=== Consolidated Assessment Tracker Schema ===\n\n| Status | Date | Time | Course | Assessment | Type | Weight | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|--------|-----------|------|--------|-------|\n| PAST | 2026-09-11 | 09:00 | ENGG400 | Quiz 1 Due | QUIZ | CR/F | Attempt 1 / Attempt 2 |\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\nTypes: QUIZ, READING_QUIZ, MIDTERM, TERM_EXAM, ASSIGNMENT, PROJECT, LAB_REPORT, FINAL, DISCUSSION, TECH_CHECK\nTimes: Exact when sourced (09:00, 11:00, 12:00, 12:00, 14:00, 16:00, 23:59), else UNSPECIFIED.\nWeights: Exact when sourced (2%, 15%, CR/F, etc.), else —.\nStatus: PAST / ACTIVE / UPCOMING / TBA.\nLabs: Only graded/due items appear here. Attendance-only lab meetings stay in the weekly calendar and course trackers.\n\n=== Course-Specific Architecture ===\n\n#### ECE302 — Electronic Devices\n\nSubsections:\n1. Timetable (LEC A2 / SEM E32 / LAB D22)\n2. Approximate Syllabus Topic Timeline — "APPROXIMATE SYLLABUS TIMELINE" label; no exact lecture dates. Schema: Approx Week(s) | Topic | Source Status\n3. Lab Tracker — Schema: Status | Date | Lab | Time | Notes (intro, Labs 1–5)\n4. Assessments — Midterm 1 (Oct 16), Midterm 2 (Nov 20), Final (TBA)\n5. Problem Set Tracker — "Problem sets assigned throughout term; dates not published in syllabus."\n6. Important Policies — pass condition, missed-midterm weight-transfer, exam formula/calculator rules\n\nMust NOT: assign exact lecture dates to chapters, invent problem set count/dates.\n\n#### ECE449 — Intelligent Systems Engineering\n\nSubsections:\n1. Lab and Report Tracker — Schema: Status | Lab | Lab Date | Topic | Report Due | Notes (Labs 1–5, Lab 4 extended period)\n2. Assessments — Midterm (Oct 19), Group Project (Dec 8), Final (TBA)\n3. Important Policies — late work = 0, calculator restriction, deferred final contingency\n\nMust NOT: create lecture-topic progression, attach chapters to dates.\n\n#### ECE485 — Digital Communications\n\nSubsections:\n1. Chapter Progress Tracker — Schema: Status | Chapter | Title | Notes (Chapters 1–7, no dates)\n2. Quiz Tracker — Schema: Status | Quiz | Date | Weight | Notes ("Best 5 of 6 count")\n3. Lab Tracker — Schema: Status | Lab | Date | Topic (Labs 1–5)\n4. Term Exam Tracker — Schema: Status | Exam | Date | Time | Weight (Term Exams 1–3)\n5. Important Policies — quizzes open book, term-exam formula sheet\n\nMust NOT: claim quiz/exam coverage beyond what syllabus states, invent missed-quiz mechanism.\n\n#### ECE490 — Electrical Engineering Design Project I\n\nSubsections:\n1. Project Milestone Timeline — Schema: Status | Date/Window | Milestone | Type | Notes (Assignments 1–6, training, CDR)\n2. Lecture/Training Progression — Schema: Date | Activity | Type (only syllabus-labelled items)\n3. Assignment Tracker — Schema: Status | Assignment | Due | Weight | Individual/Group | Notes\n4. Ongoing Responsibilities — lab notebook, team project, safety procedures\n\nMust NOT: invent weekly project meetings, assign dates to unscheduled training.\n\n#### ENGG400 — The Practice of the Engineering Profession\n\nSubsections:\n1. Lecture/Attendance Tracker — Schema: Attended? | Lecture | Date | Topic (13 rows, attendance user-entered)\n   - Summary: Attendance: X/13 (need 10/13)\n2. Quiz Credit Tracker — Schema: Quiz | Date | Attempt 1 | Attempt 2 | Best | ≥50%?\n   - Cumulative average: not entered (required ≥70%)\n3. Assignment Credit Tracker — Schema: Assignment | Due | Status | Requirement\n4. CR Checklist — [ ] Attendance ≥10/13, [ ] Each quiz ≥50%, [ ] Quiz cumulative ≥70%, [ ] All required assignments satisfactory, [ ] IDP threshold satisfied\n\nMust NOT: auto-mark attendance based on elapsed dates, mark quiz conditions satisfied without user data.\n\n#### SUST201 — Introduction to Sustainability\n\nSubsections:\n1. Assessment Timeline — Schema: Status | Assessment | Nominal Due/Window | Weight | Notes\n2. Quiz Tracker — Include nominal due dates + policy note (each open 7 additional days). Do NOT calculate exact final-access timestamps unless mechanically derived and clearly marked DERIVED.\n3. Discussion Tracker — Schema: Status | Requirement | Deadline | Notes (initial post + replies, final hard deadline)\n4. Content/Topic Reference — Schema: Status | Order | Topic (8 syllabus topics, no weekly dates)\n5. Technology/Exam Requirements — Respondus, tech check (Sep 29), exam windows (Dec 7–8)\n\nMust NOT: assign weekly pacing, invent discussion deadlines beyond syllabus.\n\n=== TBA / Contingency Architecture ===\n\nTBA section schema:\n\n| Course | Assessment | Weight | Expected Window | Status | Notes |\n|--------|-----------|--------|----------------|--------|-------|\n| ECE302 | Final Exam | 40% | Dec 10–22 | TBA | — |\n| ECE449 | Final Exam | 40% | Dec 10–22 | TBA | Syllabus says Dec 9–22; UAlberta official says Dec 10–22 |\n\nContingency section schema:\n\n| Course | Trigger | Contingency | Date / Effect |\n|--------|---------|-------------|--------------|\n| ECE302 | Missed midterm (approved) | Midterm weight transfers to final | Per syllabus |\n| ECE449 | Approved deferral | Final exam | Jan 9, 2027 |\n\nNormal TBA and contingency events stay separate — never mixed into weekly calendar.\n\n=== Recommended Planning Architecture ===\n\nSchema (Step 12 only — not populated in Step 9):\n\n| Date / Window | Course | Recommended Action | Reason | Related Official Event |\n|---------------|--------|-------------------|--------|----------------------|\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\nEvery row must visibly say [RECOMMENDED]. Never let a recommendation look like a syllabus deadline.\n\n=== Provenance / Source-Key Design ===\n\nConvention: Compact source labels in course trackers and consolidated assessment tracker. Weekly calendar kept clean with a Source Key at the end.\n\nSource Key:\n\n| Code | Source |\n|------|--------|\n| UALBERTA-CAL | UAlberta Official 2026-27 Academic Schedule |\n| UALBERTA-CAT | UAlberta Catalogue (registered sections) |\n| ECE302-SYL | MD/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/Syllabus.md |\n| ECE302-LAB | MD/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/ECE302 - f2026 - Lab Schedule.md |\n| ECE449-SYL | MD/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/Syllabus.md |\n| ECE449-LAB | MD/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/LabSchedule.md |\n| ECE485-SYL | MD/ECE485-Digital-Communications/Syllabus.md |\n| ECE490-SYL | MD/ECE490-Electrical-Engineering-Design-Project-I/Syllabus.md |\n| ENGG400-SYL | MD/ENGG400-The-Practice-of-the-Engineering-Profession/Syllabus.md |\n| SUST201-SYL | MD/SUST201-Introduction-to-Sustainability/Syllabus.md |\n| ICS | misc/FallCalender_Updated.ics (Bear Tracks-derived) |\n\nWhere provenance matters (assessment weights, policies), include the code in the Notes column.\n\n=== Status / Checkbox Rules ===\n\n- Status tags (PAST/ACTIVE/UPCOMING) appear in: Current Semester Status section and Consolidated Assessment Tracker only. NOT in weekly calendar rows.\n- Checkboxes [ ]/[x] used ONLY in: course progress trackers and ENGG400 CR checklist. NOT for official events.\n- PAST does NOT mean COMPLETE. Never auto-mark anything.\n- Reference date: 2026-09-14.\n\n=== Formatting Standards ===\n\n| Element | Convention |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Date | 2026-09-22 (Tue) |\n| Time | 24-hour (09:00, 14:00, 23:59, 12:00) |\n| Unknown time | UNSPECIFIED |\n| Weight | Exact when sourced (2%, CR/F); — when not |\n| Checkbox | [ ] incomplete, [x] user-confirmed, — not applicable |\n| Section tags | [OFFICIAL], [RECURRING], [TBA], [RECOMMENDED], [PROGRESS], [APPROXIMATE], [CONTINGENCY] |\n| Markdown | GFM tables, standard headings, no decorative emoji |\n\n=== Duplication Policy ===\n\nAn event may appear in multiple sections because each answers a different question:\n\n| Event | Where it appears | Why |\n|-------|-----------------|-----|\n| ECE485 Quiz 1 | Weekly Calendar (Week 2) | "What happens this week?" |\n| ECE485 Quiz 1 | Consolidated Assessment Tracker | "What is due next?" |\n| ECE485 Quiz 1 | ECE485 Quiz Tracker | "ECE485 quiz progress" |\n| ECE302 LEC A2 (MWF) | Weekly Timetable | "My standing schedule" |\n| ECE302 LEC A2 | Weekly Calendar (Regular Schedule) | "What meetings this week?" |\n| ENGG400 Lecture 1 topic | Weekly Calendar | Exact dated content |\n| ENGG400 Lecture 1 | ENGG400 Lecture Tracker | Attendance tracking |\n\nMeaningless duplication to avoid:\n- Never list every lecture in 3+ places with identical detail.\n- Never duplicate lab block and numbered lab as separate obligations for the same meeting.\n- Never repeat full policy text in every week.\n\n=== Expected Document Scale ===\n\n- ~16 week sections (15 instructional + exam period split into 2)\n- 1 consolidated assessment table (~80 rows)\n- 6 course tracker sections (~150 rows total across all trackers)\n- 1 university calendar table (~9 rows)\n- 1 weekly timetable table (10 rows)\n- Estimated total: ~300–400 table rows\n- Readability safeguards: collapsible course subsections via headings, clear section separators, grep-friendly tags, no excessive nesting\n\n=== Design Decisions Locked (Step 9 must follow exactly) ===\n\n1. Output path: /Users/anuragkoushik/Desktop/Fall26/semester_schedule.md\n2. Two-layer calendar: Dec 8 = registered section end, Dec 9 = university-wide last day\n3. Exam period: Dec 10–22 (UAlberta official). ECE449 syllabus "Dec 9–22" noted as discrepancy.\n4. Week numbering: Mon–Sun blocks. Week 1 = Sep 1–6 (partial). Exam period = Week 15–16.\n5. Date format: 2026-09-22 (Tue)\n6. Time format: 24-hour (09:00, 14:00, 23:59)\n7. Unknown time: UNSPECIFIED\n8. Status tags: PAST/ACTIVE/UPCOMING in Current Status + Assessment Tracker only\n9. Checkboxes: progress trackers + ENGG400 checklist only\n10. Lab blocks: numbered labs appear as special events; empty reserved blocks do NOT appear in weekly calendar\n11. Source codes: compact labels in tracker notes, Source Key at end\n12. Legend tags: [OFFICIAL], [RECURRING], [TBA], [RECOMMENDED], [PROGRESS], [APPROXIMATE], [CONTINGENCY]\n13. ECE478 excluded from all sections\n14. Recommended Planning section: schema defined, data generated in Step 12 only\n15. PAST ≠ COMPLETE — never auto-mark\n\n=== Remaining Design Questions ===\n\nNONE.\n\n=== Modification Check ===\n\nCONFIRMED: Zero repository files modified during Step 8. This is a design-only step.', 'timeout': 1800000}
