.count("\\n")` = 1618, `len(splitlines())` = 1618, ends with newline = True. The previous report said "Before = 1427, After = 1618" with a difference of 191 but described "+190 lines" — this was a minor off-by-one in the report narrative, not in the actual file.\n\n10. **Git status**: All untracked (never committed): `semester_schedule.md`, `data/`, and a few new MD/PDF files.\n\n11. **ECE478 contamination**: 0 references. ✓\n\n12. **Active courses count**: Already correctly shows 6 in the overview table.\n\n### What I Changed\n\n**File**: `semester_schedule.md`\n\n**Change**: Corrected the Assessment Summary by Type table (lines 1007–1008):\n- `| Assignments | 10 |` → `| Assignments | 12 |`\n- `| Projects / CDR / Forms / Training | 6 |` → `| Projects / CDR / Forms / Training | 4 |`\n\n### Why I Changed It\n\nThe previous Step 13 summary table had a **double error**:\n1. The summary counts (Assignments=10, Projects=6) didn\'t match the actual primary tracker row counts (Assignments=12, Projects=4).\n2. The previous report\'s category summary summed to 66 instead of 67 — the SUST201 FINAL event was apparently double-counted or misclassified somewhere in the original derivation.\n\nThe fix derives category counts directly from the canonical JSON\'s event_type field, which is the authoritative source. The mapping is:\n- ASSIGNMENT type → Assignments category (12 events)\n- PROJECT + TRAINING types → Projects/CDR/Forms/Training category (4 events)\n\nThis gives a consistent partition: 18+8+16+5+12+4+4 = 67.\n\n### Exact Validation Results\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| Primary IDs | 67 ✓ |\n| Classified IDs | 67 ✓ |\n| Unique classified IDs | 67 ✓ |\n| Unclassified IDs | 0 ✓ |\n| Category-count sum | 67 ✓ |\n| Quizzes | 18 ✓ |\n| Midterms/Term Exams | 8 ✓ |\n| Labs/Lab Activities | 16 ✓ |\n| Lab Reports | 5 ✓ |\n| Assignments | 12 ✓ (corrected from 10) |\n| Projects/CDR/Forms/Training | 4 ✓ (corrected from 6) |\n| Discussions/Tech/Final | 4 ✓ |\n| Chronolo