19:27:13 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'PROBLEM REPORT — Phase 8: TCP 2222 unreachable from Mac despite firewall rules\n\nSetup:\n- Mac (Tailscale IP 100.103.27.77) → Windows server (Tailscale IP 100.103.27.77, LAN IP 192.168.0.231)\n- Debian WSL2 running on Windows, sshd listening on TCP 2222 (confirmed via ss -lntp)\n- Windows OpenSSH on TCP 22 unchanged\n\nWhat I\'ve done:\n1. Created Hyper-V firewall rule "WSL-SSH-2222" with VMCreatorId {40E0AC32-46A5-438A-A0B2-2B479E8F2E90}, TCP, port 2222, RemoteAddresses: Any\n2. Pre-existing rule "Debian SSH 2222" has RemoteAddresses restricted to {192.168.0.0/24, 100.64.0.0/24} — Mac\'s Tailscale IP 100.103.27.77 is NOT in this range\n3. Windows native firewall only has one inbound rule for 2222: "Debian SSH 2222" (Allow)\n4. No blocking rules found\n5. Created UDP rule "WSL-Mosh-UDP-60000-60010"\n\nWhat\'s not working:\n- nc -vz 192.168.0.231 2222 — TIMEOUT\n- nc -vz server 2222 — TIMEOUT\n- nc -vz 100.103.27.77 2222 — TIMEOUT\n- Test-NetConnection from Windows localhost 127.0.0.1:2222 — TcpTestSucceeded: False\n- Test-NetConnection from Windows 192.168.0.231:2222 — TcpTestSucceeded: False\n\nBut inside Debian:\n- ss -lntp shows sshd LISTEN on 0.0.0.0:2222 and [::]:2222\n\nThe old "Debian SSH 2222" Hyper-V rule has RemoteAddresses restricted, and I tried to widen it but got "Access is denied" (requires admin). I created a new rule "WSL-SSH-2222" with RemoteAddresses: Any but it still doesn\'t work.\n\nKey observation: Test-NetConnection from Windows localhost to 127.0.0.1:2222 also fails. This means even Windows-to-WSL traffic on 2222 is blocked.\n\nWhat could be the issue? Is the Hyper-V firewall rule not matching the WSL VM? Is there a Windows Firewall rule blocking it? Do I need to use a different VMCreatorId or ResourcePoolName?', 'timeout': 1800000}
