11:43:08 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I\'m building an award-level portfolio website for an electrical engineer. I have a detailed creative/implementation plan. I need you to guide me step by step through the implementation. After each step I complete, I will report back with exactly what I did, and you will verify and give me the next step.\n\nHere is the full plan:\n\n--- START OF PLAN ---\n\n# Electrical Engineer Portfolio — Implementation Plan\n\n## 1. Project Goal\n\nBuild an outstanding, award-level portfolio website for an electrical engineer.\n\nThe site must feel like an **interactive electrical system**, not a conventional student portfolio.\n\nThe visual language should come directly from the engineering work: embedded systems, microcontrollers, FPGA/VHDL, digital logic, ADC/UART, sensors, PCB/hardware, power engineering, electrical machines, control systems, low-level ARM programming, system architecture, networking between embedded devices, real-time data and instrumentation.\n\nPrimary design principle: Every major visual interaction should represent an engineering concept.\n\n## 2. Creative Direction\n\nWorking concept name: **SIGNAL**\n\nThe experience behaves like a powered system. A signal moves through the website as the user scrolls.\n\nConceptual flow: INPUT → ENGINEER → EMBEDDED ──── FPGA → PCB ──── POWER → CONTROL → PROJECTS → OUTPUT\n\n## 3. Design Personality\n\nPrecise, technical, cinematic, premium, experimental, highly interactive, disciplined, modern. Avoid: generic dark portfolio templates, random neon gradients, excessive glassmorphism, fake terminal aesthetics, Matrix-style effects, floating particles with no meaning, excessive 3D, animations only for decoration, crowded dashboards, generic skill bars, generic project-card grids.\n\n## 4. Visual Language\n\nBase Palette: Carbon Black #080A0A, PCB Black #111414, Instrument White #E9ECE6, Muted Grey #8B9290, Deep Grey #1A1E1D\n\nSignal colors: Signal Green #B6FF4A (active/success), Logic Cyan #6EDCFF (digital/FPGA), Power Amber #FFB547 (power/machines), Fault Red #FF604A (alarm/fault)\n\n## 5. Typography\n\nDisplay Typeface: large, modern, geometric/grotesk for hero statements and section titles.\nMonospace Typeface: for component labels, signal readouts, code, technical metadata.\n\n## 6. Motion Philosophy\n\nUse Framer Motion as core. Required primitives: useScroll, useTransform, useMotionValue, useSpring, useInView, AnimatePresence, layoutId, motion.path, MotionConfig. GSAP only for highly coordinated sequences.\n\n## 7. Global Signal System\n\nPersistent visual signal running through the homepage: begins in hero, moves through SVG traces, activates project-domain nodes, branches into featured projects, powers diagrams, disappears into contact section. SVG path with scroll-linked pathLength, normalized homepage scroll progress, section-specific activation thresholds.\n\n## 8. Site Architecture\n\nRoutes: /, /projects, /projects/[slug], /about, /contact\n\n## 9. Homepage Sections\n\n00 — Boot/Hero: Full-screen, boot sequence "01 // INITIALIZING SYSTEM", then name reveal, CTA "EXPLORE SYSTEM ↓"\n01 — Engineer Profile: Who the engineer is, short bio\n02 — Engineering System Map: Interactive node graph replacing skills grid\n03 — Flagship Project: Home Security Embedded System, 6 progressive scroll scenes\n04 — Selected Work: Each project has unique preview interaction\n05 — Contact: "OPEN CIRCUIT? LET\'S CONNECT."\n\n## 10. Project Previews\n\n- Ultrasonic Tape Measure: Simulates HC-SR04 sensor with outgoing/reflected pulses\n- Joystick ADC + UART: Interactive joystick showing live ADC values and UART output\n- FPGA/Digital Logic: Timing diagrams, truth tables, VHDL\n- ARM Low-Level: Debugger interface with registers, memory, assembly\n- Power Engineering: Waveforms → phasor diagram → power triangle\n\n## 11. Tech Stack\n\nNext.js, React, TypeScript, Framer Motion, MDX, CSS Variables, SVG, Vercel\n\n## 12. Implementation Phases\n\nPhase 01 — Foundation: Next.js app, TypeScript, typography, color variables, layout, navigation, responsive container, Framer Motion config, reduced-motion handling\nPhase 02 — Hero: Boot sequence, hero typography, signal trace, engineering grid\nPhase 03 — Global Signal System: Reusable SVG signal component, scroll progress mapping\nPhase 04 — System Map: Domain nodes, traces, hover states\nPhase 05 — Flagship Project: Home Security architecture sequence\nPhase 06 — Selected Project Interactions: Ultrasonic, joystick, FPGA, ARM, power demos\nPhase 07 — Project Pages: Case study template\nPhase 08 — About/Resume/Contact\nPhase 09 — Mobile Pass\nPhase 10 — Performance Pass\nPhase 11 — Accessibility Pass\nPhase 12 — Final Polish\n\n## 13. Key Requirements\n\n- No decorative animations — every animation communicates something\n- Fully accessible (semantic HTML, keyboard nav, reduced-motion, contrast)\n- Performance: LCP < 2.5s, Lighthouse 90+\n- Mobile: transform diagrams to vertical flows, no custom cursor\n- Content: engineering decisions, system architecture, constraints, verification, results\n- Copy style: concise, technical, active, specific. No vague claims.\n\n## 14. Definition of Done\n\nHomepage has coherent system narrative, signal system connects entire page, hero is distinctive, flagship project immersive, 4+ project previews with unique engineering interactions, project pages show actual engineering process, works on mobile, reduced-motion works, Lighthouse strong, no placeholder imagery, no generic card grids.\n\n--- END OF PLAN ---\n\nHere\'s what I need from you:\n\n1. First, look at the current state of the project directory at /Users/anuragkoushik/Desktop/Proj/portfolio/ - check if anything exists there already.\n\n2. Then, give me the **very first step** of implementation. I want you to break this down into small, sequential, verifiable steps. Give me ONLY the first step right now. I will implement it, report back with exactly what I did (including file contents or changes), and then you will verify and give me the next step.\n\nDo NOT give me all steps at once. I want one step at a time so we can verify each one.', 'timeout': 1800000}
