n tokens, reset, typography)\n  components/\n    layout/\n      Container.tsx\n      Header.tsx\n      MobileNavigation.tsx\n```\n\n## Tech Stack\n- Next.js 16.3.5 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.8\n- TypeScript 5.9.3\n- ESLint 9.39.5\n- No Tailwind, no clsx, no classnames, no CVA — plain string concatenation for className\n- next/font/google for fonts\n- Import alias: @/* → ./src/*\n\n## The Plan (plan.md)\nThe plan specifies Framer Motion as the core animation library. Required primitives: useScroll, useTransform, useMotionValue, useSpring, useInView, AnimatePresence, layoutId, motion.path, MotionConfig. Must respect prefers-reduced-motion.\n\nThe plan\'s Phase 01 implementation phases show:\n- Step 4: Framer Motion configuration (MotionProvider, reduced-motion handling)\n- Step 5: Hero (boot sequence, signal trace, engineering grid)\n- Step 6: Global Signal System\n- Step 7: System Map\n- Step 8: Flagship Project\n- ...and so on\n\n## What I Need\n\nBased on the plan and what\'s done, what should the next concrete step be? Should I:\n1. Build Framer Motion infrastructure (MotionProvider, useReducedMotionSafe, custom hooks)?\n2. Jump straight to the Hero section (Step 5)?\n3. Something else?\n\nGive me specific, actionable instructions for the next step only. Don\'t plan ahead — just tell me what to do right now and how to do it.', 'timeout': 300000}
