16:37:33 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Here\'s a complete summary of what has been done on this portfolio project so far. Please read it and let me know what the next steps should be.\n\n---\n\n## Project: Electrical Engineer Portfolio — "SIGNAL"\n\nA custom, award-level portfolio website for electrical engineer Anurag Koushik. The visual language comes directly from engineering: embedded systems, FPGA, PCB, power engineering, control systems, etc. Every major visual interaction represents an engineering concept.\n\n**Plan file**: `plan.md` — 2072 lines, detailed creative direction, visual language, motion philosophy, site architecture, and 12 implementation phases.\n\n---\n\n## What Has Been Built (Milestones Complete)\n\n### Milestone 1 — Next.js Foundation Scaffold\n- Clean Next.js 16.3.5 App Router with TypeScript, ESLint, src/ directory\n- No Tailwind, no UI libraries\n- Package name: "portfolio"\n- Git initialized on main branch\n- All verification passed (lint, build, audit)\n\n### Milestone 1A — Foundation Reconciliation\n- Fixed package name from "portfolio-scaffold-temp" → "portfolio"\n- Verified plan.md byte-for-byte preserved (SHA-256 match)\n- Clean working tree\n\n### Milestone 2 — Visual Foundation\n- **Typography**: Bricolage Grotesque (display, body) + IBM Plex Mono (labels, metadata, instrumentation)\n- **Color system**: Full engineering palette as CSS custom properties\n  - Carbon Black #080a0a, PCB Black #111414, Instrument White #e9ece6, Muted Grey #8b9290, Deep Grey #1a1e1d\n  - Signal Green #b6ff4a, Logic Cyan #6edcff, Power Amber #ffb547, Fault Red #ff604a\n- **Global reset**: box-sizing, form controls, focus-visible (signal-green outline), selection styling\n- **Container component**: `src/components/layout/Container.tsx` with responsive gutters (clamp 1rem to 3rem)\n- **globals.css**: `src/app/globals.css` with all design tokens\n\n### Milestone 3 — Site Shell and Navigation\n- **Header** (`src/components/layout/Header.tsx`): Server component with sticky nav, brand [AK], links: PROJECTS, SYSTEMS, ABOUT, CONTACT\n- **Availability indicator**: ● AVAILABLE with signal-green dot\n- **Mobile navigation** (`src/components/layout/MobileNavigation.tsx`): Client component with useState, Escape key handler, aria-expanded, accessible labels\n- **Breakpoint**: 768px\n- **Route skeletons**: /projects, /about, /contact all have Container-wrapped placeholder pages\n- **Accessibility**: Semantic header/nav, keyboard navigation, focus-visible inherited\n\n### Milestone 4 — Framer Motion Foundation\n- **Framer Motion** installed\n- **MotionProvider** (`src/components/motion/MotionProvider.tsx`): Wraps app in MotionConfig, reads reduced-motion preference, exposes via React context\n  - Normal: spring { type: "spring", damping: 25, stiffness: 200 }\n  - Reduced motion: { duration: 0, ease: "linear" }\n- **Custom hooks created**:\n  - `useReducedMotionSafe` — prefers-reduced-motion OR pointer: coarse\n  - `useDeviceCapability` — { isTouch, isReducedMotion, pointerType }\n  - `usePointerPosition` — mouse position as MotionValues\n  - `useScrollProgress` — page scroll progress 0→1\n  - `useSectionProgress` — section-specific scroll progress\n- All verified: lint, build, HTTP routes all 200\n\n---\n\n## Current Git State\n- Branch: main\n- Latest commit: `ba0f1c4 feat: add motion foundation`\n- Working tree: clean\n\n## Remaining Work (per plan phases)\n- **Phase 02**: Hero (boot sequence, signal trace, engineering grid)\n- **Phase 03**: Global Signal System (SVG signal component, scroll progress mapping)\n- **Phase 04**: System Map (domain nodes, traces, hover states)\n- **Phase 05**: Flagship Project (Home Security architecture sequence)\n- **Phase 06**: Selected Project Interactions (ultrasonic demo, joystick ADC, FPGA timing, ARM debugger, power waveform)\n- **Phase 07**: Project Pages (case study template with MDX)\n- **Phase 08**: About / Resume / Contact (full pages)\n- **Phase 09**: Mobile Pass\n- **Phase 10**: Performance Pass\n- **Phase 11**: Accessibility Pass\n- **Phase 12**: Final Polish\n\n---\n\nPlease review this and advise on what to do next.'}
