20:42:01 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': "I'm building an electrical engineer portfolio in Next.js with Framer Motion. I've completed Steps 1-5 and now need to build Step 6.\n\n## Current State\n- Next.js 16.3.5, React 19, TypeScript, Framer Motion installed\n- Design system: Carbon Black #080A0A background, Signal Green #B6FF4A, Logic Cyan #6EDCFF, Power Amber #FFB547\n- Fonts: Bricolage Grotesque (display) + IBM Plex Mono (monospace)\n- Routes: /, /projects, /about, /contact\n- Header with sticky nav and mobile menu already built\n- Hero section with boot sequence animation and SVG signal trace\n\n## Current File Structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── app/\n│   ├── layout.tsx\n│   ├── page.tsx          (renders <Hero />)\n│   └── globals.css\n├── components/\n│   ├── layout/\n│   │   ├── Header.tsx\n│   │   ├── MobileNavigation.tsx\n│   │   └── Container.tsx\n│   ├── motion/\n│   │   └── MotionProvider.tsx\n│   └── home/\n│       ├── Hero.tsx\n│       ├── HeroSignal.tsx\n│       ├── HeroBootSequence.tsx\n│       └── Hero.module.css\n├── hooks/\n│   ├── useReducedMotionSafe.ts\n│   ├── useDeviceCapability.ts\n│   ├── usePointerPosition.ts\n│   ├── useScrollProgress.ts\n│   └── useSectionProgress.ts\n```\n\n## Step 6: Global Signal System\n\nPer the plan, I need to create a persistent visual signal running through the homepage that:\n1. Begins in the hero\n2. Moves through SVG traces\n3. Activates project-domain nodes\n4. Branches into featured projects\n5. Powers diagrams and measurements\n6. Disappears into the final contact section\n\nConcept from the plan:\n```\n──────●──────────────●──────────────●──────\n      MCU            FPGA           POWER\n```\n\nImplementation approach from the plan:\n- SVG path\n- Scroll-linked pathLength\n- Normalized homepage scroll progress\n- Section-specific activation thresholds\n- Reduced-motion fallback\n\n## Instructions for You\n\n**Please keep things SIMPLE.** Don't over-engineer this. I want:\n\n1. A single reusable SVG signal component that draws a path as the user scrolls\n2. Small nodes (circles) along the path that illuminate as the signal reaches them\n3. A small pulse that travels along the path\n4. It should work with the existing useScrollProgress hook\n5. It should respect reduced-motion\n6. Place it on the homepage between the Hero and wherever the first real content section will go\n\n**Please do NOT:**\n- Create multiple components when one will do\n- Add new dependencies\n- Create complex state management\n- Build 3D or Canvas elements\n- Over-think the path geometry\n\nJust give me clear, simple, step-by-step instructions. After each step, I'll report back for approval before proceeding.\n\nWhat should I build first, and how?", 'timeout': 600000}
