20:53:59 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Step 6A complete. Here\'s the report:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Files Changed\n**New:**\n- `src/components/motion/SignalPath.tsx` — Reusable SVG signal component (73 lines)\n\n**Modified:**\n- `src/app/globals.css` — Added signal section/container/svg/path base/active styles\n- `src/app/page.tsx` — Mounted `<SignalPath>` below `<Hero />` in a `100vh` test section with `id="systems"`\n- `src/hooks/useReducedMotionSafe.ts` — Removed coarse pointer check (bug fix)\n- `src/hooks/useDeviceCapability.ts` — Added independent `getCoarsePointer()` (bug fix)\n\n### What SignalPath Does\n1. Accepts a `path` (SVG path string) and `nodes` (array of {x, y, at})\n2. Uses `useScroll({ target: sectionRef })` for section-scoped scroll tracking\n3. Maps scroll progress through `useTransform([0.05, 0.55], [0, 1])` to drive signal\n4. Renders two SVG paths: faint base trace + active trace with animated `pathLength`\n5. Renders `SignalNodeCircle` sub-components — each uses `useTransform` to animate opacity (0.15→1) and scale (0.6→1) as signal reaches their `at` threshold\n6. Respects reduced motion via existing MotionProvider context (everything shows fully visible)\n\n### Bug Fix\n`useReducedMotionSafe()` previously treated `pointer: coarse` as reduced motion. This meant all phone/tablet users got reduced motion automatically. Fixed: now only checks `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. `useDeviceCapability()` handles coarse pointer detection independently.\n\n### Node Component Pattern\nEach node is a `SignalNodeCircle` sub-component. This avoids ESLint\'s "hooks inside callback" false positive while keeping hooks at the top level of each sub-component. Each receives `signalProgress` MotionValue as a prop.\n\n### Verification Results\n- Lint: PASS (0 errors, 0 warnings)\n- Build: PASS (6 static pages)\n- plan.md: SHA-256 match confirmed\n- No new dependencies\n- No decorative effects (no gradients, backdrop-filter, box-shadow, @keyframes)\n- No Canvas/Three.js/WebGL\n- Only transform/opacity/SVG path properties animated\n\n### Commit\n`42978d8` — feat: add global signal system\n\n### Browser Verification Pending (manual)\n- Trace starts unpowered, draws on scroll, reverses on scroll-back\n- Nodes activate in sequence\n- Reduced-motion shows completed trace immediately\n- Coarse pointer does NOT trigger reduced motion\n- No console errors, resize-safe\n\n### Handoff\n`docs/handoffs/06-global-signal-system.md` written.\n\n## Questions for You\n1. Does this implementation meet your approval?\n2. Can I proceed to the next step (Step 7 — System Map)?\n3. Are there any changes you want me to make before moving forward?', 'timeout': 600000}
