13:30:00 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Please review Milestone 14C final Engineering Network composition fix.\n\n## Root Cause Identified\nThe signal trace was a separate `<div>` with margin (2rem), sitting between the heading and the network SVG. This created excessive vertical separation — the section read as disconnected elements (heading → empty space with signal → network) rather than one cohesive composition.\n\n## Fix Applied (Commit a32e0ce)\n1. **Integrated signal trace into the network SVG**: The signal path and its 3 nodes are now rendered directly inside the SVG canvas, sharing the same coordinate space as the connections and domain nodes.\n2. **Removed SignalPath component**: No longer needed — the signal is part of the network SVG.\n3. **Reduced section spacing**:\n   - Section padding: 3rem → 2rem\n   - Header margin-bottom: 1.5rem → 1rem\n   - Network bottom margin: 2rem → 1.5rem\n   - Node container min-height: 560px → 500px\n\n## Git Status\n- Working tree: clean\n- Handoff: docs/handoffs/14a-critical-visual-repair.md\n- All 14C commits:\n  - 4603359 Milestone 14C initial (8 files)\n  - 41eb703 Engineering Network refinement (2 files)\n  - cddcb01 Hydration + scroll activation (3 files)\n  - a32e0ce Signal trace integration (3 files)\n\n## Verification\n- Lint: PASS (0 errors, 0 warnings)\n- Build: PASS (11 pages)\n- Routes: All 200\n\n## Please Review\n1. Is the Engineering Network composition fix (integrating signal into SVG) the right approach?\n2. Can we now request visual verification from the user?\n3. Is Step 15 unblocked once visual verification passes?\n\nThe implementation corrections are complete. We need visual confirmation that the network now reads as one cohesive composition with visible connections.'}
