16:25:01 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'MILESTONE 1 — ENGINEERING NETWORK FIX — REPORT FOR REVIEW\n\nI have completed the Engineering Network fixes. Here are the results:\n\nCRITICAL BUG FOUND: The connection lines were completely invisible due to a CSS syntax error. The code used `color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text-muted) 55% 0%)` — the `0%` is NOT a valid CSS color value. The browser discards the entire stroke declaration. This bug existed since the 14C milestone. Same bug affected hover/active glow effects.\n\nCHANGES MADE:\n\n1. Fixed CSS color-mix bug: replaced `0%` with `transparent` on all color-mix calls (connection lines, hover glow, active glow)\n2. Increased domain node font-size from 11px to 12px, weight from 500 to 600\n3. Added box-shadow to nodes for surface separation from dark background\n4. Increased dimmed node opacity from 25% to 40%, non-active from 60% to 70%\n5. Added a subtle connector line (1.5px, 40% opacity) from the signal trace node at (400, 100) to the FPGA node at (400, 70)\n6. Made active connections thicker (strokeWidth 2.5)\n7. Improved detail panel: larger labels (0.9375rem), stronger project items (0.8125rem, weight 500), signal-colored arrow markers\n8. Improved section meta text visibility\n\nFILES MODIFIED:\n- src/components/home/SystemMap.module.css\n- src/components/home/SystemMap.tsx\n\nCOMMIT: 20ecf99\n\nBUILD: PASS (TypeScript + static generation)\n\nREGRESSION CHECK: No logic changes — only visual improvements. No previously working features broken.\n\nHANDOFF DOC: docs/handoffs/15a-engineering-network-visual-repair.md\n\nPlease review and let me know:\n1. Are these fixes sufficient for the Engineering Network?\n2. Can I proceed to Milestone 2 — the Home Security architecture?', 'timeout': 1800000}
