16:47:15 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'MILESTONE 1 — ENGINEERING NETWORK VISUAL REPAIR — FULL REPORT\n\nOBJECTIVE: Fix invisible connection lines and weak node visibility in the Engineering Network section.\n\nACTIONS: Inspected the rendered SVG, tested node selection, verified mobile layout, ran build and lint.\n\nROOT CAUSE — TWO BUGS FOUND:\n\nBug 1 (CSS): color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text-muted) 55% 0%) — the `0%` is invalid CSS. Browsers discard the stroke. \nFix: Replaced `0%` with `transparent`.\n\nBug 2 (CRITICAL — primary cause): The connections array uses domain LABELS ("Embedded", "Sensors") but getDomainById() looked up by domain ID ("embedded", "sensors") — case-sensitive mismatch. Every lookup returned undefined, so getConnectedIds() and isActiveConnection() always returned empty/false. The 10 SVG connection <line> elements were NEVER rendered.\n\nFix: Added getDomainByLabel() and replaced all label-based lookups.\n\nEVIDENCE:\n- Before fix: SVG had 1 line (the signal connector I added). Zero domain connections.\n- After fix: SVG has 11 lines (1 connector + 10 domain connections).\n- CSS computed values: color-mix(in srgb, #8b9290 55% transparent) correctly applied to connection lines.\n- Screenshot 1 (default): All 8 nodes visible, 10 connection lines rendered.\n- Screenshot 2 (FPGA selected): 3 green connections highlighted (FPGA↔Digital Logic, FPGA↔PCB/Hardware, signal→FPGA).\n- Screenshot 3 (Embedded selected): 4 green connections highlighted (Embedded↔Sensors, Embedded↔Low-Level Software, Embedded↔Digital Logic, Embedded↔PCB/Hardware).\n- Screenshot 4 (mobile 375px): Vertical flow layout renders correctly.\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Browser viewport: 1280x900 (desktop), 375x812 (mobile)\n- SVG dimensions: 800x620 (matches viewBox)\n- All 8 domain buttons rendered and clickable\n- Node selection highlights correct connections\n- Detail panel updates on node selection\n- Build: PASS (TypeScript + static generation)\n- Lint: PASS (no errors)\n\nREGRESSION CHECKS:\n- Node selection state: PASS\n- Detail panel: PASS\n- Mobile vertical flow: PASS\n- No previously working features broken\n\nOUTCOME: PASS\n\nGIT:\n- Commit 1: 20ecf99 — CSS color-mix fix, node visibility improvements\n- Commit 2: 6b1dc77 — Label/ID mismatch fix (primary cause)\n- Handoff: docs/handoffs/15a-engineering-network-visual-repair.md\n\nREMAINING WORK:\n- Section header title rendering (depends on parent page)\n- Mobile flow connector contrast (deep-grey on pcb-black)\n- Section width (800px max-width is narrow for desktop)\n\nPlease review the screenshots and confirm if Milestone 1 is APPROVED. If approved, can I proceed to Milestone 2 (Home Security architecture)?', 'timeout': 1800000}
