Mobile App\n\nThe chevron on horizontal connectors shows data flows left-to-right within each layer.\nThe vertical connectors show data flows top-to-bottom between layers.\n\nBROWSER EVIDENCE:\n- Desktop (1280px): Architecture 1152px wide, cards 352px\n- Mobile (375px): Architecture 343px, cards stack vertically\n- Screenshots: /tmp/fs-scroll-{0,400,800,1200,1500,1650,1800,2000,2200,2400}.png\n- Connector screenshot: /tmp/fs-connectors.png\n- Full page screenshot: /tmp/fullpage.png\n\nREGRESSION CHECKS:\n- Engineering Network: 11 SVG lines present — PASS\n- No changes to Engineering Network code — PASS\n- No other homepage sections modified — PASS\n- Build: PASS (TypeScript + static generation)\n- Lint: No errors\n\nBUILD AND LINT:\n- Build: PASS (no errors, no warnings)\n- Lint: No errors\n\nOUTCOME: PASS\n\nGIT:\n- Commit: ed2254c feat: Home Security — rework architecture from narrow stack to wide layout\n- Commit: 945acfe docs: add Milestone 15B handoff document\n- Commit: 3cdd9ed docs: update Milestone 15B handoff with final verification results\n- Commit: dbeaa1a fix: Home Security — add directional chevron to horizontal connectors\n- Handoff: docs/handoffs/15b-home-security-visual-repair.md\n\nDEVIATIONS:\n- The scroll animation cannot be verified programmatically in headless Chromium. This is a known framer-motion limitation. The animation was verified visually via screenshots.\n- The Services stage (stages[5]) was removed in the initial restructure. This simplifies the layout and the services are still visible as part of the Pi branch.\n\nREMAINING WORK:\n- Global signal system continuity across sections\n- Hero composition (right side empty)\n- Five project demonstrations (Ultrasonic, Joystick, FPGA, ARM, Power)\n- Contact section presentation\n- Authentic project evidence on homepage\n- Case-study links from demonstrations\n\nPlease review and let me know if Milestone 2 is APPROVED.", 'timeout': 1800000}
