18:51:39 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': '## MILESTONE 15D: Critical Responsive and SVG Repairs\n\n## OBJECTIVE\nResolve confirmed mobile rendering defects and investigate the homepage SVG console error without redesigning the website or disturbing previously verified desktop functionality.\n\n## STARTING STATE\nConfirmed defects from Milestone 15C audit:\n- **P0**: Mobile Engineering Network overlapping domain nodes (8 nodes compressed into overlapping positions)\n- **P0**: Mobile architecture text clipping across all 5 case-study pages (long horizontal strings in `<pre>` containers extending beyond viewport)\n- **P0**: Homepage SVG console error `<circle> attribute cx: Expected length, "undefined"`\n- **P1**: Home Security mobile horizontal connector bars between vertically stacked subsystems\n- **P2**: Contact page "Available upon request" (deferred — no email/inventory available)\n\n## ACTIONS\n1. **HeroSignal SVG fix** (`src/components/home/HeroSignal.tsx`): Removed static `cx={0}` attribute from leading pulse `<motion.circle>`. Moved `cx: 0` into framer-motion `initial` prop. The static attribute conflicted with the animated `cx: [0, 600]` during hydration.\n\n2. **Mobile Engineering Network** (`src/components/home/SystemMap.module.css`): Added `.mobileFlowItem .domainButton` CSS override to set `position: static`, `transform: none`, `width: 100%`, `text-align: center`. This overrides the desktop absolute positioning for mobile flow items, allowing natural vertical document flow.\n\n3. **Mobile flow connectors** (`src/components/home/SystemMap.module.css`): Redesigned `.mobileFlowItem__connector` from a 1px left-aligned line to a 2px centered vertical gradient with a downward-pointing chevron pseudo-element (`::after`), matching the data-flow direction and existing chevron convention.\n\n4. **Mobile architecture text wrapping** (`src/app/globals.css`): Added `.architecture-diagram` CSS class override with `white-space: pre-wrap !important`, `word-break: break-word`, `overflow-x: visible !important`, `max-height: none !important`. This fixes the shared `<pre>` element used across all 5 project case-study pages, allowing architecture strings to wrap instead of clipping.\n\n5. **Home Security mobile connectors** (`src/components/home/FeaturedSystem.module.css`): Added `.archGroup__connector { display: none !important; }` inside the `@media (max-width: 768px)` rule. Hides the horizontal connector bars between side-by-side node pairs on mobile, restoring clean vertical flow.\n\n## ROOT CAUSES\n1. **HeroSignal error**: Static JSX attribute `cx={0}` on a `<motion.circle>` that also animates `cx` via framer-motion. During SSR/hydration, the static value conflicted with the animation, producing `undefined`.\n\n2. **Network overlap**: `DomainButton` used `position: absolute` with percentage-based coordinates (`left: ${domain.x / 800 * 100}%`). On mobile, all 8 nodes competed for the same narrow viewport space.\n\n3. **Architecture clipping**: `<pre>` with `whiteSpace: "pre"` prevents text wrapping. Architecture strings like `"Sensor WROOM → Console WROOM → UART bridge → ESP32-S3 → Raspberry Pi → Notifications / Drive / Remote Access → Mobile App"` are single-line and don\'t fit on 375px/390px viewports.\n\n4. **Home Security bars**: `.archGroup__connector` (3px horizontal bars with chevron pseudo-elements) was not hidden on mobile. The `flex-direction: column` on `.archGroup__row` stacked nodes vertically but left the horizontal connector bars visible as full-width grey bars.\n\n## BROWSER EVIDENCE\nScreenshots captured at 4 viewports (375px, 390px, 768px, 1280px) across 9 pages (36 total checks).\n\n**Before**:\n- Mobile Engineering Network: 8 nodes overlapping in dense cluster\n- Mobile architecture text: All 5 pages clipped after initial components\n- Mobile Home Security: Full-width horizontal grey bars between subsystem rows\n- Console: `[error] Error: <circle> attribute cx: Expected length, "undefined"`\n\n**After**:\n- Mobile Engineering Network: 8 nodes flow vertically, each with own space, centered chevron connectors\n- Mobile architecture text: All 5 pages show fully wrapped text (Home Security: 4 lines, Ultrasonic: 3 lines, Joystick: 2 lines, FPGA: 3 lines, Power: 3 lines)\n- Mobile Home Security: Horizontal bars gone, clean vertical flow\n- Console: No errors (only React DevTools info and HMR log)\n\nScreenshots saved in `screenshots/` and `screenshots/verify/` directories.\n\n## VERIFICATION\n- **Playwright**: 36 checks (9 pages × 4 viewports), 0 errors, 0 horizontal overflow\n- **Lint**: PASS (0 errors, 1 pre-existing warning)\n- **Build**: PASS (11 pages generated, all static)\n- **Console**: No errors on any page\n\n## REGRESSION CHECKS\n| Previously Working | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Desktop Engineering Network | PASS |\n| Desktop Home Security architecture | PASS |\n| Desktop project case-study pages | PASS |\n| Homepage hero composition | PASS |\n| Homepage interactive demos | PASS |\n| Desktop navigation | PASS |\n| Mobile navigation | PASS |\n| SelectedWork interactions | PASS |\n| FeaturedSystem scroll animations | PASS |\n\n## OUTCOME\n**PASS** — All 4 P0/P1 defects resolved. No regressions detected.\n\n## GIT\n- **Commit**: `da0e325` fix: Mobile responsive layout, architecture text wrapping, and SVG console error\n- **Handoff**: `docs/handoffs/15d-critical-responsive-svg-repairs.md`\n- **Files changed**: 5 files, +290/-11 lines\n- **Working tree**: Clean (only pre-existing playwright changes and untracked verification files remain)\n\n## DEVIATIONS\n- Contact page deferred per instructions: "do not invent an email address or resume URL"\n- No subagents used, all work performed directly\n\n## REMAINING WORK\n1. Contact page — Add actual email link, resume link, professional profile links when details available\n2. About page — Complete education section, make resume actionable\n3. Case studies — Add authentic engineering evidence (photos, schematics, test results)\n4. Projects index — Add visual previews per project\n5. ARM project — Add to Projects index if it qualifies as full project\n6. Metadata audit — Fix Vivado/MATLAB listed under Hardware instead of Software/Tools\n7. Hero composition — Improve desktop right-side empty space and mobile hero spacing\n8. Production build verification — Confirm Next.js dev indicator doesn\'t leak into production\n\n## COMPLETED CHECKLIST\n| Item | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Inspect existing implementation | PASS |\n| 2. Fix mobile Engineering Network | PASS |\n| 3. Fix mobile architecture clipping (5 case studies) | PASS |\n| 4. Fix Home Security mobile connectors | PASS |\n| 5. Investigate and fix homepage SVG console error | PASS |\n| 6. Browser verification and regression testing | PASS |\n| 7. Create detailed milestone handoff | PASS |\n| 8. Commit the verified milestone | PASS |\n| 9. Send complete report through ask_chatgpt | PASS |', 'timeout': 1800000}
