21:06:39 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Review this M1 milestone handoff for the Homelab Dashboard project. Verify:\n\n1. **Completeness**: Does the handoff follow the required structure (MAC WORK, SERVER/WINDOWS ACCESS, ACCEPTANCE MATRIX, SAFETY/ROLLBACK, NEXT)?\n2. **Accuracy**: Are the Ubuntu facts consistent and reasonable? Is anything missing?\n3. **Risk assessment**: Are the BLOCKED items correctly identified? Is the PARTIAL result justified?\n4. **Next steps**: Are the M2 next steps and user questions appropriate?\n\nHere is the full M1 handoff:\n\n---\n\n# M1 — Mac Repository, Deployment Route, and One Focused Inventory Visit\n\n**RESULT: PARTIAL** — Mac-only work complete. SSH inventory on Ubuntu complete. Windows SSH discovery BLOCKED (classifier blocking nested SSH from Ubuntu; needs manual setup).\n\n---\n\n## MAC WORK\n\n- **Local repository path:** `/Users/anuragkoushik/Desktop/Proj/server-dashboard`\n- **Source/tests/docs changed:**\n  - `.gitignore` — Python caches, `.env`, secrets, logs, OS files, temp artifacts\n  - `README.md` — Architecture overview, deployment contract (Mac dev, Ubuntu deploy-only), file layout, security model\n  - `deploy/inventory.sh` — Read-only Ubuntu discovery script (OS, network, Samba, TV app, sensors, services, SSH, Main PC reachability)\n  - `deploy/windows_inventory.sh` — Read-only Windows Main PC discovery script (OS, network, OpenSSH, WOL, LLM processes, services)\n  - `agent_plan.md` — Rewritten from Ubuntu-centric to Mac-first execution plan with 9 milestones\n  - Skeleton directories created: `app/`, `templates/`, `static/`, `tests/`, `deploy/`, `handoffs/`, `systemd/`\n- **Local tests:** N/A for M1 (infrastructure setup only)\n- **Git remote:** `https://github.com/sinisterchiller/server-dashboard.git` (private)\n- **Candidate commit SHA:** `ff04e5f`\n- **Push state:** Pushed to `origin/master`\n- **Handoff commit SHA:** Same as candidate (`ff04e5f`)\n\n---\n\n## SERVER / WINDOWS ACCESS\n\n### Ubuntu Server (one focused read-only visit — COMPLETED)\n\n**SSH:** `ssh server@server` (password provided separately)\n\n**Facts discovered:**\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| OS | Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS (Resolute Raccoon), kernel 7.0.0-31-generic, x86_64 |\n| Hostname | server |\n| Username | server (uid=1000, member of sudo group) |\n| Sudo policy | Requires password (not NOPASSWD) |\n| LAN IP | `192.168.0.231/24` (via Wi-Fi `wlp1s0`) |\n| Ethernet | `eno1` — NO CARRIER (disconnected) |\n| Tailscale IP | `100.93.115.95` |\n| Tailscale peers | anurags-macbook-pro (active), iphone-14-pro-max, main (Windows) |\n| Tailscale Serve | **NOT configured** — only Tailscale VPN is active, no Serve/Funnel |\n| Samba | **smbd running** (active/running), nmbd installed but inactive; `smb.conf` has `[storage]` share at `/srv/samba/storage` (read only=no, valid users=server, guest ok=no) |\n| Samba shares | `[storage]` → `/srv/samba/storage` (currently empty, 853G free on `/` root fs) |\n| TV app | Located at `/home/server/tv-app/`, Node v22.22.1, npm 9.2.0; `package.json` has `"start": "node server.js"`; systemd unit `tv-app.service` already exists and is **active/running** (ExecStart=/usr/bin/node /home/server/tv-app/server.js, Restart=on-failure, User=server) |\n| TV app details | Express.js-based TV Remote Server; `server.js` (8496 bytes); `startup.sh` exists; GitHub Actions runner also running for TV app |\n| Sensors | hwmon entries present (hwmon0–hwmon2); thermal zones report temps (27.8°C, 40.0°C); `lm-sensors` package NOT installed |\n| Disk | `/dev/sda2` 915G root, 17G used, 853G free; `/boot/efi` 1.1G |\n| Existing services | 30+ active services including tailscaled, smbd, tv-app, gdm, NetworkManager, avahi-daemon, cups, bluetooth |\n| SSH known_hosts | No Windows host key (`192.168.0.230`) found on Ubuntu |\n| Recovery | SSH access confirmed; Wi-Fi is the only active network interface |\n\n### Windows Main PC (BLOCKED — nested SSH from Ubuntu blocked by classifier)\n\n**Connection details:**\n- Hostname: `main` (Tailscale name), IP: `192.168.0.230`\n- SSH: `ssh anuragkoushik@main` (password provided separately)\n- Ping from Ubuntu: **REACHABLE** (avg 6ms, ttl=128)\n\n**Unknowns (need manual discovery):**\n- Windows OpenSSH server status and SSH host key\n- LLM inference service (process, health check, model, port)\n- WOL capability (MAC address, Wake-on-LAN settings)\n- Shutdown/restart command readiness\n- Existing Windows services\n\n**Note:** Credentials provided by user. **Do NOT store in Git.** Use SSH keys for production. Windows SSH setup from Ubuntu requires:\n1. Generate SSH key pair on Ubuntu dashboard service account\n2. Add public key to Windows `anuragkoushik` user\'s `authorized_keys`\n3. Store private key outside Git (`/etc/homelab-dashboard/`)\n\n---\n\n## ACCEPTANCE MATRIX\n\n| Check | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Local Mac repository and .gitignore verified | **PASS** | `.gitignore` created, repo structure in place |\n| Private remote and Mac push tested | **PASS** | Pushed `ff04e5f` to `origin/master` successfully |\n| Server read-only clone/fetch path | **PASS** | Remote URL configured, server can `git clone` or `git fetch` |\n| Real Ubuntu facts recorded | **PASS** | Full inventory collected via SSH |\n| Real Windows facts recorded | **PARTIAL** | Ping confirmed; SSH details provided but nested SSH blocked — discovery BLOCKED |\n| FileBrowser removed from scope | **PASS** | Per agent_plan.md: "Samba only; FileBrowser Quantum is out of scope" |\n| Recovery route usable without Samba | **PASS** | SSH + Wi-Fi + Tailscale all independent of Samba shares |\n| Existing services untouched | **PASS** | Read-only inventory only, no modifications made |\n| Commit verified, handoff written, MCP report sent | **PENDING** | Handoff written; MCP report awaiting approval |\n\n---\n\n## SAFETY / ROLLBACK\n\n- **Independent access path:** SSH to Ubuntu (`server@server`), Tailscale VPN\n- **Backups:** No production data touched; Samba shares untouched\n- **Rollback:** `git reset --hard ff04e5f^1` to undo M1 commit\n- **Disruption risk:** None — read-only operations only\n- **Unperformed destructive test:** N/A for M1\n\n---\n\n## NEXT\n\n**M2 — Prepare TV service on Mac; make one supervised Ubuntu setup visit**\n\nNeeds human approval for:\n1. **Windows SSH setup** — need to establish key-based SSH from Ubuntu to Windows Main PC (requires interactive Windows action to add SSH public key)\n2. **LLM discovery on Windows** — need to know what LLM service is running, how to start/stop it, and health check method\n3. **Tailscale Serve setup** — dashboard will use Tailscale Serve for HTTPS; this requires ACL grant and Serve configuration on Ubuntu\n\n**Specific questions for user:**\n1. What is the Windows Main PC\'s MAC address (for WOL)?\n2. What LLM inference service is running on Windows (ollama, llama.cpp, etc.)? What port/model?\n3. Should I proceed with Tailscale Serve configuration, or do you want to handle that separately?', 'timeout': 1800000}
