12:11:09 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': "Review the M3 (Backend Auth) handoff report for the homelab dashboard project. Check for:\n\n1. **Security issues**: Any vulnerabilities in the auth implementation (session management, CSRF, password hashing, RBAC, cookie security)\n2. **Correctness**: Any bugs or logical errors in the database schema, API endpoints, or security controls\n3. **Completeness**: Is the scope properly covered? Any missing security controls?\n4. **Best practices**: Are there any improvements needed for the auth implementation?\n\nHere is the handoff report:\n\n---\n\n# M3: Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF\n\n**Status**: COMPLETE — all 46 tests passing\n\n## Scope\n\nBuilt a complete authentication and authorization backend for the homelab dashboard API:\n\n- FastAPI project structure with ASGI lifespan for DB init\n- SQLite with WAL mode, foreign keys, versioned migrations\n- Argon2id password hashing (memory-hard, recommended for passwords)\n- Opaque revocable sessions (token hashes, idle/absolute expiry)\n- CSRF double-submit cookie protection\n- Origin validation\n- Default-deny RBAC (Admin / Operator / Viewer)\n- Account lockout (5 failed attempts → 15 min lock)\n- Audit logging for all auth events\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\napp/\n├── main.py              # FastAPI app, lifespan, health endpoint\n├── config.py            # Pydantic Settings (env var validation)\n├── database.py          # SQLite pool, WAL mode, migrations table\n├── sessions.py          # Session CRUD (create, validate, expire, revoke)\n├── security.py          # Argon2id, CSRF, origin checks, RBAC decorators, account lockout\n├── deps.py              # FastAPI dependency injections (get_current_user, verify_csrf, etc.)\n├── schemas.py           # Pydantic request/response models\n└── routers/\n    ├── __init__.py      # Router registration\n    ├── auth.py          # POST /bootstrap, /login, /logout, /me, /change-password\n    └── admin.py         # User CRUD, session management, audit log (Admin-only)\n\ntests/\n├── conftest.py          # Fixtures: test DB, httpx client, bootstrap/login helpers\n├── test_auth.py         # 18 tests: bootstrap, login, logout, me, change-password\n├── test_admin.py        # 13 tests: user CRUD, RBAC, audit log, last-admin protection\n├── test_sessions.py     # 8 tests: session lifecycle, expiry, revocation\n└── test_csrf.py         # 11 tests: CSRF token generation, validation, origin checks\n```\n\n## Database Schema\n\n### `schema_migrations`\nTracks applied migrations for versioned schema evolution.\n\n### `users`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| username | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL |\n| password_hash | TEXT | NOT NULL (Argon2id) |\n| role | TEXT | NOT NULL, CHECK IN ('admin', 'operator', 'viewer') |\n| is_active | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 1, CHECK IN (0, 1) |\n| must_change_pw | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 1, CHECK IN (0, 1) |\n| created_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| updated_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n\nIndexes: `idx_users_username`, `idx_users_role`, `idx_users_is_active`\n\n### `sessions`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| user_id | INTEGER | NOT NULL, REFERENCES users(id) |\n| token_hash | TEXT | NOT NULL, UNIQUE, SHA-256 of raw token |\n| created_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| last_accessed_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| idle_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 (idle expiry deadline) |\n| expires_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 (absolute expiry deadline) |\n| revoked | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0, CHECK IN (0, 1) |\n\nIndexes: `idx_sessions_token_hash`, `idx_sessions_user_id`, `idx_sessions_user_revoked`\n\n### `audit_log`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| timestamp | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| actor_user | TEXT | NOT NULL (username of actor) |\n| event_type | TEXT | NOT NULL |\n| success | INTEGER | NOT NULL, CHECK IN (0, 1) |\n| detail | TEXT | NOT NULL |\n\nIndexes: `idx_audit_timestamp`, `idx_audit_actor`, `idx_audit_event`\n\n## Security Details\n\n### Session Tokens\n- Generated with `secrets.token_urlsafe(48)` (64 bytes of entropy)\n- Stored as SHA-256 hashes only — raw tokens never persisted\n- Dual expiry: idle (720 min default) + absolute (1 day default)\n- Touch on access to refresh idle timer\n- Revocable individually or per-user\n\n### Cookie Security\n- Session: `__Host-homelab_session` — Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain\n- CSRF: `homelab_csrf` — HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/\n- Double-submit pattern: cookie value must match `X-CSRF-Token` header\n\n### CSRF Protection\n- Token format: `<64-hex-chars>.<16-hex-chars-signature>`\n- Signature: `SHA-256(raw + secret_key)[:16]`\n- Validated on all non-GET requests via `verify_mutation_request()`\n- Combined with origin checking (Origin/Referer header validation)\n\n### RBAC Hierarchy\n- **Admin**: Full access (all routes)\n- **Operator**: Limited access (service actions, no user management)\n- **Viewer**: Read-only access\n- Default-deny: all routes explicitly require a role\n- Last-admin protection: cannot disable or demote the final admin\n\n### Account Lockout\n- 5 failed login attempts → 15-minute lockout\n- Lockout is per-username, not per-IP\n- Generic login failure message (never reveals username existence)\n\n### Audit Log\nRecords every auth event:\n- Successful/failed logins\n- Password changes (self and admin-forced)\n- User creation/updates/deletion attempts\n- Session revocations\n- Role changes\n\n## Configuration\n\nAll via environment variables:\n\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address |\n| `PORT` | `8000` | Bind port |\n| `DB_PATH` | `data/homelab.db` | SQLite database path |\n| `SECRET_KEY` | *(required)* | HMAC signing key for CSRF/sessions |\n| `SESSION_IDLE_TTL_MINUTES` | `720` | Idle expiry (12 hours) |\n| `SESSION_ABSOLUTE_TTL_DAYS` | `1` | Absolute expiry (1 day) |\n| `CSRF_COOKIE_NAME` | `homelab_csrf` | CSRF cookie name |\n| `CSRF_HEADER_NAME` | `X-CSRF-Token` | CSRF header name |\n| `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | `http://localhost:3000` | Comma-separated allowed origins |\n| `FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS_BEFORE_LOCK` | `5` | Lockout threshold |\n| `FAILED_LOGIN_LOCKOUT_MINUTES` | `15` | Lockout duration |\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n46 passed in 3.41s\n```\n\n### Test Breakdown\n- **test_auth.py** (18 tests): Bootstrap, login (success/failure/lockout), logout, me, change-password\n- **test_admin.py** (13 tests): User CRUD, RBAC enforcement, audit log, last-admin protection, health\n- **test_sessions.py** (8 tests): Session creation, validation, expiry, revocation, password-change revocation\n- **test_csrf.py** (11 tests): Token generation, signature validation, tamper detection, origin checks\n\n## API Endpoints\n\n### Authentication\n| Method | Path | Auth | CSRF | Description |\n|--------|------|------|------|-------------|\n| POST | `/api/auth/bootstrap` | None | No | Create first admin |\n| POST | `/api/auth/login` | None | No | Login, set session cookie |\n| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | No | Current user profile |\n| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | Revoke current session |\n| POST | `/api/auth/change-password` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | Change password, revoke others |\n\n### Admin (Admin-only)\n| Method | Path | Auth | CSRF | Description |\n|--------|------|------|------|-------------|\n| GET | `/api/admin/users` | Admin | No | List all users |\n| POST | `/api/admin/users` | Admin | Yes | Create user |\n| PATCH | `/api/admin/users/{id}` | Admin | Yes | Update user role/active |\n| POST | `/api/admin/users/{id}/reset-password` | Admin | Yes | Admin-forced password reset |\n| GET | `/api/admin/sessions` | Admin | No | List active sessions |\n| DELETE | `/api/admin/sessions/{id}` | Admin | Yes | Revoke session |\n| GET | `/api/admin/audit` | Admin | No | Recent audit entries |\n\n### Health\n| Method | Path | Auth | CSRF | Description |\n|--------|------|------|------|-------------|\n| GET | `/api/health` | None | No | Health check |\n\n## Key Design Decisions\n\n1. **Token hashes, not JWTs** — Sessions stored as SHA-256 hashes in SQLite, enabling server-side revocation without token introspection. Raw tokens are never stored.\n\n2. **Cookie parsing from headers** — Session and CSRF cookies parsed manually from the `Cookie` header rather than using Starlette's `Cookie()` dependency, for reliability with ASGITransport in tests.\n\n3. **Default-deny RBAC** — Every route explicitly declares required role. No implicit access anywhere.\n\n4. **Last-admin protection** — Prevents accidentally disabling the final admin account, a common operational hazard.\n\n5. **Argon2id** — Chosen over bcrypt/SCrypt for being memory-hard and the current recommendation for password hashing.\n\n6. **WAL mode** — SQLite Write-Ahead Logging for better concurrent read performance without blocking writers.", 'timeout': 1800000}
