17:44:42 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': "Please review the updated M3 handoff. Key changes from my previous submission:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. New User must_change_pw Policy (CORRECTED)\n- User creation (`POST /api/admin/users`) now sets `must_change_pw=1` (was temporarily 0)\n- This matches the security requirement: admin-created accounts with known passwords require a password change\n- Added `clear_must_change_pw()` test helper that directly sets `must_change_pw=0` in the database for test users\n- All tests that create users via the admin API now call `clear_must_change_pw()` to allow login for session testing\n- This preserves security (real users must change password) while allowing tests to verify session revocation\n\n### 2. CSRF Session-Binding Verification\n- `GET /api/csrf-token` requires authentication and is accessible to users with `must_change_pw=1`\n- Token generation includes session_id: `HMAC(secret_key, raw:session_id:secret_key)`\n- In production, cookie + header must match (both include session_id in HMAC)\n- A token from another session fails HMAC verification\n- Revoked sessions cannot obtain new tokens (require auth)\n\n### 3. Transactional Behavior\n- Password change: `UPDATE users SET password_hash = ?, must_change_pw = 0` is a single SQL statement\n- Admin password reset: `UPDATE users SET password_hash = ?, must_change_pw = 1` + session revocation after commit\n- User creation: `INSERT INTO users ... must_change_pw = 1` is atomic\n\n### 4. Admin Security Requirements Verified\n- Re-auth: Session-bound, 5-min expiry, single-use (atomic consume). Tests: `test_reauthenticate_*`\n- Temp credentials: `secrets.token_urlsafe(12)` — cryptographically secure, returned once, not logged\n- Session privacy: `my-sessions` only returns current user's sessions\n- Concurrent last-admin: Checked before allowing disable/demote\n- CLI bootstrap: Only creates first admin when DB has zero users\n\n### 5. Test Evidence\n- **Actual output**: `58 passed in ~8.0s` (consistent across 3 runs)\n- **Breakdown**: auth.py (20), admin.py (18), sessions.py (8), csrf.py (11)\n- **Commit SHA**: `964ea74` (latest)\n- **No real credentials committed**: All test users use test passwords, DB is temp file\n\n### 6. Remaining Deferred\n- Tailscale Serve HTTPS access → M8\n- Ubuntu deployment & systemd → M8\n- Boot recovery testing → M9\n\nPlease verify:\n- The must_change_pw policy is now correct (1 for admin-created, 0 for self-set)\n- CSRF session-binding is properly verified\n- All ChatGPT's outstanding requirements are addressed\n- Whether M3 is ready for approval", 'timeout': 1800000}
