19:34:50 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'You are a security-focused code reviewer. Review the following M3 (Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF) milestone implementation for the Homelab Dashboard project. Check for correctness, security issues, logic errors, and test coverage gaps.\n\n## Project Structure\n```\napp/\n├── main.py              # FastAPI app, lifespan, health endpoint\n├── config.py            # Pydantic Settings (env var validation, production checks)\n├── database.py          # SQLite pool, WAL mode, migrations (v2: reauth_tokens table)\n├── sessions.py          # Session CRUD (create, validate, expire, revoke)\n├── security.py          # Argon2id, HMAC CSRF (session-bound), origin checks, RBAC\n├── deps.py              # FastAPI DI (get_current_user, verify_csrf, verify_reauth)\n├── schemas.py           # Pydantic request/response models\n├── cli_bootstrap.py     # CLI first-admin creation (no token output)\n└── routers/\n    ├── __init__.py      # Router registration\n    ├── auth.py          # Login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions\n    └── admin.py         # User CRUD, session management, audit log, password reset\n```\n\n## Key Security Requirements\n1. **CSRF**: HMAC-SHA256 tokens with session binding. Format: `<raw>.<hmac>` where HMAC = HMAC-SHA256(secret_key, raw || ":" || session_id || secret_key). Double-submit pattern (cookie + header).\n2. **Sessions**: Opaque tokens via `secrets.token_urlsafe(48)`. SHA-256 hash stored. Idle (720min) + absolute (7 days) expiry. Touch on access.\n3. **Cookie**: `__Host-homelab_session` with Secure=True ALWAYS, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain.\n4. **RBAC**: Admin > Operator > Viewer. Default-deny. Last-admin protection.\n5. **Account lockout**: 5 failed attempts → 15 min lockout. Generic error messages.\n6. **Re-auth**: Single-use tokens, 5-min expiry, stored in `reauth_tokens` table.\n7. **must_change_pw**: Admin-created users get must_change_pw=1, blocking all endpoints except change-password, csrf-token, and logout.\n8. **Transactional**: Password changes, session revocations, user updates in single SQLite transactions.\n\n## Test Results\n62 tests passing (0 failures):\n- test_auth.py: 26 tests (login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions, must_change_pw, cross-session CSRF)\n- test_admin.py: 18 tests (user CRUD, RBAC, audit log, last-admin protection, password reset, session revocation)\n- test_csrf.py: 11 tests (token generation, validation, tamper detection, origin checks)\n- test_sessions.py: 7 tests (session creation, validation, expiry, revocation)\n\n## Files to Review\n\n### app/main.py\n```python\n"""Homelab Dashboard — FastAPI application entry point.\n\nInitialises the database, registers routers, and provides the\nhealth-check endpoint.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\nfrom .config import get_settings\nfrom .database import init_pool, init_schema\nfrom .routers import admin, auth\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI) -> None:\n    """Initialise the database on startup."""\n    settings = get_settings()\n    init_pool(settings.db_path)\n    init_schema()\n    yield\n\n\napp = FastAPI(\n    title="Homelab Dashboard",\n    version="0.1.0",\n    lifespan=lifespan,\n)\n\n# Register routers\napp.include_router(auth.router)\napp.include_router(admin.router)\n\n\n@app.get("/api/health")\nasync def health() -> JSONResponse:\n    """Public health check — no authentication required."""\n    return JSONResponse(content={"status": "ok", "version": "0.1.0"})\n```\n\n### app/config.py\n```python\n"""Pydantic schemas for request validation and response serialisation.\n\nAll user-facing response models redact sensitive fields.  Request\nmodels enforce length limits and character restrictions.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Annotated\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field, EmailStr, field_validator\n\n# ── Authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass LoginRequest(BaseModel):\n    username: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1, max_length=128)]\n    password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1, max_length=256)]\n\n\nclass ChangePasswordRequest(BaseModel):\n    current_password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1, max_length=256)]\n    new_password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=8, max_length=128)]\n\n    @field_validator("new_password")\n    @classmethod\n    def password_strength(cls, v: str) -> str:\n        if len(v) < 8:\n            raise ValueError("Password must be at least 8 characters")\n        return v\n\n\nclass ReauthRequest(BaseModel):\n    """Re-authentication request (same shape as login)."""\n    password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1, max_length=256)]\n\n\nclass SessionResponse(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    created_at: str\n    last_activity: str\n    idle_expires_at: str\n    absolute_expires_at: str\n    is_current: bool = False\n\n\nclass MySessionResponse(BaseModel):\n    """Self-service session response."""\n    id: int\n    created_at: str\n    last_activity: str\n    idle_expires_at: str\n    absolute_expires_at: str\n    is_current: bool = False\n\n\n# ── Admin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass CreateUserRequest(BaseModel):\n    username: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1, max_length=128)]\n    password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=8, max_length=128)]\n    role: Annotated[str, Field(default="viewer")]\n\n    @field_validator("role")\n    @classmethod\n    def valid_role(cls, v: str) -> str:\n        if v not in ("admin", "operator", "viewer"):\n            raise ValueError("Role must be admin, operator, or viewer")\n        return v\n\n\nclass UpdateUserRequest(BaseModel):\n    role: str | None = None\n    is_active: bool | None = None\n\n\nclass ResetPasswordRequest(BaseModel):\n    new_password: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=8, max_length=128)]\n\n\nclass AuditEntry(BaseModel):\n    timestamp: str\n    actor_user: str\n    event_type: str\n    target: str | None = None\n    details: str | None = None\n    success: bool\n\n\nclass UserBrief(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    username: str\n    role: str\n    is_active: bool\n    created_at: str\n    last_login_at: str | None = None\n```\n\n### app/config.py (continued - Configuration)\n```python\n"""Application configuration with pydantic validation.\n\nAll settings are read from environment variables with sensible defaults\nfor local development. Production values must be set explicitly.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom pydantic_settings import BaseSettings\n\n\nclass Settings(BaseSettings):\n    """Strict configuration for the homelab dashboard.\n\n    Every field must validate on construction; missing required\n    production values will raise ``ValidationError``.\n    """\n\n    app_name: str = "Homelab Dashboard"\n    app_version: str = "0.1.0"\n\n    # Server binding\n    bind_host: str = "127.0.0.1"\n    bind_port: int = Field(default=8787, ge=1, le=65535)\n\n    # Database — relative path in dev, absolute in production\n    db_path: Path = Field(\n        default=Path(__file__).parent.parent / "data" / "homelab.db",\n    )\n\n    # Secrets — required in production\n    secret_key: str = ""\n\n    # Session settings\n    session_idle_ttl_minutes: int = Field(default=720, ge=1)  # 12 hours\n    session_absolute_ttl_days: int = Field(default=7, ge=1)\n\n    # CSRF\n    csrf_cookie_name: str = "homelab_csrf"\n    csrf_header_name: str = "X-CSRF-Token"\n\n    # Allowed origins (comma-separated hostnames, no scheme/port)\n    allowed_origins: str = ""\n\n    # Environment (development / production)\n    environment: str = "development"\n\n    model_config = {"env_file": ".env", "env_file_encoding": "utf-8"}\n\n    @property\n    def allowed_origins_set(self) -> set[str]:\n        return {o.strip() for o in self.allowed_origins.split(",") if o.strip()}\n\n    @property\n    def is_production(self) -> bool:\n        return self.environment == "production"\n\n\n_settings: Settings | None = None\n\n\ndef get_settings() -> Settings:\n    global _settings\n    if _settings is None:\n        _settings = Settings()\n    _settings._validate_production()\n    return _settings\n\n\ndef _settings_validate_production(self: Settings) -> None:\n    """Validate production configuration. Raises ``RuntimeError`` on misconfiguration."""\n    if not self.is_production:\n        return\n    if not self.secret_key or len(self.secret_key) < 32:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            "Production mode requires a non-empty SECRET_KEY with at least 32 characters. "\n            "Set the SECRET_KEY environment variable."\n        )\n    if not self.db_path.is_absolute():\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            "Production mode requires an absolute DB_PATH. "\n            "Set DB_PATH to an absolute path (e.g. /var/lib/homelab-dashboard/homelab.db)."\n        )\n    if not self.allowed_origins or not self.allowed_origins.strip():\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            "Production mode requires ALLOWED_ORIGINS to be configured. "\n            "Set the ALLOWED_ORIGINS environment variable to the trusted dashboard origin "\n            "(e.g. https://homelab-dashboard.your-tailnet.ts.net)."\n        )\n\n\nSettings._validate_production = _settings_validate_production  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n```\n\n### app/database.py\n```python\n"""SQLite database setup with WAL mode and migration support.\n\nProvides a connection pool, schema initialisation, and a simple\nversioned migration system.  All queries use parameterised statements;\nno raw user input is interpolated into SQL.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport threading\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Generator\n\nfrom .config import get_settings\n\n# ── Schema version ────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSCHEMA_VERSION = 2\n\n# ── Schema DDL (idempotent via IF NOT EXISTS) ─────────────────────\n_SCHEMA_SQL = """\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS schema_migrations (\n    version   INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    applied_at TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\'now\'))\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n    id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    username        TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    password_hash   TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    role            TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT \'viewer\',\n    is_active       INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n    must_change_pw  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    created_at      TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\'now\')),\n    last_login_at   TEXT,\n    failed_attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    locked_until    TEXT,\n    CHECK(length(username) > 0 AND length(username) <= 128),\n    CHECK(role IN (\'admin\', \'operator\', \'viewer\'))\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n    id                  INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    token_hash          TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    user_id             INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    created_at          TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\'now\')),\n    last_activity       TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\'now\')),\n    idle_expires_at     TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    absolute_expires_at TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    revoked             INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS audit_log (\n    id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    timestamp   TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\'now\')),\n    actor_user  TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    event_type  TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    target      TEXT,\n    details     TEXT,\n    success     INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    error       TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sessions_token_hash ON sessions(token_hash);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sessions_user_id ON sessions(user_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_audit_actor ON audit_log(actor_user);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_audit_timestamp ON audit_log(timestamp);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS reauth_tokens (\n    id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    token_hash      TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    user_id         INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    session_id      INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    expires_at      TEXT    NOT NULL,\n    consumed        INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    FOREIGN KEY (session_id) REFERENCES sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_reauth_token ON reauth_tokens(token_hash);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_reauth_session ON reauth_tokens(session_id);\n"""\n\n\nclass _Pool:\n    """Thread-local SQLite connection pool."""\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._local = threading.local()\n\n    def _connect(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        conn = sqlite3.connect(str(self._db_path))\n        conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        conn.execute("PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL")\n        conn.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON")\n        return conn\n\n    def get(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        if not hasattr(self._local, "conn") or self._local.conn is None:\n            self._local.conn = self._connect()\n        return self._local.conn\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        if hasattr(self._local, "conn") and self._local.conn is not None:\n            self._local.conn.close()\n            self._local.conn = None\n\n\n_pool: _Pool | None = None\n\n\ndef init_pool(db_path: Path | None = None) -> _Pool:\n    global _pool\n    if _pool is None:\n        if db_path is None:\n            db_path = get_settings().db_path\n        db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        _pool = _Pool(db_path)\n    return _pool\n\n\ndef get_db() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    """Return a thread-local database connection."""\n    return init_pool().get()\n\n\ndef init_schema() -> None:\n    """Create tables and run migrations if needed."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    try:\n        conn.executescript(_SCHEMA_SQL)\n        # Record schema version\n        conn.execute(\n            "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO schema_migrations (version, applied_at) "\n            "VALUES (?, datetime(\'now\'))",\n            (SCHEMA_VERSION,),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n    except sqlite3.Error:\n        conn.rollback()\n        raise\n\n\n@contextmanager\ndef transaction() -> Generator[sqlite3.Connection, None, None]:\n    """Context manager that commits on success or rolls back on error."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    try:\n        yield conn\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        conn.rollback()\n        raise\n\n\ndef run_migrations(conn: sqlite3.Connection | None = None) -> None:\n    """Run any pending migrations.  Currently a no-op (schema is static)."""\n    target = conn is None\n    if target:\n        conn = get_db()\n    try:\n        row = conn.execute(\n            "SELECT MAX(version) FROM schema_migrations"\n        ).fetchone()\n        current = row[0] if row[0] is not None else 0\n        if current < SCHEMA_VERSION:\n            # Placeholder for future migrations\n            conn.execute(\n                "INSERT INTO schema_migrations (version, applied_at) "\n                "VALUES (?, datetime(\'now\'))",\n                (SCHEMA_VERSION,),\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n    except sqlite3.Error:\n        if target:\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise\n```\n\n### app/sessions.py\n```python\n"""Server-side session management with hashed tokens.\n\nTokens are never stored in plaintext — only their SHA-256 hashes\nare persisted.  The client receives the raw token in an HttpOnly,\nSecure cookie.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport secrets\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\nfrom .config import get_settings\nfrom .database import get_db, transaction\n\n\ndef generate_token() -> str:\n    """Generate a cryptographically random session token."""\n    return secrets.token_urlsafe(48)\n\n\ndef hash_token(token: str) -> str:\n    """SHA-256 hash of the raw token."""\n    return hashlib.sha256(token.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef create_session(user_id: int) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    """Create a new session for *user_id*.\n\n    Returns ``(raw_token, session_id)``.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n    idle_ttl = timedelta(minutes=settings.session_idle_ttl_minutes)\n    absolute_ttl = timedelta(days=settings.session_absolute_ttl_days)\n\n    raw_token = generate_token()\n    token_hash = hash_token(raw_token)\n    idle_expires = (now + idle_ttl).isoformat()\n    absolute_expires = (now + absolute_ttl).isoformat()\n\n    conn = get_db()\n    cur = conn.execute(\n        """INSERT INTO sessions\n           (token_hash, user_id, created_at, last_activity,\n            idle_expires_at, absolute_expires_at, revoked)\n           VALUES (?, ?, datetime(\'now\'), datetime(\'now\'), ?, ?, 0)""",\n        (token_hash, user_id, idle_expires, absolute_expires),\n    )\n    session_id = cur.lastrowid\n    return raw_token, session_id\n\n\ndef get_session(token_hash: str) -> dict | None:\n    """Look up an active (non-revoked, not expired) session by hash."""\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    conn = get_db()\n    row = conn.execute(\n        """SELECT id, user_id, last_activity, idle_expires_at,\n                  absolute_expires_at, revoked\n           FROM sessions\n           WHERE token_hash = ? AND revoked = 0\n             AND idle_expires_at > ? AND absolute_expires_at > ?""",\n        (token_hash, now, now),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is None:\n        return None\n    return dict(row)\n\n\ndef touch_session(session_id: int) -> None:\n    """Refresh the idle timer for a session."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    conn.execute(\n        "UPDATE sessions SET last_activity = datetime(\'now\') WHERE id = ?",\n        (session_id,),\n    )\n\n\ndef revoke_session(session_id: int) -> None:\n    """Revoke a single session by ID."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    conn.execute("UPDATE sessions SET revoked = 1 WHERE id = ?", (session_id,))\n\n\ndef revoke_user_sessions(\n    user_id: int,\n    except_session_id: int | None = None,\n    conn: sqlite3.Connection | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    """Revoke all sessions for a user, optionally keeping one.\n\n    If conn is provided, use that connection (for transactional safety).\n    Otherwise, create a new connection from the pool.\n    """\n    if conn is None:\n        conn = get_db()\n    if except_session_id is not None:\n        conn.execute(\n            "UPDATE sessions SET revoked = 1 "\n            "WHERE user_id = ? AND id != ?",\n            (user_id, except_session_id),\n        )\n    else:\n        conn.execute(\n            "UPDATE sessions SET revoked = 1 WHERE user_id = ?",\n            (user_id,),\n        )\n\n\ndef logout_session(session_id: int) -> None:\n    """Revoke the current session (logout)."""\n    revoke_session(session_id)\n```\n\n### app/security.py\n```python\n"""Security utilities: Argon2id hashing, CSRF, RBAC, origin checks.\n\nAll password hashing uses Argon2id (the memory-hard variant recommended\nfor password hashing).  CSRF uses the double-submit cookie pattern.\nRBAC is enforced as default-deny on the backend.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport secrets\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom functools import wraps\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\n\nimport argon2\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException, Request, status\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\n# ── Password hashing (Argon2id) ──────────────────────────────────\n\n_password_hasher = argon2.PasswordHasher(\n    time_cost=3,\n    memory_cost=65536,\n    parallelism=2,\n    hash_len=32,\n    salt_len=16,\n    type=argon2.Type.ID,\n)\n\n\ndef hash_password(password: str) -> str:\n    """Hash a password with Argon2id."""\n    return _password_hasher.hash(password)\n\n\ndef verify_password(password: str, password_hash: str) -> bool:\n    """Verify a password against an Argon2id hash.\n\n    Always runs the full verification (constant-time) even if the\n    provided hash is malformed, to prevent timing attacks.\n    """\n    try:\n        return _password_hasher.verify(password_hash, password)\n    except argon2.exceptions.VerifyMismatchError:\n        return False\n    except argon2.exceptions.InvalidHash:\n        # Hash is malformed — always return False (not an error)\n        return False\n\n\n# ── CSRF (session-bound HMAC token) ─────────────────────────────\n\n_CSRF_RAW_LENGTH = 32  # 256 bits of randomness\n\n\ndef generate_csrf_token(secret_key: str, session_id: int | None = None) -> str:\n    """Generate a CSRF token signed with HMAC-SHA256.\n\n    When *session_id* is provided the token is bound to that session —\n    an attacker who obtains the token from another session cannot use it.\n\n    Format: ``<32-hex-chars>.<32-hex-chars-hmac>``\n    """\n    raw = secrets.token_hex(_CSRF_RAW_LENGTH)\n    # Include session_id in the HMAC payload when available\n    payload = raw.encode("utf-8")\n    if session_id is not None:\n        payload += f":{session_id}".encode("utf-8")\n    payload += secret_key.encode("utf-8")\n    signature = hmac.new(secret_key.encode("utf-8"), payload, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    return raw + "." + signature\n\n\ndef validate_csrf_token(token: str, secret_key: str, session_id: int | None = None) -> bool:\n    """Validate a CSRF token against its HMAC signature.\n\n    If *session_id* is provided the token must have been generated\n    for that specific session.  When session_id is None the token\n    is validated without session binding (legacy behaviour).\n    """\n    parts = token.split(".", 1)\n    if len(parts) != 2:\n        return False\n    raw, sig = parts\n    payload = raw.encode("utf-8")\n    if session_id is not None:\n        payload += f":{session_id}".encode("utf-8")\n    payload += secret_key.encode("utf-8")\n    expected = hmac.new(secret_key.encode("utf-8"), payload, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    return hmac.compare_digest(sig, expected)\n\n\ndef create_csrf_cookie(token: str) -> tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    """Return (token_value, cookie_kwargs) for setting the CSRF cookie."""\n    return token, {\n        "httponly": True,\n        "samesite": "strict",\n        "secure": False,  # overridden per-environment\n        "path": "/",\n        "domain": None,\n    }\n\n\n# ── Origin checking ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef check_origin(request: Request, allowed_origins: set[str]) -> bool:\n    """Validate the Origin/Referer header against allowed origins."""\n    origin = request.headers.get("origin")\n    referer = request.headers.get("referer")\n\n    if origin:\n        # Extract hostname from origin\n        from urllib.parse import urlparse\n        parsed = urlparse(origin)\n        host = parsed.hostname or ""\n        return host in allowed_origins\n\n    if referer:\n        from urllib.parse import urlparse\n        parsed = urlparse(referer)\n        host = parsed.hostname or ""\n        return host in allowed_origins\n\n    # No origin/referer — allow same-origin requests (no Origin header)\n    return True\n\n\n# ── RBAC helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nROLES = {"admin", "operator", "viewer"}\nROLE_HIERARCHY = {"viewer": 0, "operator": 1, "admin": 2}\n\n\ndef require_role(allowed_roles: set[str]) -> Callable:\n    """Decorator that enforces RBAC on a route handler.\n\n    Usage::\n\n        @router.get("/admin/users")\n        @require_role({"admin", "operator"})\n        def list_users(current_user: dict):\n            ...\n    """\n    def decorator(func: Callable) -> Callable:\n        @wraps(func)\n        def wrapper(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n            # The current_user dict is passed as a kwarg by the dependency\n            current_user = kwargs.get("current_user")\n            if current_user is None:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n                    detail="Not authenticated",\n                )\n            user_role = current_user.get("role", "viewer")\n            if user_role not in allowed_roles:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n                    detail="Insufficient permissions",\n                )\n            return func(*args, **kwargs)\n        return wrapper\n    return decorator\n\n\ndef require_admin(func: Callable) -> Callable:\n    """Shorthand for require_role({\\"admin\\"})."""\n    return require_role({"admin"})(func)\n\n\ndef require_admin_or_operator(func: Callable) -> Callable:\n    """Shorthand for require_role({\\"admin\\", \\"operator\\"})."""\n    return require_role({"admin", "operator"})(func)\n\n\n# ── Cooldown / rate limiting helpers ─────────────────────────────\n\ndef is_locked(locked_until: str | None) -> bool:\n    """Check if an account is currently locked."""\n    if not locked_until:\n        return False\n    try:\n        lock_time = datetime.fromisoformat(locked_until).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        return datetime.now(timezone.utc) < lock_time\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n        return False\n\n\ndef lock_account(max_attempts: int = 5, lock_minutes: int = 15) -> str:\n    """Return an ISO timestamp for when the lock expires."""\n    return (\n        datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        + timedelta(minutes=lock_minutes)\n    ).isoformat()\n\n\ndef reset_failed_attempts() -> tuple[int, None]:\n    """Reset failed attempt counter after successful login."""\n    return 0, None\n```\n\n### app/deps.py\n```python\n"""FastAPI dependency injections.\n\nProvides ``get_current_user`` which extracts the session cookie,\nvalidates the token, and returns the user dict from the database.\nAlso provides CSRF verification, re-auth verification, and origin\nchecking.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom fastapi import Header, HTTPException, Request, status\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\nfrom . import sessions as session_mgr\nfrom .config import get_settings\nfrom .database import get_db\nfrom .security import (\n    check_origin,\n    create_csrf_cookie,\n    generate_csrf_token,\n    validate_csrf_token,\n)\n\n# Cookie names\nSESSION_COOKIE = "__Host-homelab_session"\nCSRF_COOKIE_NAME = "homelab_csrf"\nCSRF_HEADER_NAME = "X-CSRF-Token"\nREAUTH_HEADER_NAME = "X-Reauth-Token"\n\n\nasync def get_current_user(\n    request: Request,\n) -> dict:\n    """Extract and validate the session cookie.\n\n    Returns a dict with keys: ``id``, ``username``, ``role``, ``is_active``,\n    ``must_change_pw``.  Raises HTTP 401 on any validation failure.\n\n    If ``must_change_pw`` is set and the path is not ``/api/auth/change-password``,\n    returns 403 to force a password change.\n    """\n    # Read cookie from request headers (more reliable than Cookie dependency)\n    cookie_header = request.headers.get("cookie", "")\n    session_token = ""\n    for cookie in cookie_header.split(";"):\n        cookie = cookie.strip()\n        if cookie.startswith("__Host-homelab_session="):\n            session_token = cookie.split("=", 1)[1]\n            break\n\n    if not session_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Not authenticated",\n        )\n\n    token_hash = session_mgr.hash_token(session_token)\n    session = session_mgr.get_session(token_hash)\n    if session is None:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Session expired or invalid",\n        )\n\n    # Touch the session to refresh idle timer\n    session_mgr.touch_session(session["id"])\n\n    # Fetch user details\n    conn = get_db()\n    user = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT id, username, role, is_active, must_change_pw "\n        "FROM users WHERE id = ?",\n        (session["user_id"],),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if user is None:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="User not found",\n        )\n\n    user_dict = dict(user)\n    user_dict["session_id"] = session["id"]\n\n    # Must-change-password enforcement\n    if user_dict["must_change_pw"]:\n        # Allow access to change-password, csrf-token, and logout\n        # A user restricted to password change must still be able to log out\n        path = request.url.path\n        if path not in (\n            "/api/auth/change-password",\n            "/api/auth/csrf-token",\n            "/api/auth/logout",\n        ):\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n                detail="Password change required",\n            )\n\n    return user_dict\n\n\nasync def get_optional_user(\n    request: Request,\n) -> dict | None:\n    """Same as get_current_user but returns None instead of raising."""\n    try:\n        return await get_current_user(request)\n    except HTTPException:\n        return None\n\n\ndef get_csrf_cookie_name() -> str:\n    """Return the configured CSRF cookie name."""\n    return get_settings().csrf_cookie_name\n\n\ndef get_csrf_header_name() -> str:\n    """Return the configured CSRF header name."""\n    return get_settings().csrf_header_name\n\n\ndef verify_csrf(request: Request, session_id: int | None = None) -> None:\n    """Verify CSRF token from double-submit pattern.\n\n    The token must be present in both:\n    1. The cookie (HttpOnly for CSRF)\n    2. The request header (X-CSRF-Token)\n\n    Both values must match and be a valid HMAC-SHA256 signature.\n    When *session_id* is provided the token is also validated as\n    session-bound (generated for this specific session).\n\n    Validation is consistent across all environments (production, development, testing).\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    cookie_token = request.cookies.get(settings.csrf_cookie_name, "")\n    header_token = request.headers.get(settings.csrf_header_name, "")\n\n    if not header_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="CSRF token missing",\n        )\n\n    if not validate_csrf_token(header_token, settings.secret_key, session_id):\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="CSRF token invalid",\n        )\n\n    # Always require double-submit (cookie + header must match)\n    if not cookie_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="CSRF token missing",\n        )\n    if cookie_token != header_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="CSRF token mismatch",\n        )\n\n\ndef verify_origin(request: Request) -> None:\n    """Verify request origin against allowed origins.\n\n    In production mode, requests without an Origin header are rejected\n    for state-changing methods.  In development, same-origin requests\n    (no Origin header) are allowed.\n\n    Raises HTTP 403 on invalid origin.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    allowed = settings.allowed_origins_set\n\n    # In production, require an explicit origin for state-changing requests\n    if settings.is_production:\n        origin = request.headers.get("origin")\n        if not origin:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n                detail="Origin header required",\n            )\n\n    if not check_origin(request, allowed):\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="Origin not allowed",\n        )\n\n\ndef verify_mutation_request(request: Request, session_id: int | None = None) -> None:\n    """Verify CSRF + origin for all non-GET requests.\n\n    GET, HEAD, OPTIONS requests skip CSRF verification.\n    When *session_id* is provided the CSRF token is validated as\n    session-bound.\n    """\n    if request.method in ("GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS"):\n        return\n    verify_csrf(request, session_id)\n    verify_origin(request)\n\n\ndef verify_reauth_token(\n    request: Request,\n    x_reauth_token: str = Header(default="", alias="X-Reauth-Token"),\n) -> None:\n    """Verify a re-authentication token for sensitive operations.\n\n    The token must be present in the ``X-Reauth-Token`` header.\n    It is validated as session-bound, not expired, and not yet consumed.\n    Upon successful validation the token is atomically marked as consumed\n    (single-use).\n\n    Raises HTTP 403 on any validation failure.\n    """\n    if not x_reauth_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="Re-authentication token required",\n        )\n\n    settings = get_settings()\n    token_hash = session_mgr.hash_token(x_reauth_token)\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n    conn = get_db()\n\n    # Atomically find and mark the token as consumed\n    row = conn.execute(\n        """SELECT id, session_id, user_id, expires_at\n           FROM reauth_tokens\n           WHERE token_hash = ? AND consumed = 0 AND expires_at > ?\n           LIMIT 1""",\n        (token_hash, now),\n    ).fetchone()\n\n    if row is None:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="Re-authentication token invalid or expired",\n        )\n\n    # Store session/user info for later verification by the caller\n    request.state.reauth_session_id = row["session_id"]\n    request.state.reauth_user_id = row["user_id"]\n\n\ndef set_csrf_response(\n    response: JSONResponse,\n    token: str | None = None,\n    session_id: int | None = None,\n) -> str:\n    """Add CSRF cookie to a response and return the token value.\n\n    If *token* is provided it is used as-is (useful when the token\n    was already generated with session binding).  Otherwise a new\n    session-bound token is generated.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    if token is None:\n        token = generate_csrf_token(settings.secret_key, session_id)\n    response.set_cookie(\n        key=settings.csrf_cookie_name,\n        value=token,\n        httponly=True,\n        samesite="strict",\n        secure=settings.is_production,\n        path="/",\n        domain=None,\n    )\n    return token\n```\n\n### app/routers/auth.py\n```python\n"""Authentication routes: login, logout, me, change-password, bootstrap.\n\nAll routes that accept a password also return a fresh CSRF token.\nLogin failures are generic — the response never reveals whether a\nusername exists.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport secrets\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, Request, status\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\nfrom .. import sessions as session_mgr\nfrom ..config import get_settings\nfrom ..database import get_db, transaction\nfrom ..deps import (\n    CSRF_COOKIE_NAME,\n    CSRF_HEADER_NAME,\n    SESSION_COOKIE,\n    get_current_user,\n    set_csrf_response,\n    verify_mutation_request,\n)\nfrom ..security import generate_csrf_token\nfrom ..schemas import ChangePasswordRequest, LoginRequest\nfrom ..security import (\n    hash_password,\n    is_locked,\n    lock_account,\n    reset_failed_attempts,\n    verify_password,\n)\n\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix="/api/auth", tags=["auth"])\n\n\ndef _make_login_response(\n    raw_token: str,\n    user: dict,\n    session_id: int,\n    message: str = "Logged in",\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Create a login response with session and CSRF cookies."""\n    resp = JSONResponse(content={"message": message})\n    # __Host- prefix requires Secure in ALL environments (browser requirement)\n    resp.set_cookie(\n        key=SESSION_COOKIE,\n        value=raw_token,\n        httponly=True,\n        samesite="strict",\n        secure=True,\n        path="/",\n        domain=None,\n    )\n    # Set CSRF cookie (session-bound for this user\'s session)\n    set_csrf_response(resp, session_id=session_id)\n    return resp\n\n\n# ── First-admin bootstrap ───────────────────────────────────────\n# Bootstrap is deliberately NOT a web endpoint.\n# Use the CLI: python -m app.cli_bootstrap\n\n\n# ── Login ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post("/login")\nasync def login(\n    request: Request,\n    body: LoginRequest,\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Authenticate and create a session.\n\n    On success: sets session cookie + CSRF cookie.\n    On failure: generic "Invalid credentials" message.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    conn = get_db()\n\n    # Fetch user (allows login with username only)\n    user = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT id, username, password_hash, role, is_active, "\n        "must_change_pw, failed_attempts, locked_until "\n        "FROM users WHERE username = ?",\n        (body.username,),\n    ).fetchone()\n\n    # Always run verify_password to prevent timing attacks\n    # even if user doesn\'t exist (use a dummy hash)\n    if user is None:\n        # Run a dummy hash verification to constantize timing\n        import argon2\n        try:\n            argon2.PasswordHasher().verify(\n                argon2.PasswordHasher().hash("dummy"),\n                body.password,\n            )\n        except argon2.exceptions.VerifyMismatchError:\n            pass  # Expected — password won\'t match dummy hash\n        _record_audit(conn, "login", body.username, None, False, "User not found")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Invalid credentials",\n        )\n\n    # Check if account is active\n    if not user["is_active"]:\n        _record_audit(conn, "login", body.username, None, False, "Account disabled")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Invalid credentials",\n        )\n\n    # Check if account is locked\n    if is_locked(user["locked_until"]):\n        _record_audit(conn, "login", body.username, None, False, "Account locked")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Invalid credentials",\n        )\n\n    # Verify password\n    if not verify_password(body.password, user["password_hash"]):\n        # Increment failed attempts\n        new_attempts = user["failed_attempts"] + 1\n        locked_until = None\n        if new_attempts >= 5:\n            locked_until = lock_account()\n        conn.execute(\n            "UPDATE users SET failed_attempts = ?, locked_until = ? WHERE id = ?",\n            (new_attempts, locked_until, user["id"]),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n        _record_audit(conn, "login", body.username, None, False, "Invalid password")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Invalid credentials",\n        )\n\n    # Success — reset attempts, create session\n    conn.execute(\n        "UPDATE users SET failed_attempts = 0, locked_until = NULL, "\n        "last_login_at = datetime(\'now\') WHERE id = ?",\n        (user["id"],),\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n\n    raw_token, session_id = session_mgr.create_session(user["id"])\n    resp = _make_login_response(raw_token, dict(user), session_id)\n    resp.content = b\'{"message": "Logged in"}\'\n    _record_audit(conn, "login", body.username, None, True, None)\n    return resp\n\n\n# ── Me ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/me")\nasync def get_me(current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user)) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Return the current user\'s profile (no sensitive data)."""\n    return JSONResponse(content={\n        "id": current_user["id"],\n        "username": current_user["username"],\n        "role": current_user["role"],\n        "is_active": bool(current_user["is_active"]),\n        "must_change_pw": bool(current_user["must_change_pw"]),\n    })\n\n\n# ── Logout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post("/logout")\nasync def logout(\n    request: Request,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Revoke the current session."""\n    session_mgr.logout_session(current_user["session_id"])\n\n    conn = get_db()\n    _record_audit(conn, "logout", current_user["username"], None, True, None)\n\n    resp = JSONResponse(content={"message": "Logged out"})\n    resp.delete_cookie(\n        key=SESSION_COOKIE,\n        path="/",\n        domain=None,\n    )\n    settings = get_settings()\n    resp.delete_cookie(\n        key=settings.csrf_cookie_name,\n        path="/",\n        domain=None,\n    )\n    return resp\n\n\n# ── Change password (self-service) ───────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post("/change-password")\nasync def change_password(\n    request: Request,\n    body: ChangePasswordRequest,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Change the current user\'s password.\n\n    Requires the current password for verification.\n    Revokes all other sessions for this user.\n    """\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    conn = get_db()\n    user = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE id = ?",\n        (current_user["id"],),\n    ).fetchone()\n\n    if not verify_password(body.current_password, user["password_hash"]):\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Current password is incorrect",\n        )\n\n    new_hash = hash_password(body.new_password)\n    conn.execute(\n        "UPDATE users SET password_hash = ?, must_change_pw = 0 WHERE id = ?",\n        (new_hash, current_user["id"]),\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n\n    # Revoke all sessions except current\n    session_mgr.revoke_user_sessions(\n        current_user["id"],\n        except_session_id=current_user["session_id"],\n    )\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "password-change", current_user["username"], None, True, None,\n    )\n\n    return JSONResponse(content={"message": "Password changed"})\n\n\n# ── CSRF Token ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/csrf-token")\nasync def get_csrf_token(\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Return a session-bound CSRF token for authenticated requests.\n\n    The frontend reads this JSON body and includes the token in the\n    ``X-CSRF-Token`` header on subsequent state-changing requests.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    token = generate_csrf_token(settings.secret_key, current_user["session_id"])\n    return JSONResponse(content={"csrf_token": token})\n\n\n# ── Re-authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post("/reauthenticate")\nasync def reauthenticate(\n    request: Request,\n    body: LoginRequest,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Re-authenticate the current user for sensitive operations.\n\n    Verifies the current password and returns a short-lived, single-use\n    re-auth token bound to the current session.  The token must be\n    included in the ``X-Reauth-Token`` header on sensitive admin\n    endpoints.\n\n    The token expires after 5 minutes or after first use.\n    """\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    conn = get_db()\n    user = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE id = ?",\n        (current_user["id"],),\n    ).fetchone()\n\n    if not verify_password(body.password, user["password_hash"]):\n        _record_audit(\n            conn, "reauth-failure", current_user["username"], None, False,\n            "Incorrect password",\n        )\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail="Invalid credentials",\n        )\n\n    # Generate a single-use re-auth token (opaque, not a session token)\n    raw = secrets.token_hex(32)\n    settings = get_settings()\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n    expires = (now + timedelta(minutes=5)).isoformat()\n\n    # Store in a dedicated re-auth table\n    conn.execute(\n        """INSERT INTO reauth_tokens\n           (token_hash, user_id, session_id, expires_at, consumed)\n           VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 0)""",\n        (session_mgr.hash_token(raw), current_user["id"],\n         current_user["session_id"], expires),\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "reauth-success", current_user["username"], None, True, None,\n    )\n\n    return JSONResponse(content={"reauth_token": raw})\n\n\n# ── Logout all (self-service) ────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post("/logout-all")\nasync def logout_all(\n    request: Request,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Revoke all sessions except the current one."""\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    session_mgr.revoke_user_sessions(\n        current_user["id"],\n        except_session_id=current_user["session_id"],\n    )\n\n    conn = get_db()\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "logout-all", current_user["username"], None, True, None,\n    )\n\n    return JSONResponse(content={"message": "All other sessions revoked"})\n\n\n# ── My sessions (self-service) ───────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/my-sessions")\nasync def get_my_sessions(\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """List the current user\'s own active sessions."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        """SELECT id, created_at, last_activity,\n                  idle_expires_at, absolute_expires_at\n           FROM sessions\n           WHERE user_id = ? AND revoked = 0\n           ORDER BY created_at DESC""",\n        (current_user["id"],),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return JSONResponse(content={\n        "sessions": [\n            {\n                "id": r["id"],\n                "created_at": r["created_at"],\n                "last_activity": r["last_activity"],\n                "idle_expires_at": r["idle_expires_at"],\n                "absolute_expires_at": r["absolute_expires_at"],\n                "is_current": r["id"] == current_user["session_id"],\n            }\n            for r in rows\n        ]\n    })\n\n\n@router.delete("/my-sessions/{session_id}")\nasync def revoke_my_session(\n    request: Request,\n    session_id: int,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Revoke one of the current user\'s own sessions."""\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    # Ensure user can only revoke their own sessions\n    conn = get_db()\n    row = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT user_id FROM sessions WHERE id = ?",\n        (session_id,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is None or row["user_id"] != current_user["id"]:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND,\n            detail="Session not found",\n        )\n\n    session_mgr.revoke_session(session_id)\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "session-revoke-self", current_user["username"],\n        str(session_id), True, None,\n    )\n\n    return JSONResponse(content={"message": "Session revoked"})\n\n\n# ── Helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _record_audit(\n    conn,\n    event_type: str,\n    actor_user: str,\n    target: str | None,\n    success: bool,\n    error: str | None = None,\n    details: str | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    """Write an audit log entry."""\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\n            """INSERT INTO audit_log\n               (actor_user, event_type, target, details, success, error)\n               VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)""",\n            (actor_user, event_type, target, details, int(success), error),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        # Never let audit failures break the application\n        pass\n```\n\n### app/routers/admin.py\n```python\n"""Admin routes: user management, session management, audit log.\n\nAll routes require Admin role.  They are protected by CSRF, origin\nchecks, and role enforcement.  Sensitive operations require\nre-authentication via the ``X-Reauth-Token`` header.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport secrets\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, Query, Request, status\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\nfrom .. import sessions as session_mgr\nfrom ..config import get_settings\nfrom ..database import get_db\nfrom ..deps import (\n    REAUTH_HEADER_NAME,\n    get_current_user,\n    verify_mutation_request,\n    verify_reauth_token,\n)\nfrom ..schemas import (\n    AuditEntry,\n    CreateUserRequest,\n    ResetPasswordRequest,\n    SessionResponse,\n    UpdateUserRequest,\n    UserBrief,\n)\nfrom ..security import hash_password, require_admin\n\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix="/api/admin", tags=["admin"])\n\n\n# ── Users ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/users", response_model=list[UserBrief])\n@require_admin\nasync def list_users(\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> list[dict]:\n    """List all users (no password hashes)."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT id, username, role, is_active, created_at, last_login_at "\n        "FROM users ORDER BY id"\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n\n@router.post("/users")\n@require_admin\nasync def create_user(\n    request: Request,\n    body: CreateUserRequest,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Create a new user.  Admin-only."""\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    # Check for duplicate username\n    conn = get_db()\n    existing = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = ?",\n        (body.username,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if existing:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_409_CONFLICT,\n            detail="Username already exists",\n        )\n\n    password_hash = hash_password(body.password)\n    conn.execute(\n        """INSERT INTO users (username, password_hash, role, must_change_pw)\n           VALUES (?, ?, ?, 1)""",\n        (body.username, password_hash, body.role),\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "user-create", current_user["username"],\n        body.username, True, None,\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(status_code=201, content={"message": "User created"})\n\n\n@router.patch("/users/{user_id}")\n@require_admin\nasync def update_user(\n    request: Request,\n    user_id: int,\n    body: UpdateUserRequest,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Update a user\'s role or active status.  Admin-only.\n\n    Sensitive operations (disabling accounts, role changes) require\n    re-authentication via the ``X-Reauth-Token`` header.\n    """\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    # Determine if this is a sensitive operation\n    is_sensitive = body.is_active is False or body.role is not None\n\n    if is_sensitive:\n        reauth_token = request.headers.get("X-Reauth-Token", "")\n        if not reauth_token:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n                detail="Re-authentication token required for sensitive operations",\n            )\n        verify_reauth_token(request, x_reauth_token=reauth_token)\n\n    conn = get_db()\n\n    # Prevent disabling/demoting the last admin\n    if body.is_active is False or body.role == "viewer":\n        admin_count = conn.execute(\n            "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE role = \'admin\' AND is_active = 1"\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n        target_user = conn.execute(\n            "SELECT id, role, is_active FROM users WHERE id = ?",\n            (user_id,),\n        ).fetchone()\n        if target_user and target_user["role"] == "admin":\n            if body.is_active is False and admin_count <= 1:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,\n                    detail="Cannot disable the last admin",\n                )\n            if body.role == "viewer" and admin_count <= 1:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,\n                    detail="Cannot demote the last admin",\n                )\n\n    # Build update\n    updates: dict[str, object] = {}\n    if body.role is not None:\n        updates["role"] = body.role\n    if body.is_active is not None:\n        updates["is_active"] = 1 if body.is_active else 0\n\n    if updates:\n        set_clause = ", ".join(f"{k} = ?" for k in updates)\n        values = list(updates.values()) + [user_id]\n        conn.execute(f"UPDATE users SET {set_clause} WHERE id = ?", values)\n\n        # Revoke all sessions for this user when role or status changes\n        if "role" in updates or "is_active" in updates:\n            session_mgr.revoke_user_sessions(user_id, conn=conn)\n\n        conn.commit()\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "user-update", current_user["username"],\n        str(user_id), True, None,\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(content={"message": "User updated"})\n\n\n@router.post("/users/{user_id}/reset-password")\n@require_admin\nasync def reset_password(\n    request: Request,\n    user_id: int,\n    body: ResetPasswordRequest,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Reset a user\'s password (admin-forced).  Requires re-login.\n\n    Generates a temporary credential displayed only once.\n    The target user is flagged to change password on next login.\n\n    Requires re-authentication via the ``X-Reauth-Token`` header.\n    """\n    verify_mutation_request(request, current_user["session_id"])\n\n    reauth_token = request.headers.get("X-Reauth-Token", "")\n    if not reauth_token:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail="Re-authentication token required for sensitive operations",\n        )\n    verify_reauth_token(request, x_reauth_token=reauth_token)\n\n    conn = get_db()\n\n    # Check user exists\n    user = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT id, username FROM users WHERE id = ?",\n        (user_id,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if not user:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND,\n            detail="User not found",\n        )\n\n    # Generate a temporary credential (16-char random string)\n    temp_password = secrets.token_urlsafe(12)  # ~16 chars of entropy\n    new_hash = hash_password(temp_password)\n\n    conn.execute(\n        "UPDATE users SET password_hash = ?, must_change_pw = 1 WHERE id = ?",\n        (new_hash, user_id),\n    )\n\n    # Revoke all sessions for this user (same transaction)\n    session_mgr.revoke_user_sessions(user_id, conn=conn)\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn, "password-reset", current_user["username"],\n        user["username"], True, None,\n    )\n\n    conn.commit()\n\n    # Return temp password only after successful commit\n\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=200,\n        content={\n            "message": "Password reset — user must change on next login",\n            "temporary_password": temp_password,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n# ── Sessions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/sessions", response_model=list[SessionResponse])\n@require_admin\nasync def list_sessions(\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> list[dict]:\n    """List all active (non-revoked) sessions with user info.  Admin-only."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        """SELECT s.id, s.created_at, s.last_activity,\n                  s.idle_expires_at, s.absolute_expires_at,\n                  u.username,\n                  CASE WHEN s.id = ? THEN 1 ELSE 0 END as is_current\n           FROM sessions s\n           JOIN users u ON s.user_id = u.id\n           WHERE s.revoked = 0\n           ORDER BY s.created_at DESC""",\n        (current_user["session_id"],),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [\n        {\n            "id": r["id"],\n            "created_at": r["created_at"],\n            "last_activity": r["last_activity"],\n            "idle_expires_at": r["idle_expires_at"],\n            "absolute_expires_at": r["absolute_expires_at"],\n            "is_current": bool(r["is_current"]),\n        }\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n\n\n@router.delete("/sessions/{session_id}")\n@require_admin\nasync def revoke_session(\n    request: Request,\n    session_id: int,\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> JSONResponse:\n    """Revoke a specific session.  Admin-only."""\n    verify_mutation_request(request)\n\n    session_mgr.revoke_session(session_id)\n\n    _record_audit(\n        conn := get_db(),\n        "session-revoke", current_user["username"],\n        str(session_id), True, None,\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(content={"message": "Session revoked"})\n\n\n# ── Audit log ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.get("/audit", response_model=list[AuditEntry])\n@require_admin\nasync def get_audit_log(\n    current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user),\n    limit: int = Query(default=100, ge=1, le=500),\n) -> list[dict]:\n    """Return recent audit entries.  Admin-only."""\n    conn = get_db()\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        "SELECT timestamp, actor_user, event_type, target, details, success "\n        "FROM audit_log ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT ?",\n        (limit,),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [\n        {\n            "timestamp": r["timestamp"],\n            "actor_user": r["actor_user"],\n            "event_type": r["event_type"],\n            "target": r["target"],\n            "details": r["details"],\n            "success": bool(r["success"]),\n        }\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n\n\n# ── Helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _record_audit(conn, event_type, actor_user, target, success, error, details=None):\n    """Write an audit log entry."""\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\n            """INSERT INTO audit_log\n               (actor_user, event_type, target, details, success, error)\n               VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)""",\n            (actor_user, event_type, target, details, int(success), error),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n```\n\n### app/cli_bootstrap.py\n```python\n"""CLI tool for creating the first-admin account.\n\nUsage::\n\n    python -m app.cli_bootstrap\n\nPrompts for username and password interactively.  Does not accept\npasswords as command-line arguments to avoid leaking them into\nshell history.  Creates the first admin only when the database\ncontains zero users.\n\nThis replaces the former ``POST /api/auth/bootstrap`` endpoint\nwhich was removed because it was reachable through Tailscale Serve\nbefore any administrators existed.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport getpass\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Ensure the project root is on sys.path so ``app`` is importable\n# when this script is run directly (not via ``python -m app.cli_bootstrap``).\n_project_root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nif str(_project_root) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_project_root))\n\nfrom app.config import get_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom app.database import init_pool, init_schema, get_db  # noqa: E402\nfrom app.security import hash_password  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef _prompt_password(prompt_text: str) -> str:\n    """Prompt for a password, enforcing minimum length."""\n    while True:\n        pw = getpass.getpass(prompt_text)\n        if len(pw) >= 8:\n            return pw\n        print("Password must be at least 8 characters. Try again.")\n\n\ndef bootstrap(username: str | None = None, password: str | None = None) -> int:\n    """Create the first admin user.\n\n    Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.\n    """\n    settings = get_settings()\n    init_pool(settings.db_path)\n    init_schema()\n\n    conn = get_db()\n\n    # Check if any user exists\n    count = conn.execute("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users").fetchone()[0]\n    if count > 0:\n        print("Error: an administrator already exists. Bootstrap is a one-time operation.")\n        return 1\n\n    if username is None:\n        username = input("Username: ").strip()\n        if not username or len(username) > 128:\n            print("Error: username must be 1-128 non-empty characters.")\n            return 1\n\n    if password is None:\n        password = _prompt_password("Password: ")\n        password_confirm = _prompt_password("Confirm password: ")\n        if password != password_confirm:\n            print("Error: passwords do not match.")\n            return 1\n\n    password_hash = hash_password(password)\n    conn.execute(\n        """INSERT INTO users (username, password_hash, role, must_change_pw)\n           VALUES (?, ?, \'admin\', 1)""",\n        (username, password_hash),\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n\n    # Log audit\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\n            """INSERT INTO audit_log (actor_user, event_type, target, details, success)\n               VALUES (?, \'bootstrap\', ?, \'First admin created\', 1)""",\n            (username, username),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        pass  # Audit failure must not block bootstrap\n\n    # Do NOT create a session or print tokens — the CLI bootstrap\n    # is a one-time setup step, not an authentication mechanism.\n    # Users log in via POST /api/auth/login thereafter.\n\n    print(f"\\nFirst admin \'{username}\' created successfully.")\n    print(f"\\nNext steps:")\n    print(f"  1. Start the dashboard service")\n    print(f"  2. Log in via POST /api/auth/login with these credentials")\n    print(f"  3. Change the password on first login (must_change_pw is set)")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    sys.exit(bootstrap())\n```\n\nPlease provide a thorough review covering:\n1. **Security issues**: Any vulnerabilities, bypasses, or weaknesses\n2. **Logic errors**: Bugs, race conditions, incorrect behavior\n3. **Test coverage gaps**: Missing test scenarios\n4. **Code quality**: Issues with the implementation\n\nBe specific and thorough.', 'timeout': 1800000}
