19:53:10 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Please review the following M3 (Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF) milestone handoff for completeness and correctness. This is the final milestone before M4 (Linux monitoring). I need you to verify that M3 is truly complete and that there are no gaps, security issues, or inconsistencies that would block progression to M4.\n\n**MILESTONE: M3 — Backend, Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF (v4 — Final)**\n\n**RESULT: COMPLETE — 62 tests passing, 0 deferred**\n\n**PREREQ:** M1 (inventory) and M2 (TV service) are PASS.\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### Architecture\n- FastAPI backend, SQLite with WAL mode, schema version 2\n- Files: `app/main.py`, `config.py`, `database.py`, `sessions.py`, `security.py`, `deps.py`, `schemas.py`, `cli_bootstrap.py`, `app/routers/auth.py`, `app/routers/admin.py`\n- Tests: `tests/test_auth.py` (26), `tests/test_admin.py` (18), `tests/test_sessions.py` (7), `tests/test_csrf.py` (11) = 62 total\n\n### Security Features\n1. **Argon2id** password hashing (time=3, mem=65536, par=2)\n2. **Opaque revocable sessions** — SHA-256 token hashes stored, raw tokens never persisted\n3. **CSRF** — HMAC-SHA256 double-submit pattern, session-bound (HMAC includes session_id in payload)\n4. **Cookie security** — `__Host-homelab_session` with Secure=True (all environments), HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain\n5. **RBAC** — Admin/Operator/Viewer, default-deny, role hierarchy\n6. **Account lockout** — 5 failed attempts → 15 min lockout\n7. **Generic login failure** — never reveals username existence\n8. **must_change_pw enforcement** — blocks all endpoints except change-password, csrf-token, logout\n9. **Admin re-auth** — `X-Reauth-Token` required for disable/demote and password reset\n10. **Last-admin protection** — cannot disable/demote final admin\n11. **Transactional operations** — password change + session revocation in same SQLite transaction\n12. **Production config validation** — SECRET_KEY (32+ chars), DB_PATH (absolute), ALLOWED_ORIGINS (non-empty)\n13. **Listener** — binds 127.0.0.1:8787 only\n14. **CLI bootstrap** — first admin creation, no web endpoint, no token output\n\n### Database Schema (v2)\n- `users` — id, username, password_hash, role, is_active, must_change_pw, created_at, last_login_at, failed_attempts, locked_until\n- `sessions` — id, user_id, token_hash, created_at, last_activity, idle_expires_at, absolute_expires_at, revoked\n- `audit_log` — id, timestamp, actor_user, event_type, target, details, success, error\n- `reauth_tokens` — id, token_hash, user_id, session_id, expires_at, consumed\n\n### API Endpoints\n- Auth: login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions, my-sessions/{id}\n- Admin: users (CRUD), sessions (list/revoke), audit log\n- Health: /api/health (public)\n\n### Test Results\n```\n62 passed in ~10.7s\n```\n\n### Recent Critical Fixes (v3→v4)\n1. CSRF now truly session-bound (HMAC includes session_id)\n2. Admin re-auth properly enforced (not just checking header existence)\n3. CLI bootstrap no longer prints session tokens\n4. `must_change_pw` for admin-created users (was 0, now 1)\n5. `set_csrf_response` accepts optional token/session_id\n6. Production `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` validation (rejects empty)\n7. Session cookie always Secure (not just production)\n8. Logout accessible when must_change_pw=1\n9. Test fixtures use HTTPS base URL\n10. Test counts reconciled (62, not 60)\n\n### Deferred to M8\n- Real HTTPS browser cookie behavior\n- Tailscale Serve HTTPS access\n- Ubuntu deployment and systemd service\n- Production login through deployed service\n- Boot recovery testing (M9)\n\n---\n\nPlease verify:\n1. Is the M3 handoff consistent and complete?\n2. Are there any security gaps or inconsistencies?\n3. Are the 62 tests sufficient for the claimed scope?\n4. Is the milestone truly ready to be marked COMPLETE?\n5. Any issues that would block M4 (Linux monitoring)?', 'timeout': 1800000}
