20:00:28 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Please review the corrected M3 (Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF) milestone handoff. The previous review identified critical issues. This version addresses them. I need final confirmation that M3 is complete and ready for M4 (Linux monitoring).\n\n**MILESTONE: M3 — Backend, Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF (v5 — Final, post-verification)**\n\n**RESULT: COMPLETE — 64 tests passing, 0 deferred**\n\n**PREREQ:** M1 (inventory) and M2 (TV service) are PASS.\n\n---\n\n## Issues from Previous Review — RESOLVED\n\n### 1. Password-Change Transaction Atomicity — FIXED\n**Problem**: `change_password()` in `auth.py` committed the password UPDATE, then called `revoke_user_sessions()` as a separate operation. If revocation failed, old sessions remained valid after password change.\n\n**Fix**: Moved session revocation into the same transaction (same `conn`, before `conn.commit()`). Wrapped in `try/except` with `conn.rollback()`. The `reset_password()` in `admin.py` and `update_user()` in `admin.py` were already correct (single transaction).\n\n**Verification**: 2 new tests in `TestPasswordChangeAtomicity`:\n- `test_password_change_revokes_other_sessions_atomic` — verifies self-service password change atomicity\n- `test_admin_password_reset_atomic` — verifies admin password reset atomicity\n\n### 2. Handoff Consistency — FIXED\n- "62 tests passing, 0 deferred" → "64 tests passing, 0 deferred"\n- Correctly distinguishes local tests (PASS) from production integration (deferred to M8)\n- M1 was PARTIAL ACCEPTED (noted in M1 handoff); deployment blocker resolved in M2\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### Security Features\n1. **Argon2id** password hashing (time=3, mem=65536, par=2)\n2. **Opaque revocable sessions** — SHA-256 token hashes stored, raw tokens never persisted\n3. **CSRF** — HMAC-SHA256 double-submit pattern, session-bound (HMAC includes session_id)\n4. **Cookie security** — `__Host-homelab_session` with Secure=True (all envs), HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain\n5. **RBAC** — Admin/Operator/Viewer, default-deny, role hierarchy\n6. **Account lockout** — 5 failed attempts → 15 min lockout\n7. **Generic login failure** — never reveals username existence\n8. **must_change_pw enforcement** — blocks all endpoints except change-password, csrf-token, logout\n9. **Admin re-auth** — `X-Reauth-Token` required for disable/demote and password reset\n10. **Last-admin protection** — cannot disable/demote final admin\n11. **Transactional operations** — password change + session revocation in same SQLite transaction (v5 fix)\n12. **Production config validation** — SECRET_KEY (32+ chars), DB_PATH (absolute), ALLOWED_ORIGINS (non-empty)\n13. **Listener** — binds 127.0.0.1:8787 only\n14. **CLI bootstrap** — first admin creation, no web endpoint, no token output\n\n### Database Schema (v2)\n- `users` — id, username, password_hash, role, is_active, must_change_pw, created_at, last_login_at, failed_attempts, locked_until\n- `sessions` — id, user_id, token_hash, created_at, last_activity, idle_expires_at, absolute_expires_at, revoked\n- `audit_log` — id, timestamp, actor_user, event_type, target, details, success, error\n- `reauth_tokens` — id, token_hash, user_id, session_id, expires_at, consumed\n\n### Test Results\n```\n64 passed in ~10.0s\n```\n\n### Test Breakdown\n- `test_auth.py` (26): login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions, must_change_pw, cross-session CSRF\n- `test_admin.py` (18): User CRUD, RBAC, audit log, last-admin protection, password reset, session revocation\n- `test_sessions.py` (9): Session CRUD, validation, expiry, revocation, password-change revocation, **atomicity (2 new)**\n- `test_csrf.py` (11): HMAC token generation, validation, tamper detection, origin checks\n\n### Deferred to M8\n- Real HTTPS browser cookie behavior\n- Tailscale Serve HTTPS access\n- Ubuntu deployment and systemd service\n- Production login through deployed service\n\n---\n\nPlease confirm:\n1. Is the password-change transaction fix correct and sufficient?\n2. Is the M3 handoff now consistent and complete?\n3. Is M3 ready to be marked COMPLETE for progression to M4?\n4. Are there any remaining issues that would block M4?', 'timeout': 1800000}
