20:06:16 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Please review the final corrected M3 (Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF) milestone handoff. All previously identified issues have been addressed. I need FINAL confirmation that M3 is complete and ready for M4 (Linux monitoring).\n\n**MILESTONE: M3 — Backend, Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF (v6 — Final)**\n\n**Status**: COMPLETE — 64 local tests passed, 0 skipped. Production integration DEFERRED → M8; reboot recovery DEFERRED → M9.\n\n**PREREQ:** M1 (inventory) and M2 (TV service) are PASS.\n\n---\n\n## All Issues from Previous Reviews — RESOLVED\n\n### 1. Password-Change Transaction Atomicity — FIXED (v5)\n**Problem**: `change_password()` committed password UPDATE, then called `revoke_user_sessions()` separately.\n**Fix**: Moved session revocation into same transaction (same `conn`, before `commit()`). Wrapped in `try/except` with `rollback()`.\n**Tests**: 2 new tests in `TestPasswordChangeAtomicity`.\n\n### 2. Bootstrap Concurrency — FIXED (v6)\n**Problem**: Two concurrent bootstrap processes could both see count==0 and both INSERT.\n**Fix**: `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` serializes check-and-insert. Gets "database is locked" if another write is in progress.\n**Code**: `app/cli_bootstrap.py` — try/except for `sqlite3.OperationalError`.\n\n### 3. Re-Auth Token Invalidation — FIXED (v6)\n**Problem**: Password changes, account disables, and role changes did not invalidate outstanding re-auth tokens.\n**Fix**: All three functions (`change_password`, `reset_password`, `update_user`) now execute `UPDATE reauth_tokens SET consumed = 1 WHERE user_id = ?` in the same transaction.\n\n### 4. Handoff Wording — FIXED (v6)\n- "64 local tests passed, 0 skipped. Production integration DEFERRED → M8; reboot recovery DEFERRED → M9."\n- M1 remains PARTIAL ACCEPTED (historically accurate).\n\n### 5. CSRF Cookie Security\n- Session cookie: `__Host-homelab_session` — Secure=True (ALL environments), HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain\n- CSRF cookie: `homelab_csrf` — HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, Secure=settings.is_production\n- The `__Host-` prefix requires Secure in all environments (browser requirement). This is satisfied by the session cookie.\n\n### 6. Re-Auth Token Security\n- Tokens are session-bound (include session_id)\n- Single-use (atomic consume via UPDATE WHERE consumed=0)\n- 5-minute expiry\n- Invalidated on password change, account disable, role change, and password reset\n- Cannot be used after session is revoked (token lookup checks session_id)\n\n---\n\n## Test Results\n```\n64 passed in ~10.0s\n```\n\n- `test_auth.py` (26): login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions, must_change_pw, cross-session CSRF\n- `test_admin.py` (18): User CRUD, RBAC, audit log, last-admin protection, password reset, session revocation\n- `test_sessions.py` (9): Session CRUD, validation, expiry, revocation, password-change revocation, atomicity (2 new)\n- `test_csrf.py` (11): HMAC token generation, validation, tamper detection, origin checks\n\n---\n\nPlease confirm FINAL acceptance:\n1. Is M3 now COMPLETE with no remaining security issues?\n2. Can we proceed to M4 (Linux monitoring)?', 'timeout': 1800000}
