20:18:27 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Review the following M3 (Milestone 3) implementation of a backend authentication system for the Homelab Dashboard. This is a security-critical milestone that implements auth, RBAC, sessions, CSRF, and re-authentication.\n\nPlease verify:\n1. **Correctness**: Are there any security bugs, logic errors, or missing protections?\n2. **Completeness**: Does the implementation match all the documented requirements?\n3. **Test coverage**: Are the tests adequate to catch regressions?\n4. **Acceptance criteria**: Is M3 truly complete per the acceptance matrix?\n\n---\n\n# M3: Backend — Auth, RBAC, Sessions, CSRF (v6 — Final)\n\n**Status**: 64 local tests passed, 0 skipped.\n\n**Architecture**:\n```\napp/\n├── main.py              # FastAPI app, lifespan, health endpoint\n├── config.py            # Pydantic Settings (env var validation, production checks)\n├── database.py          # SQLite pool, WAL mode, migrations (v2: reauth_tokens table)\n├── sessions.py          # Session CRUD (create, validate, expire, revoke)\n├── security.py          # Argon2id, HMAC CSRF (session-bound), origin checks, RBAC\n├── deps.py              # FastAPI DI (get_current_user, verify_csrf, verify_reauth)\n├── schemas.py           # Pydantic request/response models\n├── cli_bootstrap.py     # CLI first-admin creation (no token output)\n└── routers/\n    ├── auth.py          # Login, logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions\n    └── admin.py         # User CRUD, session management, audit log, password reset\n```\n\n## Key Security Features\n\n### 1. Password Hashing\n- Argon2id: time_cost=3, memory_cost=65536, parallelism=2, hash_len=32, salt_len=16\n- Constant-time verification (always runs full verification even on malformed hashes)\n\n### 2. CSRF Protection (Session-Bound HMAC)\n- Token format: `<32-hex-chars>.<64-hex-chars-hmac>` where HMAC = `HMAC-SHA256(secret_key, raw || ":" || session_id)`\n- Session binding: Token includes current session\'s ID in HMAC payload\n- Double-submit: cookie (`homelab_csrf`) + header (`X-CSRF-Token`) must match\n- Always required in ALL environments (no relaxation)\n\n### 3. Session Management\n- Tokens: `secrets.token_urlsafe(48)` = 48 bytes = 384 bits entropy\n- Stored as SHA-256 hashes only (raw tokens never persisted)\n- Dual expiry: idle (720 min default) + absolute (7 days default)\n- Touch on access to refresh idle timer\n- Cookie: `__Host-homelab_session` — Secure(always), HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain\n\n### 4. RBAC\n- Admin/Operator/Viewer hierarchy\n- Default-deny: all routes explicitly require a role\n- Last-admin protection: cannot disable or demote the final admin\n\n### 5. Account Lockout\n- 5 failed attempts → 15-minute lockout\n- Generic login failure message (never reveals username existence)\n- Dummy hash verification on non-existent users to prevent timing attacks\n\n### 6. Re-authentication\n- `POST /api/auth/reauthenticate` — verifies password, returns single-use 5-min reauth token\n- Stored in `reauth_tokens` table with session binding\n- Required for: disable/demote users, password reset\n- Atomic token consumption (UPDATE ... WHERE consumed=0)\n\n### 7. Transactional Password Change (v5 fix)\n- `change_password()`: password UPDATE + session revocation + reauth token invalidation in single transaction\n- `reset_password()`: same atomic pattern\n- `update_user()`: role/status change + session + reauth token invalidation in single transaction\n- `try/except` with `conn.rollback()` wraps the entire operation\n\n### 8. Re-auth Token Invalidation (v6 fix)\n- All password changes, session revocations, and role changes invalidate outstanding reauth tokens\n- Tokens marked as consumed (not deleted) to preserve audit trail\n\n### 9. CLI Bootstrap Concurrency (v6 fix)\n- Uses `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` before the count check\n- Acquires RESERVED lock, blocking other write transactions\n- Prevents two concurrent bootstrap processes from both creating first-admin accounts\n\n### 10. must_change_pw Enforcement\n- When `must_change_pw=1`, blocks all endpoints except `/change-password`, `/csrf-token`, `/logout`\n- Returns 403 "Password change required"\n- Auto-cleared on successful password change\n- Admin-created users and admin-reset users get `must_change_pw=1`\n\n## API Endpoints\n\n### Authentication\n| Method | Path | Auth | CSRF | Reauth | Description |\n|--------|------|------|------|--------|-------------|\n| POST | `/api/auth/login` | None | No | No | Login, set session cookie |\n| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | No | No | Current user profile |\n| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | No | Revoke current session |\n| POST | `/api/auth/change-password` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | No | Change password, revoke others |\n| GET | `/api/auth/csrf-token` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | No | No | Get session-bound CSRF token |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reauthenticate` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | No | Get single-use reauth token |\n| POST | `/api/auth/logout-all` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | No | Revoke all other sessions |\n| GET | `/api/auth/my-sessions` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | No | No | List own sessions |\n| DELETE | `/api/auth/my-sessions/{id}` | Admin/Operator/Viewer | Yes | No | Revoke own session |\n\n### Admin (Admin-only)\n| Method | Path | Auth | CSRF | Reauth | Description |\n|--------|------|------|------|--------|-------------|\n| GET | `/api/admin/users` | Admin | No | No | List all users |\n| POST | `/api/admin/users` | Admin | Yes | No | Create user (must_change_pw=1) |\n| PATCH | `/api/admin/users/{id}` | Admin | Yes | Yes* | Update user role/active |\n| POST | `/api/admin/users/{id}/reset-password` | Admin | Yes | Yes | Admin-forced password reset |\n| GET | `/api/admin/sessions` | Admin | No | No | List all active sessions |\n| DELETE | `/api/admin/sessions/{id}` | Admin | Yes | No | Revoke session |\n| GET | `/api/admin/audit` | Admin | No | No | Recent audit entries |\n\n## Database Schema (v2)\n\n### `users`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| username | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL |\n| password_hash | TEXT | NOT NULL (Argon2id) |\n| role | TEXT | NOT NULL, CHECK IN (\'admin\', \'operator\', \'viewer\') |\n| is_active | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 1 |\n| must_change_pw | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 |\n| created_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| last_login_at | TEXT | |\n| failed_attempts | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 |\n| locked_until | TEXT | |\n\n### `sessions`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| user_id | INTEGER | NOT NULL, REFERENCES users(id) |\n| token_hash | TEXT | NOT NULL, UNIQUE, SHA-256 of raw token |\n| created_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| last_activity | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| idle_expires_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| absolute_expires_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| revoked | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 |\n\n### `audit_log`\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| timestamp | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| actor_user | TEXT | NOT NULL |\n| event_type | TEXT | NOT NULL |\n| target | TEXT | |\n| details | TEXT | |\n| success | INTEGER | NOT NULL |\n| error | TEXT | |\n\n### `reauth_tokens` (NEW in v2)\n| Column | Type | Constraints |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| id | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT |\n| token_hash | TEXT | NOT NULL, UNIQUE |\n| user_id | INTEGER | NOT NULL, REFERENCES users(id) |\n| session_id | INTEGER | NOT NULL, REFERENCES sessions(id) |\n| expires_at | TEXT | NOT NULL, ISO 8601 |\n| consumed | INTEGER | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 |\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n64 passed in ~10.0s\n```\n\n### Test Breakdown\n- **test_auth.py** (26 tests): login (success/failure/lockout), logout, me, change-password, csrf-token, reauthenticate, logout-all, my-sessions, must_change_pw enforcement, initial password change E2E, cross-session CSRF rejection\n- **test_admin.py** (18 tests): User CRUD, RBAC enforcement, audit log, last-admin protection (sequential + concurrent), health, password reset (temp cred, reauth), session revocation (disable/role change)\n- **test_sessions.py** (9 tests): Session creation, validation, expiry, revocation, password-change revocation, password-change atomicity (2 new), admin password reset atomicity\n- **test_csrf.py** (11 tests): HMAC token generation, validation, tamper detection, origin checks\n\n## Acceptance Matrix (45 requirements)\n\nAll 45 requirements PASS with evidence in code/tests:\n1. FastAPI project with ASGI lifespan — PASS\n2. SQLite with WAL mode, foreign keys, migrations — PASS\n3. Argon2id password hashing — PASS\n4. Opaque revocable sessions (SHA-256 token hashes) — PASS\n5. CSRF double-submit (HMAC-SHA256, session-bound, consistent envs) — PASS\n6. Origin validation (production rejects without Origin) — PASS\n7. Default-deny RBAC (Admin/Operator/Viewer) — PASS\n8. Account lockout (5 attempts → 15 min) — PASS\n9. Generic login failure message — PASS\n10. Audit logging for auth events — PASS\n11. CLI bootstrap (first admin, no web endpoint, no token output) — PASS\n12. Concurrent first-admin protection — PASS\n13. GET /api/csrf-token (authenticated, session-bound HMAC) — PASS\n14. POST /api/auth/reauthenticate (session-bound, 5-min expiry, single-use) — PASS\n15. GET /api/auth/my-sessions (self-service, user isolation) — PASS\n16. DELETE /api/auth/my-sessions/{id} (self-service) — PASS\n17. POST /api/auth/logout-all (revokes other sessions) — PASS\n18. Admin password reset (temp credentials, must_change_pw=1, reauth required) — PASS\n19. Forced password change flow (admin-created users must_change_pw=1) — PASS\n20. must_change_pw enforcement (blocks non-password endpoints) — PASS\n21. change-password clears must_change_pw=0 — PASS\n22. Weak password rejection — PASS\n23. Session revocation on logout — PASS\n24. Session revocation on disable/role change (transactional) — PASS\n25. Session revocation on password reset (transactional) — PASS\n26. Last-admin protection — PASS\n27. Production config validation — PASS\n28. Production listener (127.0.0.1:8787) — PASS\n29. No secrets in Git — PASS\n30. Session-bound CSRF (HMAC includes session_id) — PASS\n31. CSRF cookie + header rejection (missing cookie/header) — PASS\n32. CSRF token from another session rejected — PASS\n33. Re-auth token session-binding — PASS\n34. Re-auth token single-use (atomic consume) — PASS\n35. Re-auth token 5-min expiry — PASS\n36. Session privacy (users can only see own sessions) — PASS\n37. Transactional account updates (password + revocation) — PASS\n38. Admin re-auth enforced on sensitive operations — PASS\n39. CLI bootstrap does not print session tokens — PASS\n40. Production ALLOWED_ORIGINS required — PASS\n41. Cross-session CSRF rejection — PASS\n42. Concurrent last-admin protection (database-level) — PASS\n43. Session cookie always Secure (__Host- prefix) — PASS\n44. Logout accessible when must_change_pw=1 — PASS\n45. 64 tests passing, 0 skipped — PASS\n\n## Iterative Fixes (v2 → v6)\n\n### v3 fixes:\n1. CSRF is truly session-bound (`session_id` in HMAC payload)\n2. Admin re-auth enforced (was `pass` — no actual validation)\n3. CLI bootstrap no longer prints session tokens\n4. `must_change_pw` for admin-created users (was 0, now 1)\n5. `set_csrf_response` no longer overwrites tokens\n6. Production `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` validation\n\n### v4 fixes:\n7. Session cookie always Secure (`__Host-` prefix requires Secure in ALL environments)\n8. Logout accessible when must_change_pw=1\n9. Test fixtures use HTTPS base URL\n10. Test count reconciled (62 → 64 with atomicity tests)\n\n### v5 fixes:\n11. Password-change transaction atomicity (moved session revocation into same transaction)\n12. Atomicity tests added (2 new tests)\n\n### v6 fixes:\n13. Re-auth token invalidation on password change\n14. Re-auth token invalidation on admin actions (reset_password, update_user)\n15. Bootstrap concurrency protection (BEGIN IMMEDIATE)\n\n## Deferred to M8 (Production Integration)\n- Real HTTPS browser cookie behavior\n- Tailscale Serve HTTPS access\n- Ubuntu deployment and systemd service\n- Production login through deployed service\n\n---\n\nPlease review this implementation thoroughly. Is M3 complete and correct? Are there any security issues, missing protections, or test gaps you can identify?', 'timeout': 1800000}
