20:43:04 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'Review the following M4 (Milestone 4) implementation of monitoring, service health, and bounded logs for the Homelab Dashboard. This is a read-only monitoring milestone.\n\nPlease verify:\n1. **Correctness**: Are there any security bugs, logic errors, or missing protections?\n2. **Completeness**: Does the implementation match all M4 requirements?\n3. **Test coverage**: Are the tests adequate?\n4. **Acceptance criteria**: Is M4 truly complete per the acceptance matrix?\n\n---\n\n# M4 — Monitoring, Service Health, Bounded Logs (v1)\n\n**Status**: 111 local tests passed, 0 skipped.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\napp/\n├── monitoring.py           # System metrics (CPU, RAM, uptime, disk, network, temp)\n├── monitoring_services.py  # Service health (Samba + TV systemd + HTTP/SMB probes)\n├── monitoring_logs.py      # Bounded journal logs (fixed allowlist, redaction, escaping)\n└── routers/\n    └── status.py           # GET /api/status — aggregated snapshot with timeouts\n```\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### 1. System Metrics (`app/monitoring.py`)\n- **CPU**: `psutil.cpu_percent(interval=0.1)` — bounded to 100ms\n- **RAM**: `psutil.virtual_memory()` — total, used, available, percent\n- **Uptime**: `psutil.boot_time()` — seconds + human-readable format\n- **Disk**: `psutil.disk_usage(mount)` — configurable mount points (default: `/`)\n  - Never labels Mac `/` as Ubuntu storage — mount points are configurable inputs\n  - Skips missing mounts silently (OSError caught)\n- **Network**: `psutil.net_io_counters()` — cumulative bytes/packets since boot\n- **Temperature**: `psutil.sensors_temperatures()` — returns `None` on unsupported platforms\n- **Pydantic models**: `CpuInfo`, `MemoryInfo`, `DiskUsage`, `NetworkInfo`, `TemperatureInfo`, `SystemMetrics`\n\n### 2. Service Health (`app/monitoring_services.py`)\n- **States**: `HEALTHY`, `DEGRADED`, `STOPPED`, `STARTING`, `FAILED`, `UNKNOWN`\n- **Samba**: \n  - `systemctl is-active smbd.service` (timeout 1s)\n  - If active: `smbclient -L localhost -m SMB3 -N` (timeout 2s) to verify share accessibility\n  - Active + share accessible → `HEALTHY`\n  - Active + share inaccessible → `DEGRADED`\n  - Inactive/failed → `STOPPED`/`FAILED`\n  - Subprocess error → `UNKNOWN`\n- **TV app**:\n  - `systemctl is-active tv-app.service` (timeout 1s)\n  - If active: `httpx.get(http://localhost:3000)` (timeout 1s)\n  - Active + HTTP 200 → `HEALTHY`\n  - Active + HTTP non-200/error → `DEGRADED`\n  - Inactive/failed → `STOPPED`/`FAILED`\n  - Subprocess error → `UNKNOWN`\n- **Configurable**: service names from M1 inventory (`smbd`, `tv-app`), TV HTTP port (3000)\n- **Pydantic models**: `ServiceHealth`, `SambaHealth`, `TvHealth`\n\n### 3. Bounded Logs (`app/monitoring_logs.py`)\n- **Fixed allowlist**: only `smbd`, `tv-app`, `homelab-dashboard` journal units\n- **Rejects arbitrary input**: `ValueError` if unit not in allowlist\n- **Bounded**: `journalctl -u <unit> --no-pager -n 200 --since "10 min ago"`\n  - Max 200 entries, 10-minute lookback\n  - Timeout: 1 second\n- **Secret redaction**: regex-based removal of passwords, tokens, private keys, long hex strings\n- **HTML escaping**: all log text escaped via `html.escape()` before JSON serialization\n- **Pydantic models**: `LogEntry`, `UnitLogs`\n\n### 4. Status Endpoint (`app/routers/status.py`)\n- **Route**: `GET /api/status` — requires Admin/Operator/Viewer auth (no CSRF for GET)\n- **Concurrent probes**: all probes run concurrently via `asyncio.create_task` + `run_in_executor`\n- **Timeouts**:\n  - System metrics: 2s\n  - Service health: 3s\n  - Logs: 1s\n  - Overall soft cap: 5s\n- **Field-level degradation**: failed probes return default values with `"unknown": true`\n- **Partial flag**: `"partial": true` when any probe fails\n- **Per-probe freshness**: each field includes `"unknown": true` if probe failed\n- **Response includes**: timestamp, elapsed_ms, partial flag, system metrics, service health, logs\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n111 passed in ~11.7s\n```\n\n### Test Breakdown (47 new tests)\n- **TestCollectCpu** (2): CPU percent, bounded 0-100\n- **TestCollectMemory** (2): Memory info, total ≈ used + available\n- **TestCollectUptime** (1): Uptime positive, human-readable format\n- **TestCollectDisks** (4): Default mount, custom mounts, missing mount, empty list\n- **TestCollectNetwork** (1): Network info\n- **TestCollectTemperature** (2): Temperature available, no sensors\n- **TestCollectSystemMetrics** (1): All fields present\n- **TestSambaHealth** (4): Healthy, degraded, unknown, custom unit\n- **TestTvHealth** (4): Healthy, degraded, stopped, unknown\n- **TestCheckAllServices** (1): Returns dict with both services\n- **TestAllowlistValidation** (4): Allowed unit, disallowed raises, all units in list, frozenset\n- **TestLogRedaction** (3): Passwords, private keys, long tokens\n- **TestHtmlEscaping** (2): HTML entities, ampersand\n- **TestGetAllAllowedLogs** (1): Returns all units\n- **TestLogEntryParsing** (2): Journal line, fallback line\n- **TestStatusEndpoint** (6): Requires auth, returns data, viewer access, service unknown on Mac, elapsed_ms, logs default\n- **TestEdgeCases** (7): Empty disks, custom mounts, systemctl timeout, journalctl timeout, journalctl not found, max entries, lookback\n\n### Mock Strategy\nAll tests use `unittest.mock.patch` to mock:\n- `psutil` functions (cpu_percent, virtual_memory, disk_usage, net_io_counters, boot_time, sensors_temperatures)\n- `subprocess.run` for systemctl and journalctl calls\n- `httpx.get` for TV HTTP health probe\n\n## Ubuntu Validation (Read-Only Visit)\n\nOne focused read-only SSH visit to Ubuntu:\n- Mount points: `df -h` matches psutil `disk_usage` — **PASS**\n- CPU/Memory: `top -bn1` / `free -m` matches psutil — **PASS**\n- Temperature: `psutil.sensors_temperatures()` returns real hwmon data on Ubuntu — **PASS**\n- Network: `cat /proc/net/dev` matches psutil `net_io_counters` — **PASS**\n- Samba: `systemctl is-active smbd` → active, `smbclient -L localhost` → lists shares — **HEALTHY**\n- TV app: `systemctl is-active tv-app` → active, `curl http://localhost:3000` → HTTP 200 — **HEALTHY**\n- Journal: `journalctl -u smbd -n 5` → bounded entries — **PASS**\n- Disallowed unit: rejected by allowlist — **PASS**\n- **No production service was restarted.**\n\n## Acceptance Matrix\n\n| Check | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mac tests cover each metric | **PASS** | 14 tests in TestCollect* |\n| Mac tests cover service health & failure modes | **PASS** | 15 tests in TestSambaHealth, TestTvHealth, TestEdgeCases |\n| Fixed log targets, no arbitrary file access | **PASS** | ALLOWED_UNITS frozenset, ValueError on disallowed |\n| Read-only Ubuntu validates mount/CPU/mem/temp/net | **PASS** | df/top/free/cat /proc/net/dev match psutil |\n| Read-only Ubuntu validates Samba share status | **PASS** | smbd + smbclient → HEALTHY |\n| Read-only Ubuntu validates TV response | **PASS** | tv-app + HTTP 200 → HEALTHY |\n| Read-only Ubuntu validates available logs | **PASS** | journalctl returns bounded entries |\n| Sensor/log failures degrade only their own field | **PASS** | Per-probe timeouts, independent degradation |\n| Sensor/log failures do not crash or expose secrets | **PASS** | All exceptions caught, secrets redacted, HTML escaped |\n| No production service restarted | **PASS** | All checks read-only |\n| Handoff records Mac test evidence + remote result | **PASS** | 111 tests, Ubuntu validation completed |\n\n---\n\nPlease review this implementation thoroughly. Is M4 complete and correct? Are there any security issues, missing protections, or test gaps you can identify?', 'timeout': 1800000}
